\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills in Louisiana Could Soon Be in Same Category as Opioids; Louisiana would become the first state to classify misoprostol and mifepristone as controlled substances\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph De Avila \par \uc2 717 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2024\par 21:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 The last name of Thomas Pressly was misspelled as Pressley in an earlier version of this article. (Corrected on May 23)\par \par \uc2 The Louisiana Senate passed legislation classifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills as controlled substances, setting up the state to become the first in the U.S. to criminalize possession of the drugs without a prescription.\par \par \uc2 The measure passed the GOP-controlled Senate Thursday by a vote of 29 to 7. It passed the state House on Tuesday. If Republican Gov. Jeff Landry signs the bill, as expected, Louisiana would become the first state to classify misoprostol and mifepristone\u8212\'20\'14two drugs used to end pregnancies\u8212\'20\'14as controlled substances.\par \par \uc2 The reclassification would put the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs in the same category as opioids and other addictive substances. Under the law, it would be illegal to possess mifepristone or misoprostol without a prescription. Violators could face jail time.\par \par \uc2 The change in classification was part of a broader bill that makes it a crime for someone to give the medication to pregnant people without their knowledge. Medication and surgical abortions are already banned in Louisiana except to save a patient's life or because a pregnancy is "medically futile," so the change doesn't affect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 But misoprostol and mifepristone have uses apart from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as management of miscarriages and to address postpartum hemorrhage. Opponents of the Louisiana bill said it could create dangerous delays in emergency situations, such as heavy bleeding from a miscarriage or postpartum hemorrhaging.\par \par \uc2 Republican state Sen. Thomas Pressly said the legislation isn't intended to impede medical uses of misoprostol and mifepristone outside of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pressly said he introduced the bill after his former brother-in-law tried to give his sister an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill without her knowledge.\par \par \uc2 "I think this is a step in the right direction to keep these drugs out of the hands of bad actors," Pressly said during debate of the bill Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs lack the potential for abuse and don't pose public-health risks. Democratic state Sen. Royce Duplessis said the bill has the potential to harm women seeking medical care.\par \par \uc2 "I believe it's going to lead to harm down the road," Duplessis said.\par \par \uc2 Medication abortions, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/abortion-pill-increase-roe-wade-68472ff8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became more common }}}\uc2  after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fall of Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , have come under attack from antiabortion advocates. Medication abortions accounted for nearly two-thirds of abortions in the U.S. in 2023, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Because pills can be sent through the mail, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 antiabortion groups fear mifepristone }}}\uc2  can help women flout \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in states that have outlawed the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Blue states have passed so-called shield laws designed to protect providers from liability or prosecution if they send pills to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-arguments-abortion-pill-mifepristone-c31de31a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in March }}}\uc2  heard a case where a group of antiabortion doctors are seeking to limit access to mifepristone. While it still has to issue an opinion, the court appeared likely to preserve access to the pill. Several justices questioned whether the plaintiffs that brought the case had the right to sue.\par \par \uc2 Physicians' groups have said hundreds of studies show mifepristone's safety and serious side effects occur in less than 1% of patients.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion advocates said adding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs to the controlled substance list protects pregnant women from being given the drug without their knowledge.\par \par \uc2 "Like morphine and Valium, the drugs in question will still be available for prescription for legitimate medical reasons\u8212\'20\'14like miscarriage care\u8212\'20\'14but will be harder for abusers to obtain," said Caitlin Connors, southern regional director of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, an advocacy group that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters say the change in classification creates obstacles for women seeking care in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 "This bill would make it incredibly difficult to obtain and use these drugs for those medically necessary purposes," said Ellie Schilling, a Louisiana attorney who specializes in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on a call about the bill organized by the Biden election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joseph De Avila at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joseph.deavila@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joseph.deavila@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240523ek5n005mt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
