\par \par \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks would be just the third Black woman ever elected to the Senate if she wins in November. PHOTO: Kent Nishimura for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks won the hard-fought Democratic Senate primary in Maryland, defeating Rep. \uc2 David Trone\uc2 , who spent a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/maryland-senate-race-trone-alsobrooks-hogan-bdbf949a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record-setting amount of his own money }}}\uc2  in the contest.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press projected Alsobrooks, who currently serves as Prince George's County executive, as the winner late Tuesday. She led 54% to 42%, with about two-thirds of the vote counted.\par \par \uc2 She will face popular former two-term Republican Gov. \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  in the contest to replace retiring Democratic Sen. Ben Cardin in what is expected to be one of the fall's marquee face-offs to determine control of the Senate. Democrats currently have a 51-49 majority, but they are expected to lose West Virginia and are defending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/2024-presidential-senate-and-house-election-forecasts-5c4b54b8?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vulnerable seats in Ohio and Montana, among others }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks, if she wins in November, would be just the third Black woman ever elected to the Senate. Rep. \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2 , a Democrat running for the Senate in Delaware, is favored to win and is expected to add to the ranks of the chamber's Black women.\par \par \uc2 "We are going to defeat \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , keep Maryland blue, and keep our Senate under Democratic control\u8212\'20\'14spread the word," Alsobrooks said on social media Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks, 53 years old, previously served as state's attorney in Prince George's County and as a prosecutor before taking over as the county's top official. In overcoming Trone's big advertising advantage, she locked up the support of much of the state's Democratic political establishment, including Gov. \uc2 Wes Moore\uc2 , Sen. \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  and Reps. \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  and \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , among others.\par \par \uc2 Hogan, who was heavily recruited by Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/anti-trump-republican-larry-hogan-runs-for-senate-in-maryland-79e337f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entered the Senate race }}}\uc2 in February and quickly established a sizable lead in hypothetical matchups against either Democrat in opinion surveys, but recent polling has shown a tightening contest. As a centrist GOP governor of a blue state, Hogan was able to largely focus on state and local issues during his terms, while also being critical of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I will stand up to the current president, the former president, to the Democratic Party, or the Republican Party," Hogan said in remarks after winning the GOP primary Tuesday night. "I will continue to be the same strong independent leader for Maryland that I always have been."\par \par \uc2 Democrats expect the Senate race and its emphasis on national issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be more challenging for Hogan, who has said he would caucus with Republicans if elected. He easily won his primary Tuesday night. Hogan has said he would oppose a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but hasn't said if he would support federal legislation codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. In 2022, he vetoed state legislation to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Maryland by ending a restriction that only physicians could perform them.\par \par \uc2 It isn't clear if Hogan's popularity as governor will carry over to the Senate race, where party politics loom larger.\par \par \uc2 In gubernatorial races, voters in blue states such as Maryland and Massachusetts "will give themselves permission to reach across partisan lines and elect a Republican they like and respect," said Len Foxwell, a Democratic political consultant in Maryland. "That does not translate in any way to Senate races, in which the issues are nationalized."\par \par \uc2 This fall, voters in Maryland will vote on whether to enshrine the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks's victory marked a comeback for a candidate who had trailed in polling for months in the face of Trone's unprecedented spending. The 68-year-old founder of \uc2 Total Wine & More\uc2  sank nearly $62 million into the race, becoming the biggest-ever self-funder in a Senate primary. Trone spent more on ads in the statewide race than President Biden's re-election campaign has nationwide to date.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Who do you think will win Maryland's open Senate seat? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 But Trone stumbled at times in his efforts to navigate issues of race and other sensitive matters, both in his ads and public appearances.\par \par \uc2 He used an antiquated racial slur during a congressional hearing on tax policy, when he said he meant to say "bugaboo." He apologized. An attack ad from the Trone campaign backfired when a Black elected official in it said the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  is "not a place for training wheels," in a dig at Alsobrooks. The spot drew a letter of condemnation from Black female elected officials, activists and church leaders.\par \par \uc2 Black voters make up about 46% of registered Democrats and 24% of all registered voters in Maryland, according to L2, a nonpartisan vendor of voter data.\par \par \uc2 In other primary contests Tuesday, West Virginia Gov. \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  cruised to victory in his GOP Senate primary to succeed retiring Democratic Sen. \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , defeating Rep. Alex Mooney. Swing-district GOP Rep. \uc2 Don Bacon\uc2  also won his Nebraska primary easily.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kristina Peterson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kristina.peterson@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kristina.peterson@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240515ek5f000m9\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
