\par\par \uc2 Wonder Land\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump's Wildwood Days; The raucous New Jersey rally had the outlines of a broader election appeal.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Henninger \par \uc2 923 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2024\par 21:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 At times it gets hard to see the line that divides \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the presidential candidate from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the pop culture figure.\par \par \uc2 After spending days in a Manhattan courtroom listening to porn star Stormy Daniels tell tales of a tryst in a Vegas hotel, The Donald spent Saturday on the boardwalk in Wildwood, N.J. After that week, who wouldn't go to Wildwood?\par \par \uc2 New Jersey is a state that named a rest stop on its parkway after Jon Bon Jovi. Mr. Trump, who one guesses was a get-around adolescent in the New York City borough of Queens, no doubt remembers teen idol Bobby Rydell's 1963 hit, "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kYev9lXE2J8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wildwood Days}}}\uc2 ," an anthem to summer fun. It's no surprise Mr. Trump would want to spend Saturday with some 100,000 of his closest friends at a rally in Wildwood.\par \par \uc2 Even with a chance to visit wonderful Wildwood, the media was not impressed. The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 's lead conclusion: "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Saturday insulted the prosecutor who has charged him in his ongoing New York criminal trial, speaking at a large rally on the Jersey Shore filled with personal attacks, coarse language and vulgar expressions from the former president and his supporters."\par \par \uc2 All true. But that wasn't all he said.\par \par \uc2 A main theme of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's presidential campaign is the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As headlines everywhere noted last month, "Biden blames Trump for Florida's six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, says women nationwide face health crisis." Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is building her entire campaign around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Late in the Wildwood rally, Mr. Trump addressed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For the record, it is worth quoting. The media covered the s-word but had nothing on the a-word.\par \par \uc2 "We've also gotten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of the federal government and back to the states," Mr. Trump said, a reference to the Supreme Court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization (2022), which overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 "[It] is now up to the will of the people in each state," he said. "Some states will be more conservative and others will be more liberal. . . . Some will have more weeks than others, or many more weeks."\par \par \uc2 In a bow to political reality, he described the recent results on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures in two Midwestern states: "If you take a look at Ohio, they just voted a different vote than people thought, much more liberal, you would say, much more, as they would say, progressive. . . . Kansas the same thing. But that's the way it is, and it's something that we should cherish."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump's position as he described it Saturday is more in sync with what \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  said during the primaries. If Mr. Trump blunts this issue, a huge crack opens in the Biden "extremist" strategy.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, Mr. Trump running against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  got 48% of the independent vote. In 2020 against Mr. Biden, that fell to 41%. To win now, Mr. Trump has to expand beyond his ever-loyal base. Wildwood's 100,000 people were a big, raucous crowd, but so what? In 2020, some 1.8 million New Jerseyans voted for Mr. Trump, who lost the state by 16 points. On Saturday, the former president said he could win New Jersey, Minnesota and Virginia. How?\par \par \uc2 Politico's representative described the Wildwood speech as "well-worn lines on the border, windmills and electric vehicles, China and migrants." Biden-Trump is a long slog, and May is a tad early to dismiss the details. This rally speech suggested the outlines of a Trump effort at a broader appeal, and I don't mean his apparent pitch for the cannibal vote, at one point referring to the "late, great Hannibal Lecter, a wonderful man." Go figure.\par \par \uc2 As usual, Mr. Trump talked at length about illegal migrants, a now-potent issue handed him by Mr. Biden, who chose to let millions flow across the southern border.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump ripped into the persistence of inflation under Mr. Biden, but more notable was his attempt to "suburbanize" these high economic costs.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey, he said, has "some of the highest property and sales taxes in the nation," which is true. He added, "Instead of a tax hike, I'll give you a middle class, lower class, upper class, and business class tax cut." The Biden tax {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/03/11/fact-sheet-the-presidents-budget-cuts-taxes-for-working-families-and-makes-big-corporations-and-the-wealthy-pay-their-fair-share/#:~:text=Now, President Biden's Budget will,a penny in new taxes."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledge}}}\uc2  is no one making less than $400,000 will "pay a penny in new taxes." Which is more appealing, or credible?\par \par \uc2 He denounced "\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's insane electric-vehicle mandate," but mainly as a matter of allowing greater individual choice. "You can buy electric if you want," he said, "you can buy gas if you want, and that's the way it should be."\par \par \uc2 A promise to keep "men out of women's sports" drew loud applause. Less predictable was his attack on a Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/07/27/biden-harris-administration-announces-actions-to-lower-housing-costs-and-boost-supply/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal}}}\uc2  to require the construction of denser housing in the suburbs: "He will destroy your property value, he will destroy your wealth."\par \par \uc2 In short, Mr. Trump is making personal federal coercion an election issue. That pushes past his base.\par \par \uc2 I am making this speech sound more coherent than it came out in the Trumpian stream of disconnected consciousness. As always, the whatabouts abound. But if Mr. Trump ever gets out of his own way, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's definition of "MAGA extremists" may need to be expanded.\par \par \uc2 Write henninger@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240515ek5f006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
