\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 New York Judge Strikes  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Related Measure From November Ballot; Legislature failed to comply with requirement for putting equal-rights amendment before voters, judge says\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2024\par 19:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A New York judge has struck a measure from the November ballot that Democrats had hoped would put {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-election-ballot-2024-3c50731d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the politically potent issue of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  front and center for several competitive congressional elections.\par \par \uc2 The New York measure provides broad equal-rights protections, including for pregnancy and reproductive healthcare, that supporters say would make laws restricting abortions unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 Justice Daniel Doyle, a lower court judge in upstate New York, said the state legislature had failed to follow the proper procedure for putting a measure on the ballot. The legislature's misstep, said Doyle: a failure to give the state's attorney general time to issue an advisory opinion before the vote.\par \par \uc2 The legislature's quick vote "frustrated the deliberative process," the judge wrote.\par \par \uc2 The ruling, while technical in nature, is at least a temporary blow to advocates and Democrats who have sought to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measures on the ballot in more than half a dozen states for the November election. Some advocates have feared that trying to mount campaigns in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so many states could lead to efforts  }}}\uc2  that are hastily put together or poorly funded.\par \par \uc2 The state's attorney general, Letitia James, said she plans to appeal the ruling. Democrats say they expect the case to move quickly and that they will still be able to get the measure on the ballot and have sufficient time to mount a campaign to voters. If they do lose on appeal, however, the measure is unlikely to get on the ballot this November.\par \par \uc2 "This is a disappointing court decision, but we will appeal because New Yorkers deserve to be protected by their Constitution, especially as our basic freedoms and rights are under attack," James said.\par \par \uc2 The idea for a referendum on an equal rights amendment in New York germinated for years mostly among lawmakers. State legislators in July 2022 took the first required step to put it on the ballot, just days after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York was legalized before the 1973 Roe decision, but state lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-vote-on-abortion-bill-on-roe-v-wade-anniversary-11548162001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overhauled and strengthened  }}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in 2019. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed in the first 24 weeks of pregnancy or later, if doctors determine it necessary for the health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs in the lawsuit, a Republican state legislator and two of her constituents, said that in its haste the legislature had failed to comply with a provision of the state's constitution that requires the legislature give the state attorney general time to issue an opinion about the measure's impact on other constitutional provisions before voting.\par \par \uc2 "They were in such a rush and a frenzy" that they failed to follow this requirement, said Christian Browne, an attorney for the plaintiffs.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  , a Democrat, said "our decades-long fight to protect equality and reproductive freedom will not be thrown off track by one extremist judge and I look forward to casting my ballot for the Equal Rights Amendment in November."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jimmy.vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jimmy.vielkind@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jimmy Vielkind at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240507ek57005v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
