\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Florida Activists Gird for November Vote to Undo Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law; Voters have preserved  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in other states, but passing such a measure in Florida could be more difficult\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephanie Armour and James V. Grimaldi \par \uc2 1,525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2024\par 09:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups with a deep war chest are facing off against organizers determined to protect a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/six-week-abortion-ban-florida-c5f00f7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near ban on the procedure in Florida }}}\uc2  that went into effect this month.\par \par \uc2 The pitched battle is over a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/florida-abortion-rulings-to-keep-issue-front-and-center-in-november-1168511c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November ballot initiative }}}\uc2  that would override the state's new ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks and enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the Florida constitution. Democrats view the ballot measure as a catalyst that will galvanize party voters, possibly putting the red state in play for President Biden.\par \par \uc2 But it is also a steeper hurdle for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters than in past battles because Florida requires a supermajority to pass ballot initiatives. That has transformed the organizing effort into an expensive and multimillion-dollar referendum that could deliver organizers their first loss and potentially shape the outcome of other races on the ballot, including contests for the White House and Congress.\par \par \uc2 "In many ways, all eyes are on Florida to see what the future is going to hold for the protection of life," said \uc2 Roger Severino\uc2 , vice president of domestic policy at \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . "It's a big, important state. It's a bellwether and could dictate a lot of the future landscape in the next few years."\par \par \uc2 The referendum would bar any law from restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus is viable, which is generally around 24-28 weeks, or when a healthcare provider determines an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary to protect the patient's health. The current six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban for most abortions that went into effect May 1 replaced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 15-week ban on most abortions }}}\uc2  that was signed by Republican Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Voters on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other ballot initiatives }}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 places like California, Michigan, Ohio, Kansas and Vermont }}}\uc2  have favored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But Florida has tilted even more red in recent years, and its voters supported former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016 and 2020. The 60% total that ballot organizers need for the measure to pass is a perilously high aim because Florida has 5.24 million active registered Republican voters\u8212\'20\'14almost a million more than Democrats, according to the Florida Division of Elections.\par \par \uc2 Floridians Protecting Freedom, a statewide campaign driving the initiative known as Amendment Four, has raised almost $18 million and $2 million in-kind contributions, according to the most recent campaign finance reports ending in March. Fundraising is still brisk. Think Big America, Illinois Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2 's group backing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, has given $500,000 to the Florida ballot campaign, and plans to provide research, financial support and communications support, a Think Big spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 "If we don't put an end to this, legislators won't stop," said Lauren Brenzel, the group's campaign director. She said of the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that "many women don't know they are pregnant at six weeks. It's one of the most draconian bans."\par \par \uc2 Behind the scenes, \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  also is heavily involved in pushing the ballot amendment. The group has provided funding, and some organizers and volunteers have ties to the group.\par \par \uc2 Brenzel, who served as statewide organizing director for the Florida Alliance of Planned Parenthood Affiliates, said the effort will include major outreach to get the measure passed. On the ground, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists say they are working at a feverish pace and trained 500 volunteers in a week to be messengers of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 With training sessions on how to communicate about the initiative, they hope to sway Florida's moderate Republicans and independents by portraying the near-ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an intrusive political interference in private medical decisions.\par \par \uc2 The message resonates with some GOP voters such as former Republican state Rep. Carlos Lacasa, who broke with his party to gather signatures to get the measure on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 "I've always been wary of the government trying to take privacy rights away from us," he said. "The issue of a woman's right to choose is a privacy issue. Once my neighbor's rights are compromised, mine are next."\par \par \uc2 On the other side of the battle are antiabortion groups with ties to Catholic organizations. They describe their struggle as a David vs. Goliath standoff against supporters who are armed with the financial and planning power of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lila Rose, founder and president of the antiabortion organization Live Action, said \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  is pouring "a ton of cash for the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  side" into pushing the ballot amendment.\par \par \uc2 In fact, \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  and its Florida affiliates have donated about $4.5 million to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group, giving more than any other group, but it is only about a quarter of the total, campaign-finance reports show.\par \par \uc2 The antiabortion side has raised about $76,000, primarily from the Florida Conference of Catholic Bishops, state financial disclosures show. Support for the measure is greater likely because funds were needed to gather signatures to get it on the ballot, while the opponents are just beginning to ramp up for the campaign.\par \par \uc2 In addition, opponents will benefit from evangelical organization Faith & Freedom Coalition, a group that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and plans a national campaign for Trump. The group plans to knock on the doors of one million evangelical voters' homes in Florida, and more than 6,000 churches in Florida will distribute their voter guides.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis and other Florida Republicans have criticized the ballot measure as extreme, and opponents are looking at ways to challenge the legality of the initiative if it passes.\par \par \uc2 The president last month campaigned in Tampa, saying Trump is eroding women's \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden's comments last month that the state is in play was mocked by Florida GOP leaders and earned a rebuttal from DeSantis, who in an April 23 press event said, "Floridians are not buying what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is selling."\par \par \uc2 Since 1952, Democratic presidential candidates have won Florida only five times. Hoping to add to those wins, the Biden campaign has opened more than 130 offices in the state.\par \par \uc2 Recent polls show organizers don't yet have a supermajority, with a significant share of voters still undecided. An Emerson College Polling survey on April 11 found 42% of voters plan to vote yes on the November ballot measure that will provide a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, 32% are unsure, and 25% will vote no.\par \par \uc2 Democrats see opportunity. On May 1, the day the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  launched a sky banner over Trump's Mar-a-Lago resort in Palm Beach that read "Trump's Plan: Ban \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Punish Women."\par \par \uc2 Sara Johnson, statewide grass-roots director at Florida Voters Against Extremism, a political committee opposed to the amendment, said the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws would be among the most liberal in America if it passes.\par \par \uc2 "We are committed to making sure that every Florida voter knows the truth about Amendment Four\u8212\'20\'14that it is deceptive and extreme," she said.\par \par \uc2 The group's chairperson is Mary Jo O'Sullivan, a doctor of maternal fetal medicine and medical director at Heartbeat of Miami, a pregnancy resource center that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Treasurer Noreen Fenner is a former legislative and executive branch lobbyist who is also a former Florida county treasurer for the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mathew Staver is considering legal strategies for overturning the ballot initiative if it passes. The 67-year-old lawyer in 1989 launched Liberty Counsel, a nonprofit Christian ministry, with his wife, Anita. The counsel focuses on litigation, education and policy organization that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He argues that the referendum is too vague and addresses too many issues to withstand a legal test.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think Florida voters will overturn the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "There are 58 categories of healthcare providers," said Staver, who argued unsuccessfully before the Florida Supreme Court to block the amendment from the ballot. "You could have a tattoo artist saying it's necessary for the health of the mother."\par \par \uc2 Staver is a former vice president of \uc2 Liberty University\uc2 , which was founded by \uc2 Jerry Falwell\uc2 . He is working with groups such as Liberty Counsel Action, Florida Right to Life and the Florida Family Planning Council to educate voters about the ballot measure he says is broad and confusing.\par \par \uc2 Outreach will include pamphlets, postcards, handouts, yard signs, bumper stickers, meetings and events to mobilize voters.\par \par \uc2 Staver bristles at the notion Florida could be in play over the ballot measure. Instead, Staver said, it could drive turnout among voters opposed to the measure who would be loath to back the current president.\par \par \uc2 "Biden thinks the ballot could put the state at play, but it could be a millstone around Biden's neck," Staver said. "It actually could backfire."\par \par \uc2 Write to Stephanie Armour at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Stephanie.Armour@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie.Armour@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and James V. Grimaldi at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:james.grimaldi@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 james.grimaldi@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240505ek550008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
