\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Arizona Legislature Votes to Repeal State's Ban on Virtually All Abortions; Democratic governor promises to sign the measure overturning the restrictions, but they could be in place for a few months this summer\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 940 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par 21:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PHOENIX\u8212\'20\'14Two Republicans joined with Democrats in the Arizona Senate to roll back the state's nearly total ban on abortions, as some in the GOP look to reverse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a significant political liability }}}\uc2  for the party ahead of the November elections.\par \par \uc2 The move Wednesday comes a week after the Arizona state House also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/gavin-newsom-arizona-abortion-california-5c1f3382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to repeal the ban }}}\uc2 . Three Republicans joined with all Democrats in that vote.\par \par \uc2 "This total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban would have jailed doctors, threatened the lives of women across our state and stripped millions of Arizonans of their bodily autonomy," Democratic Gov. \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  said in a written statement. Her office said she would sign the bill Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona Supreme Court's decision last month to bring back {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-ban-821501cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 160-year-old, near-total ban }}}\uc2  on the procedure inflamed the politics in one of the country's top electoral battlegrounds, which is now effectively ground zero for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics. It hasn't gone into effect yet and the state's 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is still the law of the land.\par \par \uc2 However, because of a quirk in legislative procedure in Arizona, residents are likely to spend much of their summer under the 160-year-old law because bills in the state typically take effect 90 days after the legislative session ends. The state's Democratic attorney general has said she is looking at legal options to keep the Civil War-era ban from taking place at all.\par \par \uc2 Republican Sens. Shawnna Bolick and T.J. Shope crossed party lines to advance the measure. Both are seen as Democratic targets in this year's election. Bolick is also married to one of the Supreme Court justices who voted to reinstate the ban.\par \par \uc2 Even though the ban was overturned, Democrats are still expected to campaign heavily on access to the procedure in Arizona and elsewhere across the U.S., arguing that former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sowed uncertainty by nominating justices to the Supreme Court who repealed the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Republicans are likely to continue to push to limit access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Arizona voters are expected to consider at least one ballot measure to expand access to the procedure beyond 15 weeks, along with at least a half-dozen other states. One of them is Florida, which put in place a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban Wednesday, giving Democrats another opportunity to cast Republicans as extreme on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Across our nation, we witness a full-on assault, state by state, on reproductive freedom. And understand who's to blame. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this," Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said Wednesday in Jacksonville, Fla.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-calls-for-release-of-wall-street-journal-reporter-evan-gershkovich-c6804a94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Time magazine }}}\uc2  published Tuesday, didn't directly answer whether he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president, saying he didn't think a bill would get to the president's desk, adding: "It's about states' rights." Asked whether he was supportive of states punishing women who seek abortions or monitoring pregnancies to try to prevent abortions, he said those decisions should be with the states.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How will the Arizona Legislature's move to repeal the state's ban on nearly all abortions affect the November elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is seen as one of the most important states ahead of the November election. Voters in the state could decide who controls the White House and each chamber of Congress. The state Senate and state House, both currently controlled by Republicans, are also viewed as highly competitive.\par \par \uc2 The decision to bring back the near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen as helpful for Democrats who are on defense regarding other major issues in the state, such as the economy and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Bolick said in a lengthy floor speech Wednesday that she opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and wanted "to protect more babies," which was why she was voting to return to the 15-week ban. Some Republicans have argued that returning the state to a 15-week restriction could help blunt the chances of the ballot measure passing.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the state legislature are also considering getting their own more restrictive initiatives on the ballot, including a measure that would allow for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the beginning of the 15th week, according to a strategy memo viewed by The Wall Street Journal last month.\par \par \uc2 Most Republicans in the state Senate wanted to keep the 160-year-old ban. "The epitome of delusion is saying I am pro-life yet voting to repeal an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban," Sen. Anthony Kern, a Republican who opposed the repeal, said on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Trump and Kari Lake, the expected GOP Senate candidate, have said the outright ban goes too far and have called on the legislature to remove it. But Lake has also said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://idahodispatch.com/kari-lake-visits-idaho-responds-to-idaho-chooses-life-criticism/#google_vignette"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the Idaho Dispatch }}}\uc2  last month that given the attorney general had said she wouldn't enforce it, "we don't have that law as much as many of us wish we did."\par \par \uc2 A Wall Street Journal poll from March {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-biden-poll-swing-states-ad594acb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found Arizona voters }}}\uc2  were most likely to say that they wouldn't support a candidate they disagreed with on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the poll, which was conducted before the Arizona ruling, the majority of voters there said they supported access to the procedure\u8212\'20\'14and more voters said they backed President Biden's approach than that of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240501ek510050l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
