\par\par \uc2 World News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 Trump Calls for Release of Wall Street Journal Reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 ; 'I think he's a very brave young man,' says former president\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Leary and Vivian Salama \par \uc2 1,170 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 April 2024\par 19:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  should be freed from a Russian jail.\par \par \uc2 "The reporter should be released and he will be released," Trump told Time magazine in an interview published Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich, 32 years old, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/evan-gershkovichs-stolen-year-in-a-russian-jail-61234ec9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was detained in Russia }}}\uc2  on March 29, 2023, while doing his job as a journalist. He is being held on an allegation of espionage that he, the Journal and the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  vehemently deny.\par \par \uc2 The State Department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-deems-wsj-reporter-evan-gershkovich-wrongfully-detained-by-russia-f1be833"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has declared Gershkovich wrongfully detained }}}\uc2  and President Biden has promised his family he would bring him home. On April 23, a Moscow court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/russian-court-rejects-wsj-reporter-evan-gershkovichs-appeal-against-detention-f3112f37"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected an appeal by Gershkovich }}}\uc2  against his detention, meaning the U.S. citizen, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/a-timeline-of-evan-gershkovichs-year-in-a-russian-prison-7c9b7d4f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been awaiting trial }}}\uc2  for more than a year, will remain behind bars until at least June 30.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/campaigning-biden-and-court-bound-trump-collide-in-new-york-c05a37a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing a rematch with Biden }}}\uc2 , hadn't previously publicly weighed in on the journalist's plight.\par \par \uc2 Asked by Time why he hadn't called for Gershkovich's release earlier, Trump said: "I guess because I have so many other things I'm working on. I have hundreds of things."\par \par \uc2 "And I probably have said very good things about him," Trump added. "Maybe it wasn't reported. I think he's a very brave young man."\par \par \uc2 Trump sat for the magazine interview on April 12, in a wide-ranging discussion that touched on various topics. The cover story published Tuesday with the headline, "If he wins."\par \par \uc2 Trump has often touted his relationship with Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . "Here's the difference between me and Biden: I'll get him released," Trump said. "Putin's going to release him," he added, referring to Gershkovich.\par \par \uc2 The Russian Embassy in Washington didn't respond to a request for comment Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 White House spokesman Andrew Bates noted Biden has brought home more than 60 Americans who were held hostage or wrongfully detained abroad, and has worked ceaselessly for Gershkovich.\par \par \uc2 "President Biden welcomes this new support for bringing Evan back from Russia, and he will continue to demand both Evan and Paul's release."\par \par \uc2 American Paul Whelan, a former U.S. Marine and corporate-security executive, has been held in Russia since 2018 and is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/u-s-responds-to-putin-with-call-for-release-of-evan-gershkovich-paul-whelan-aeea4e53"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serving a 16-year sentence }}}\uc2  for espionage that he, the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  and his family say is bogus.\par \par \uc2 Biden mentioned both men during a speech Saturday at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-calls-for-release-of-wsj-journalist-evan-gershkovich-141d2361"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House Correspondents' Association dinner }}}\uc2 . "We're not going to give up until we get them home," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Putin should release Evan," the president added. "We are doing everything we can."\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Journal said, "We are encouraged by the ongoing, bipartisan support shown for Evan and continue to call for his immediate release. The time to bring him home is now."\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich is the first American journalist to be held in Russia on an allegation of espionage since the end of the Cold War. The State Department has said he isn't a spy and has never worked for the government, and has called for his immediate release.\par \par \uc2 "This year has been unimaginable for our family in so many ways. It has felt like holding our breath," his family wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/it-has-felt-like-holding-our-breath-dfd5d3ec?st=8lzx6jy3gf0ssb9&reflink=desktopwebshare_permalink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter to Journal readers }}}\uc2  in late March. "We have been living with a constant ache in our hearts thinking about Evan every moment of every day."\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/u-s-and-russia-pursue-secret-prisoner-swap-talks-russian-diplomat-says-0229afc0?st=osbg05rskejgyat&reflink=desktopwebshare_permalink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Journal reported }}}\uc2  that the U.S. and Russia are using a confidential channel to discuss a potential prisoner exchange that could include Gershkovich and Whelan.\par \par \uc2 Putin said in an interview with former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  in February that he was open to an exchange for Gershkovich.\par \par \uc2 Biden has secured the release of a number of political prisoners, including women's basketball star Brittney Griner from Russia in 2022 as part of a prisoner swap with Russian arms dealer Viktor Bout, a deal Trump described as a "one-sided disaster."\par \par \uc2 Trump secured the release of several U.S. hostages and detainees, some of them through prisoner swaps. His administration brokered a prisoner exchange with Iran in 2019, freeing \uc2 Xiyue Wang\uc2 , a graduate student at \uc2 Princeton University\uc2  who was serving a 10-year sentence in Iran on espionage charges. Wang {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/iran-sentences-princeton-grad-student-on-spy-charges-1500242286?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was arrested in Tehran in 2016 }}}\uc2  while researching century-old manuscripts. U.S. officials have denied Wang was a spy. The U.S., in exchange, freed Masoud Soleimani, an Iranian scientist convicted of export violations.\par \par \uc2 In the Time interview, Trump spoke about a prospective second-term agenda that would include extending tax cuts he signed into law in his first term and a much more aggressive stance on immigration. He told the magazine he would carry out a mass-deportation effort, relying on the National Guard to remove 11 million people. He would also look to deny federal funding to local jurisdictions whose police forces decline to help.\par \par \uc2 Trump repeated his vow to pardon those who participated in the Jan. 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol, part of an effort to overturn his loss to Biden. He didn't rule out possible violence surrounding the coming election. "If we don't win, you know, it depends," Trump said. "It always depends on the fairness of the election."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  in reaction Tuesday said, "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's repeated threats of political violence are as horrifying and dangerous as they are un-American."\par \par \uc2 Pressed on whether he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president, he didn't directly answer, saying he didn't think a bill would get to the president's desk and saying, "It's about states' rights." Asked if he was supportive of states punishing women who seek abortions or monitoring pregnancies to try to prevent abortions, he said those decisions should be with the states.\par \par \uc2 "It's irrelevant whether I'm comfortable or not," Trump said. "It's totally irrelevant, because the states are going to make those decisions."\par \par \uc2 The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/abortion-donald-trump-2024-election-fe641cc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has tried to straddle the subject of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , at once heralding the overturning of Roe v. Wade but avoiding getting too specific about limitations on the procedure. He has said he supports exceptions for rape and incest and to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Trump declined to say how he would vote in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum in Florida in November that would restore broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state. He also said he would be releasing a statement on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone. The Supreme Court recently heard arguments on whether to preserve access to the medication.\par \par \uc2 Biden's campaign condemned Trump's comments in a statement, saying, "November's election will determine whether women in the United States have reproductive freedom."\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Vivian Salama at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:vivian.salama@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vivian.salama@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240430ek4u004s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
