\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Pushes  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Message in Trump's Home State of Florida; The president's Tampa speech comes a week before the state's six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban takes effect\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 754 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2024\par 20:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TAMPA, Fla.\u8212\'20\'14President Biden took his push for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to Florida, where he blamed rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/florida-abortion-ballot-measure-supreme-court-a3340feb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looming six-week ban }}}\uc2  in the Republican's home state as he seeks to keep the issue at the forefront for voters.\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke in Tampa on Tuesday, a week before the state's ban is set to take effect, looking to harness the momentum on an issue that has energized Democrats since the Supreme Court eliminated the right to the procedure in 2022. While the state isn't considered a top presidential battleground, it provides a powerful backdrop as Democrats assail the ban and campaign for a November ballot initiative that would restore broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 "Let's be real clear. There's one person responsible for this nightmare and he's acknowledged and he's bragged about it: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ," Biden said. "He bragged about overturning Roe v. Wade."\par \par \uc2 While polls show Republicans with an edge on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/central-banking/trump-allies-federal-reserve-independence-54423c2f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the economy }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-2024-immigration-issue-voters-84916a17"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration }}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the issue where Democrats have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-poll-trump-swing-state-voters-2024-election-3e12f57c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the greatest advantage }}}\uc2  over Republicans. Biden, who previously espoused more moderate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views and at times has been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-activists-push-for-biden-to-be-more-outspoken-11653044400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reluctant messenger }}}\uc2 , devoted his first rally of the year to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is leaning into the issue with this visit.\par \par \uc2 Biden tied Trump, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee, to bans in Florida and other states, stressing that his predecessor appointed three justices to the court that overturned the Roe decision. Biden pledged to restore federal protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and argued that other freedoms could be at risk, like access to contraception and same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 "Today in 2024, women have fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ," said Biden. "I don't think we're going to let him get away with it, do you?"\par \par \uc2 Trump now makes his home in Florida, but he will be stuck for the next few weeks at his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/trump-hush-money-trial-begins-b0500bb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hush-money trial }}}\uc2  in a Manhattan courtroom. Trump beat Biden in 2020 in Florida by 3.4 percentage points, and recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida polls }}}\uc2  show Trump leading Biden by a wider margin in the state this year.\par \par \uc2 Trump spokesman \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said that "Florida is Trump country." In a statement, Florida Republican Party Chairman Evan Power said: "Floridians' top issues are immigration, the economy, and inflation, in all three areas \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has failed. Instead of coming to talk to Floridians about manufactured issues, he should get to work solving the real issues that he has failed to lead on."\par \par \uc2 Trump has struggled to find his footing on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has offered conflicting positions over the years. He has taken credit for appointing the justices who overturned Roe, but has also said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the states, avoiding a position on a national ban. After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona revived }}}\uc2  a Civil-war era ban on most abortions, he said the state's high court had gone too far.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/six-week-abortion-ban-florida-c5f00f7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On the Florida law }}}\uc2 , Trump has mostly avoided giving a clear answer. But he recently said "Florida's probably, maybe, going to change," adding "it's the will of the people."\par \par \uc2 The Florida law was signed last year by Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . It has limited exceptions, including for rape and incest and for certain medical emergencies. But the state's voters will have the chance to weigh in on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November, on a ballot measure that if successful would restore the broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access the state had before the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since Roe fell, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates have won {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-election-ballot-2024-3c50731d?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven straight referendum victories }}}\uc2 . And Democratic candidates for governor, Congress and state legislative contests have successfully campaigned in opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The Florida ballot measure would need to receive at least 60% approval from voters to pass. A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.faupolling.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/mainstreet-florida-apr-2024-public.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Atlantic University poll }}}\uc2  showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure had the support of 49%, while 19% opposed it and 32% said they didn't know.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are hopeful that turnout will be boosted by ballot measures in multiple states. The Biden campaign hasn't invested heavily in Florida, but Biden Communications Director Michael Tyler told reporters Monday that the campaign isn't writing off the state, saying they "can afford to invest in many paths to victory, and that includes Florida."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240423ek4n004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
