\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 As Trump Stands Trial, Biden Sees Campaign Opening; President has made small gains in polls and is set to receive endorsement from members of Kennedy family\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Thomas \par \uc2 1,433 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 April 2024\par 18:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SCRANTON, Pa.\u8212\'20\'14Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be sitting in a courtroom for much of the next several weeks, giving President Biden a window of opportunity to play offense and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-races-to-trump-proof-his-agenda-92f38239"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 build support }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14if he can take advantage of it.\par \par \uc2 Biden embarked on a multiday tour of Pennsylvania this week as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/donald-trump-hush-money-trial-jury-selection-5a65e772"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jury selection began }}}\uc2  in Trump's criminal hush-money trial in New York, opening a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trumps-split-screen-strategy-put-criminal-trial-at-center-of-his-campaign-0767fb34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential split-screen }}}\uc2  that voters will see this spring.\par \par \uc2 Recent national polls show the race between the two men essentially tied, with Biden's support rising gradually since his State of the Union address in March. Trump still holds a narrow lead in many of the battleground states that will help decide the election, making it imperative for the president to build momentum in states such as Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The start of Trump's trial, which will keep him in the New York City courtroom for four days a week, follows a recent spate of news about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/arizona-republicans-repeal-abortion-ban-da903fa4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban in Arizona }}}\uc2 , another battleground state where Democrats could be helped by an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights ballot initiative in the fall.\par \par \uc2 In Philadelphia, Biden received the endorsement Thursday of several members of the Kennedy family, led by Kerry Kennedy, the daughter of the late Sen. Robert F. Kennedy and niece of President \uc2 John F. Kennedy\uc2 . Kerry Kennedy said Biden had "been a champion for all the rights and freedoms that my father and my uncle stood for," adding: "The Kennedy family endorses \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for president."\par \par \uc2 That comes as \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , the late senator's son, has mounted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/rfk-jr-to-name-nicole-shanahan-as-running-mate-for-presidential-bid-4b9a698e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an independent bid for president }}}\uc2 , with polls showing him getting support in the double-digits. Kennedy said Thursday he had qualified for the ballot in Michigan, a key battleground state. Many Kennedy family members have criticized his campaign, saying it could help elect Trump.\par \par \uc2 But the conflict in the Middle East remains a wild card for Biden as the risk of a broader war between Israel and Iran could inject uncertainty into the campaign and some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/bidens-approach-to-israel-gaza-conflict-angers-both-sides-46fa0280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 young and progressive voters remain unhappy }}}\uc2  with his support for Israel. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/inflation-biden-trump-2024-election-026e7499"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is also still wrestling with inflation }}}\uc2 , a political problem the president has few tools to address.\par \par \uc2 Biden struck a populist tone this week in Scranton, Pa., where he lived as a boy until his family moved to Delaware, portraying Trump as supportive of tax policies that only benefit the wealthy and corporations. Biden said when he viewed the economy, "I don't see it through the eyes of Mar-a-Lago, I see it through the eyes of Scranton," referring to the former president's private club in Palm Beach, Fla.\par \par \uc2 At a union event Wednesday in Pittsburgh, Biden urged his trade office to raise tariffs on imports of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-calls-for-steep-hike-to-tariff-on-chinese-steel-dd131264"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 steel and aluminum from China }}}\uc2 , backing a protectionist approach favored by the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union.\par \par \uc2 Even before this week's split screen, the race appeared to be tightening. An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.economist.com/interactive/us-2024-election/trump-biden-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 average of national public polls }}}\uc2  calculated by the Economist finds Biden and Trump tied, with 44% support each, compared with a 3-point Trump advantage in early February. (Based on recent elections, Biden would need to win the national popular vote by at least a few percentage points to have a good shot at winning the Electoral College.)\par \par \uc2 Polling suggests that several factors could be giving Biden a lift. A Wall Street Journal survey in February found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/voters-are-more-upbeat-on-economy-but-biden-gets-little-benefit-wsj-poll-shows-8e608db8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters shedding some of their pessimism }}}\uc2  about the economy, and consumer sentiment, as measured by the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/consumers/americans-are-finally-feeling-better-about-the-economy-e964804f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has improved markedly }}}\uc2  in recent months, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/consumers/u-s-consumers-still-arent-feeling-sunnier-d1dda3af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 though it slipped }}}\uc2  in March.\par \par \uc2 The renewed attention on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the news might also have helped Biden by shifting voters' focus to that issue and away from problems at the border with Mexico, which is one of Biden's weakest issues. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/WSJ_Swing_State_Poll_Full_Toplines_March_2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Journal polling of seven swing states }}}\uc2  last month, voters said Biden was better able than Trump to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 12 percentage points, but that Trump was better on immigration and border security by 20 points.\par \par \uc2 Next Tuesday, Biden will travel to Tampa, Fla., as his campaign has suggested the state is winnable in large part due to the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Trump won the state by 3 percentage points in 2020, and a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.faupolling.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/mainstreet-florida-apr-2024-public.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Atlantic University poll }}}\uc2  shows Trump leading Biden there among registered voters, 50% to 42%.) The state's higher court earlier this month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/florida-abortion-ballot-measure-supreme-court-a3340feb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared the way for a ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy to take effect, but it also approved a November ballot measure that, if successful, would undo the ruling and restore broad access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jefrey Pollock, a Biden campaign pollster, said the tighter polling reflects a shift since the State of the Union, when many voters who remained doubtful of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/presidential-election-2024-guide-a264d4fe#who-is-running-for-president-in-f489b6d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Biden-Trump rematch }}}\uc2  started to view the election as a choice. "\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took it to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ," Pollock said. "And it was the clear beginning of Biden saying this is going to be a mano a mano, and we're going to have a conversation about my vision and his vision."\par \par \uc2 Republicans note that Trump still has an advantage in the battleground states. The Journal survey found the former president leading in six of the seven most competitive states, with Trump holding leads of between 2 and 8 percentage points in six states\u8212\'20\'14Pennsylvania, Michigan, Arizona, Georgia, Nevada and North Carolina. In each case, the lead was within or right at the edge of the poll's margin of error.\par \par \uc2 Trump spokeswoman Karoline Leavitt said the former president was winning "because voters are tired of Biden's weakness, record-high inflation and open border chaos," and that the campaign is expanding operations in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Trump made an appearance at a Harlem bodega in New York City following Tuesday's court proceedings and planned to hold a rally Saturday in Wilmington, N.C., offering a window into how he is likely to proceed during the trial. His campaign is planning events in and around New York as well as additional rallies in battleground states. He will increase media interviews, people familiar with the strategy say, and has the ability to do virtual events in the evenings.\par \par \uc2 The Harlem event, scene of a 2022 assault on a store clerk\u8212\'20\'14who fatally stabbed his attacker\u8212\'20\'14was designed for Trump to highlight fears over violent crime, even as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/murder-rates-down-new-york-san-francisco-philadelphia-508b6855"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numbers overall are down nationally }}}\uc2  from pandemic highs.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How should President Biden take advantage of an opportunity to gain ground against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Manhattan District Attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , a Democrat, charged the bodega clerk Jose Alba with second-degree murder before later dropping the charges amid a backlash. Bragg also brought the hush-money charges against Trump.\par \par \uc2 "There's no crime," Trump claimed of his own prosecution. "You know where the crime is\u8212\'20\'14in the bodegas where they come and rob them every week."\par \par \uc2 Even though the trial, replete with unsavory accusations, will curtail Trump's ability to actively campaign, his allies said the proceedings will help him press his case against what he calls the unfair nature of the nation's justice system.\par \par \uc2 "Seeing him in court reinforces the message the president has been putting out there\u8212\'20\'14Democrats attempt to keep me off the ballot," said \uc2 David Urban\uc2 , a senior adviser to Trump's 2016 campaign effort in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Urban said it remained unclear how a potential conviction in the case might affect the electorate. "It's a Rorschach test\u8212\'20\'14people are going to see what they want to see," he said.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-trial-indictment-hush-money-poll-b3d9a555993faf22e6ebfaf798bfbd2b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent AP-NORC poll }}}\uc2  found 35% of Americans thought Trump committed a crime in the hush-money trial, the lowest percentage to express that belief among the four criminal cases he faces. But the survey also found that 50% of respondents said he would be unfit to be president if convicted in the New York case, while 29% said he would still be fit and 21% weren't sure.\par \par \uc2 The White House and the Biden campaign have declined to weigh in on Trump's trial, saying the president is focused on his work. But Biden repeatedly reminds voters of his predecessor's past statements and warns that Trump, if re-elected, would threaten the underpinnings of the nation's democracy.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Zitner and Alex Leary contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ken Thomas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ken.thomas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ken.thomas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240418ek4i001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
