\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Arizona Republicans Block Another Push to Repeal  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Election battleground state is at center of fight for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access after reinstatement of 160-year-old ban, set to take effect in coming weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 1,124 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2024\par 22:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PHOENIX\u8212\'20\'14Republicans in the Arizona state House blocked two attempts Wednesday to repeal the state's 160-year-old near total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite pressure on the GOP\u8212\'20\'14including from former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14to change course on the hot-button issue.\par \par \uc2 But later in the day, two Senate Republicans joined with Democrats\u8212\'20\'14enough to create a majority\u8212\'20\'14to move forward on their version of a repeal. A final vote on the bill could be weeks away. If the Senate does ultimately vote to repeal the ban, the measure would go back to the House, where it would still face a difficult path.\par \par \uc2 Democrats had been hopeful that a small number of Republicans would join with them in both chambers forcing a vote to overturn the law, which is expected to go into effect in early summer. However, in the House, just one Republican ended up joining with Democrats in a failed effort to overcome a GOP blockade of the measure, even as the political reality of having one of the strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the country set in.\par \par \uc2 The earlier votes took place as antiabortion and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access advocates filled the House.\par \par \uc2 Arizona has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become ground zero }}}\uc2  in the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after the state Supreme Court reinstated a 160-year-old law earlier this month banning nearly all abortions. The ruling has given some momentum to Democrats in a state that could decide the White House and both chambers of Congress.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Arizona has been allowed through 15 weeks of pregnancy under a law the GOP-controlled state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-legislature-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11648156791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed in 2022 }}}\uc2 . The state's high court said in its April 9 decision that the recent law doesn't override one dating to 1864\u8212\'20\'14before Arizona was a state\u8212\'20\'14that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy except in lifesaving situations.\par \par \uc2 "I would ask everyone in this chamber to respect the fact that some of us\u8230\'20\'26believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in fact the murder of children," Speaker Ben Toma, a Republican, said on the House floor.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Alma Hernandez, a Democrat, responded: "The fact that we will not even entertain a motion to allow those who have been raped or pregnant by incest to be able to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is extremely, extremely disappointing."\par \par \uc2 Polling shows the majority of Americans and Arizonans aren't aligned with Republicans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A Wall Street Journal poll from March {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-biden-poll-swing-states-ad594acb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found Arizona voters }}}\uc2  were most likely to say that they wouldn't support a candidate they disagreed with on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the poll, which was conducted before the Arizona ruling, the majority of voters there said they supported access to the procedure\u8212\'20\'14and more voters said they backed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Biden }}}\uc2 's approach than that of Trump, the presumptive GOP presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of the political ramifications of the decision, Trump and Kari Lake, the expected GOP Senate candidate, both have said the outright ban goes too far and called on the legislature to remove it. Both previously said they oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Trump has touted his nomination of three justices to the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  who helped overturn Roe v. Wade, and Lake had praised the ban. In recent days, Lake has called some GOP lawmakers and urged them to vote to roll back the measure and offered them support for doing so, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 "President Trump has long been consistent in supporting the rights of states to make decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Trump spokeswoman Karoline Leavitt said in a statement after the votes Wednesday. A Lake spokesman didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 "Ask the women of Arizona if they are 'happy' or they think it is 'incredible' that Trump overturned Roe and took their rights back to 1864," Biden spokesman James Singer said in a statement, noting past comments Trump had made in reference to the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's overturning of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have been gathering signatures to put a measure on the ballot in November that would expand access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability, or about halfway through a typical pregnancy. The coalition of groups has said they already have more than enough signatures to get on the ballot. Democrats are hopeful that in addition to passing, it will help voters turn out for their candidates in November.\par \par \uc2 An effort last week to repeal the 1864 law by Rep. Matt Gress, who represents a competitive seat, was quashed by GOP lawmakers. Gress was the only Republican to cross party lines Wednesday in the House. In the Senate, Republicans Shawnna Bolick\u8212\'20\'14who is married to one of the high court judges who voted to put in place the ban\u8212\'20\'14and T.J. Shope joined with Democrats.\par \par \uc2 All three along with several other Republican lawmakers are top targets for Democrats in this year's election. Democrats believe the GOP majority is particularly vulnerable on this issue and Republicans' refusal to repeal the ban puts their fragile majority in play.\par \par \uc2 The GOP is fractured on this issue because some members of its base oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and members who represent conservative districts face pressure to hold strong in support of the ban.\par \par \uc2 Alternative proposals, presented by the House GOP counsel during a virtual meeting with Republicans on Monday, offered the party other options to address the total ban.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How should Arizona Republicans approach the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The strategy memo, reviewed by The Wall Street Journal, offered several suggestions for how the Arizona legislature could deal with the issue, including offering additional ballot measures, aimed at undermining the viability ballot measure's chance of passage.\par \par \uc2 One of the proposed options would be titled something related to a 15-week measure but was described in the GOP memo as "a 14-week law disguised as a 15-week law because it would only allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the beginning of the 15th week." Another option would allow an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the sixth week of pregnancy, with some exceptions after the limit. There was also a proposed ballot initiative that would only take effect if the viability measure was passed and would still allow lawmakers to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "This shows yet again why Arizonans can't leave our most basic and personal rights in the hands of politicians," Dawn Penich, a spokesperson for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access ballot initiative, said in response to the leaked presentation.\par \par \uc2 Laura Kusisto contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240417ek4h001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
