\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Kari Lake's Baby Bonus Bust; New entitlements won't work as political cover for an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 624 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2024\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week said he won't support a federal limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , no doubt noticing that Republicans are losing elections on the issue. Arizona Republican Senate candidate Kari Lake is now rebooting her own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position while endorsing European-style entitlements for children. This isn't a winning political safe harbor.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake released a five-minute video on Thursday after the Arizona Supreme Court upheld an 1864 state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except to save the mother's life. A state court suspended the law after the Supreme Court's decision in Roe v. Wade, which the U.S. High Court reversed in 2022. Ms. Lake now says the ruling "is out of line with where the people of this state are," which may be true. Ms. Lake now also accepts a woman's right to choose: "I chose life. But I'm not every woman."\par \par \uc2 She adds by way of changing the subject that she "had a real eye-opening experience this last summer," and her revelation is worth examining. "I had the opportunity to visit Hungary, and it completely changed my view of how we should deal with this complicated, difficult issue. In Hungary, what they did I thought was so amazing." When "you get married, they give you a cut in your tax rate."\par \par \uc2 And "by the time a mother has four children, she never pays taxes again. That's called a baby bonus. I think we should do that here in America. We bail out banks and multinational corporations all the time. When's the last time we've given an assist to a struggling mother and a family?"\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake is in part playing to a portion of the Trumpian right that is preoccupied with its Prime Minister \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2 . Budapest offers a bevy of subsidies to families, plus the income-tax advantage.\par \par \uc2 The country's birth rate has increased modestly since 2010, and some subsidies are still relatively new. But the increase may be a blip. At roughly 1.59 children per woman, the country isn't close to a replacement fertility rate of 2.1. Such spending programs have failed to lift declining birth rates across the globe from Europe to Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The price tag is also astonishing. Hungary spends roughly 6% of its economy on family subsidies. That's twice the share the United States dedicates to its entire military and national defense.\par \par \uc2 While she tries to escape the 1864 trap on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ms. Lake is walking into another one. Progressives have long pilloried Republicans as caring about children only until birth. As political cover, some Republicans line up for new programs such as paid family leave, which Ms. Lake also supports.\par \par \uc2 Progressives will bank the progress on expanding the entitlement state and then refuse to compromise on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which Democrats increasingly view as a fundamental right. Ms. Lake also supports "extending the child tax credit," currently $2,000 a year and partially paid in a check to those who owe no income tax\u8212\'20\'14a fact that belies her pander that government does nothing for families. But voters who dig that idea will sign up with her Democratic opponent, Rep. \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , who is offering a bigger family payout.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. is sorting out its views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in decades, and we've counseled Republicans to develop a more cogent policy that meets most voters where they are. But if Republicans start running on converting the U.S. into a European welfare state to dodge difficult questions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they will keep losing and deserve it.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240414ek4e002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
