\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Arizona Supreme Court Bans Nearly All Abortions, Reviving 160-Year-Old Law; Decision thrusts issue back into the national political spotlight and could shake up races in battleground state\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Eliza Collins and Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,045 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par 00:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PHOENIX\u8212\'20\'14Arizona's highest court revived a 160-year-old ban on nearly all abortions, a decision that turns up the political heat on an issue that is pivotal in the battleground state and beyond {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-abortion-poll-election-2024-def7bb14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the 2024 presidential race }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling Tuesday from the Arizona Supreme Court was the latest twist in the patchwork of state laws that has emerged since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade and eliminated constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June 2022. Nearly two years later, rules governing the availability of the procedure remain unsettled for millions of Americans, making it one of the most salient political issues for voters heading into the November elections.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/arizona-republicans-repeal-abortion-ban-da903fa4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  in Arizona }}}\uc2  has been allowed through 15 weeks of pregnancy under a law that the GOP-controlled state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-legislature-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11648156791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed in 2022 }}}\uc2 , shortly before the Supreme Court's ruling. In Tuesday's decision, the state's high court said the recent law didn't override one dating to 1864\u8212\'20\'14before Arizona was a state\u8212\'20\'14that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy except in lifesaving situations.\par \par \uc2 "To date, our legislature has never affirmatively created a right to, or independently authorized, elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Justice John R. Lopez IV wrote in the court's 4-to-2 decision. He added that lawmakers in 2022 made clear that they wished to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as much as federal law allowed.\par \par \uc2 The court delayed implementation of the ban for at least two weeks, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates appear to have few options to prevent it from taking effect. If the ban becomes enforceable, the state will have one of the nation's strictest limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , similar to laws in deep-red states such as Oklahoma and Texas.\par \par \uc2 Presumptive Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has sought to pivot away from the issue as he runs to recapture the White House, as have other Republican candidates. But the Arizona decision adds to a string of legal developments that have kept \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the center of the national political debate, potentially boosting Democrats who have leveraged the issue for gains across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 "It nationalizes the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue once again," said Democratic strategist Paul Begala. "These cases just keep coming."\par \par \uc2 The Florida Supreme Court last week issued a ruling that allows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/florida-abortion-ballot-measure-supreme-court-a3340feb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after six weeks of pregnancy }}}\uc2  to take effect in the coming weeks and cleared a ballot measure that could reinstate broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in that state. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups are trying to get similar measures on the ballot in at least half-a-dozen states\u8212\'20\'14including Arizona.\par \par \uc2 President Biden has campaigned on a promise to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and has assailed Trump, who as president appointed three Supreme Court justices who were part of the majority that overruled Roe. "This ruling is a result of the extreme agenda of Republican elected officials who are committed to ripping away women's freedom," Biden said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Trump spokeswoman Karoline Leavitt said: "President Trump could not have been more clear. These are decisions for people of each state to make."\par \par \uc2 The ruling puts Trump under additional pressure as he tries to avoid commentary on some of his own party's efforts. On Monday, he skirted taking a position on whether to support federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and said the issue was best left with the states.\par \par \uc2 Trump's team has sought to focus on issues such as immigration and the economy, where voters favor him over Biden. The question is where voters will focus their attention. Republican strategist Alex Conant said: "I can't recall an election where the two campaigns are going to be talking about such wildly different issues."\par \par \uc2 It is unclear when or whether the Arizona ban will ultimately be enforced. State Attorney General Kris Mayes, a Democrat, said Tuesday that women and doctors won't be prosecuted while she holds office, under an order from the Democratic governor that gives her office authority over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related prosecutions. Antiabortion groups have said they think local prosecutors could still pursue charges against doctors.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Arizona said it plans to continue providing abortions for a handful of weeks, but providers said they would have to weigh the legal risk of continuing to do so if the ban takes effect.\par \par \uc2 The measure that could be on on Arizona's ballot in November would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access through fetal viability, or more than halfway through a typical pregnancy. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups already have collected more than 500,000 signatures, putting the measure on track to clear the threshold required to appear on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is a longtime GOP bastion that has been electing Democrats in recent years. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a potent issue in the 2022 midterm elections, when Democrats won all major statewide offices and performed better than expected across the country.\par \par \uc2 November's election will see many competitive races in the state, meaning Arizona voters could decide which party controls the White House and both chambers of Congress. Republicans have worried that an outright ban would push winnable voters into the Democratic column.\par \par \uc2 Biden narrowly won Arizona in 2020 but is trailing Trump in most surveys this year, including in a Wall Street Journal poll from March. The poll found that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a rare issue in which voters in seven battleground states favored Biden over Trump.\par \par \uc2 Arizona was one of a handful of states that never formally repealed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that had been on their books before the 1973 Roe decision that recognized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide for nearly 50 years. When the Supreme Court overturned Roe, the old bans once again became potentially enforceable.\par \par \uc2 "Arizona's pro-life law has protected unborn children for over 100 years, and the people of Arizona, through their elected representatives, have repeatedly affirmed that law," said Jake Warner, an attorney with the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a conservative legal group that argued in favor of allowing the law to take effect.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240409ek49004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
