\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Trump Says States Should Chart Their Own Paths on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; Former president had floated the idea of a 15- or 16-week ban\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Leary, Catherine Lucey and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,132 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2024\par 00:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sidestepped a position on national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions Monday, betting that the move would be his best chance to neutralize Democrats' most animating issue and keep his rematch with President Biden focused on immigration and the economy.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee, gave his long-awaited stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in a video released by the campaign. He didn't mention the number of weeks at which he thought the procedure should be banned, instead saying that what states decide should be respected.\par \par \uc2 "Many states will be different," Trump said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/users/realDonaldTrump/statuses/112235238031827342"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the video}}}\uc2 . "At the end of the day, this is all about the will of the people." He also sought to portray Democrats as extreme on the issue, though that argument has failed to move voters in recent elections.\par \par \uc2 His remarks underscored how fraught the issue is for Republicans. The GOP has repeatedly lost on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the polls since the 2022 Supreme Court ruling in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization that overturned the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision, eliminating federal protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 "Always go by your heart," said Trump, adding: "but we must win." He has previously expressed concern about the weight of the issue on Republicans while issuing messages aimed at both sides.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State laws}}}\uc2  now run the gamut on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some places have virtually no access to the procedure except in the most dire of medical emergencies, while other places have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access protected until the final weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "I don't know that anything will take the attention off the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue given some of the extremely restrictive bills that have been passed," said GOP consultant Whit Ayres, who called Trump's position a politically smart one. "But it is the most likely strategy to allow the focus on other issues."\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot in states such as Florida and possibly Arizona this fall, the issue was already going to be a factor. Whether Trump would back a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has gained more attention as he recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-nears-decision-on-abortion-stance-aims-to-make-both-sides-happy-433b0904?st=b5poin55s5e57tg&reflink=desktopwebshare_permalink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  support for one at 15 or 16 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Still, his strategy carries risks. Trump has upset some religious conservatives who had wanted him to promote a national ban. At the same time, his taking credit for appointing three conservative justices to the court was a gift to Democrats eager to cast him as responsible for the upheaval across the country and as supportive of stricter bans in some states.\par \par \uc2 While some Republicans view 15 weeks as an acceptable middle ground, a failed attempt at such a ban in Virginia last year showed the limits of the approach. Trump, who had previously said states should decide, reiterated Monday he believes in exceptions for rape and incest and to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Before he ran for president in 2016, Trump had supported broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access before taking a more conservative stance. "I'm pro-life, and I was originally pro-choice," he said during that campaign. "I have evolved."\par \par \uc2 Biden on Monday seized on Trump's comments, saying that his predecessor is "responsible for creating the cruelty and the chaos that has enveloped America since the Dobbs decision."\par \par \uc2 Following the Supreme Court ruling overturning Roe, Biden and Democrats have made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a rallying cry and voters have opposed restrictions in numerous off-year elections.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the few bright spots for Democrats as Trump leads Biden in many national and swing state polls. In a recent Wall Street Journal poll of seven swing states, Trump held double-digit leads in every state when voters were asked who can best handle the economy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/consumers/whats-wrong-with-the-economy-its-you-not-the-data-cfa911e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation}}}\uc2  and immigration. But on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Biden was viewed as the preferable candidate, and some said it was the issue that would decide who they supported. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
