\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the antiabortion group Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, said Trump was ceding the national debate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Democrats. PHOTO: Stephen Voss for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Democrats argued that Trump could still sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president, with Biden saying that if Republicans sent one to him, "Trump will sign it into law." The Trump campaign didn't respond to a request for comment on that possibility or other possible measures he could take. Trump could, for example, choose as president to enforce the Comstock Act, an obscure 1873 law that could be used to ban mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and more.\par \par \uc2 Biden's campaign also released a television ad Monday featuring a Texas woman who says she nearly died when she couldn't receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and went into septic shock. Amanda Zurawski, who has challenged the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, is shown sobbing before the screen goes black and the words "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this" appear.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the antiabortion group Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, expressed disappointment in Trump's position Monday, saying it ceded the national debate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Democrats. "We had hoped and expected for something different. We respectfully disagree with him. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a states' rights question," she said. Dannenfelser added that the group would oppose Biden and Democrats in the general election.\par \par \uc2 Some advisers close to Trump said they feel like such criticism helps the former president appeal to more centrist voters.\par \par \uc2 Other Republicans including former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who helped Trump win over social conservatives, weren't happy, either. Pence called it a "slap in the face" to those who voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R, S.C.) said on X that he respectfully disagreed with Trump's statement that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a states' rights issue, drawing stinging rebukes from the former president on his own social-media platform. "I blame myself for \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , because the only reason he won in the Great State of South Carolina is because I Endorsed him!" Trump wrote in one post on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Still, failing to commit to a national ban is unlikely to cost Trump seriously with the antiabortion movement, which already credits him with helping overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life of America, said she thought Democrats would have used whatever limit Trump chose to paint him as extreme. "He didn't fall for the bait," she said. "This still shows our work is cut out for us when it comes to educating him that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a federal issue."\par \par \uc2 Write to Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240408ek48002p9\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
