\par\par \uc2 Future View\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 's Influence on the 2024 Election; Students debate the issue's impact, as Trump says it's a state issue and Arizona's Supreme Court upholds its 1864 ban.\b0\par\par\uc2 845 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2024\par 22:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Editor's note: In this  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/news/types/future-view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Future View }}}\uc2 , students discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the election. Next week we'll ask, "The \uc2 National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics\uc2  approved on April 8 a policy that will allow athletes to participate in women's sports only if they were born female and have not begun hormone therapy. The policy will also allow all athletes to participate in male sports. Is this the right decision? Why or why not?" Students should  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://futureview.wsj.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 click here }}}\uc2  to submit opinions of fewer than 250 words by April 15. The best responses will be published Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 Rework the Messaging\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a critical issue on the ballot this year, as it was during the midterm elections two years ago. Many in the pro-life movement and the Republican Party have made it clear that they intend to implement as strict an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as possible, which isn't in line with the average American voter. Democrats have seized this opportunity to highlight the extreme views espoused by some on the right, including an aversion to exceptions in case of rape, the desire to ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and restrictions on travel to other states for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Whichever party has more compelling messaging on this issue will benefit politically. So far, it seems that Democrats are ahead. Given that such states as Kentucky and Ohio, both ruby red, voted against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, there's a case to be made that many Republicans and right-leaning independents are willing to turn out for a pro-choice referendum.\par \par \uc2 This November, expect ardently pro-life congressional and senatorial candidates to perform worse than expected in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot, and expect the same for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he doesn't take a moderate stance on the issue. This might explain why he recently said the issue should be left to the states. Not a good sign for the close race predicted by most polls.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14David Cheng, \uc2 University of California, Berkeley\uc2 , political science\par \par \uc2 We Have Other Things to Worry About\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be an issue on the ballot this November, but it won't be the most critical one. Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, Republicans have underperformed in state and federal elections. If Republicans continue to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they have, by pushing for blanket bans, then they will continue to lose. If Mr. Trump leads a charge against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Republicans will lose.\par \par \uc2 But according to a Quinnipiac poll, among Republicans, the top issue is immigration, followed by the economy. Among Democrats, the top issue is preserving democracy, followed by climate change and gun violence. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't rank in the double digits for either party.\par \par \uc2 The economy will likely be the issue that swings independent voters. With rent and food prices rising across the country and wages lagging behind, many Americans are struggling financially. Independent voters care about who will make their day-to-day life better.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Bren Routly, \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2 , law\par \par \uc2 Watch Out for the Gen Z Vote\par \par \uc2 A March poll revealed that 1 in 6 women ages 18 to 49 considers \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a pivotal factor when choosing a presidential candidate this coming election. Many who care most about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws being overturned are the younger generation. Gen Z activists are influencing the debate on social-media platforms and are marching in protests. Seventy-four percent of adults under 30 say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal, according to \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the 2022 midterm elections, Gen Z voted at a higher rate than previous generations had with more than 28% turnout, outpacing millennials and Gen X when they were young. It's also higher than baby boomers' 27.9% turnout in the midterm election of 1974. Younger generations today are more involved in politics, and their votes could make a difference in 2024. But this will only influence the presidential election's outcome if they keep up the momentum and vote come November.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14McKenna Randall, \uc2 Baylor University\uc2 , marketing and management\par \par \uc2 It's a Loser for the GOP\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a significant issue in the coming presidential race. As shown in every election since the Dobbs decision, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a motivator for the electorate. Voters have roundly rejected both measures that restrict abortions and antiabortion candidates up and down the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion positions are hurting candidates. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , a Democrat, won the governorship in Kentucky in a contest that focused intensely on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Democratic state legislators in Virginia swept the state House and Senate, focusing on the threat a Republican legislature posed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Democrats will continue to make the issue salient to voters, a position that has resulted in many victories thus far. Republicans running on antiabortion platforms will continue to alienate voters and lose elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Ignatius Fitzgerald, St. Olaf College, history and economics\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://futureview.wsj.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here }}}\uc2  to submit a response to next week's Future View.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240409ek4900691\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
