\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden, Trump and the 2024 Election: What to Know; A 2020 rematch looms in an unprecedented election\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alyssa Lukpat \par \uc2 995 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2024\par 18:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Two unpopular candidates are set to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-trump-general-election-rematch-cef0ac3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 face each other again  }}}\uc2  in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 President Biden is poised to reclaim the Democratic nomination, and the Republican field has shrunk to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The historic rematch has two of the oldest presidential candidates in U.S. history essentially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/why-bidens-agenda-is-filled-with-old-ideas-7aeeca61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running as incumbents  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14both widely disliked.\par \par \uc2 The election, which culminates on Nov. 5, is taking place amid tensions over the economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , war and the state of U.S. democracy.\par \par \uc2 Here is our guide to the race.\par \par \uc2 * Who is running for president in 2024?\par \par \uc2 * Could third-party challengers affect the election?\par \par \uc2 * Will Trump be on the ballot?\par \par \uc2 * Who are the swing voters?\par \par \uc2 * What are the key dates in the 2024 election?\par \par \uc2 * What are the biggest issues?\par \par \uc2 * What are the key states to watch?\par \par \uc2 * What role does the Electoral College play?\par \par \uc2 Who is running for president in 2024?\par \par \uc2 The Democrat: Despite concerns about Biden's age\u8212\'20\'14at 81 years old, he is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-eclipse-reagan-as-oldest-president-as-washington-leadership-ages-11610809201?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oldest president  }}}\uc2  in U.S. history\u8212\'20\'14he has cruised toward the nomination.\par \par \uc2 The Republican: The GOP field dwindled from more than a dozen to just Trump, who is 77. Former South Carolina Gov. \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , his last challenger, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/nikki-haley-drops-out-2024-presidential-election-625277ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended her campaign  }}}\uc2  in March following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-super-tuesday-wins-will-add-pressure-on-haley-to-drop-out-35b013b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poor showing  }}}\uc2  on Super Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Trump retains his grip on the electorate while facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/a-guide-to-donald-trumps-legal-perils-b9b64891"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal charges  }}}\uc2 , including for his efforts to overturn his 2020 election loss. He has denied wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 For more information on who is running for president, check out The Wall Street Journal's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/whos-running-for-president-in-2024-adb754e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guide to the candidates  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Could third-party challengers affect the election?\par \par \uc2 Independent candidates such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/voters-want-something-different-is-it-rfk-jr-14f434fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.  }}}\uc2 , a lawyer who has pushed antivaccine conspiracy theories, have little support in polls but could peel off votes, including in critical swing states.\par \par \uc2 Will Trump be on the ballot?\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-ruling-trump-ballot-colorado-092852fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court ruling  }}}\uc2  in March ended the debate over whether Trump would be excluded from the ballot. The justices decided Colorado couldn't disqualify him based on his actions on Jan. 6, 2021, which also ended similar ballot challenges in other states.\par \par \uc2 Who are the swing voters?\par \par \uc2 Biden is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-biden-poll-swing-states-ad594acb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggling to connect  }}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/president-joe-biden-old-stories-7b8e9198"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 young people  }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/black-voters-show-signs-of-slipping-away-from-biden-in-2024-69ae78b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some voters of color  }}}\uc2 , and some Democratic voters have criticized his support for Israel in its war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Trump has tired many voters with his claims about the 2020 election and a string of court cases.\par \par \uc2 Key demographic groups that help decide elections include suburban women who have drawn closer to Democrats since the fall of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 ; Black voters, who can help power Democratic wins; and Latino voters, with whom Republicans have made inroads.\par \par \uc2 What are the key dates in the 2024 election?\par \par \uc2 July 15-18: Republican National Convention in Milwaukee\par \par \uc2 Aug. 19-22: Democratic National Convention in Chicago\par \par \uc2 Nov. 5: Election Day\par \par \uc2 Jan. 20, 2025: Inauguration Day\par \par \uc2 What are the biggest issues?\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-dobbs-year-after-roe-support-politics-d1ef5a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a winning issue for Democrats  }}}\uc2  since the Supreme Court last year overturned Roe v. Wade, shifting the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to the states. Trump in April said decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/abortion-donald-trump-2024-election-fe641cc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be left to states  }}}\uc2 . He had previously floated the idea of a 15- or 16-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Democracy\par \par \uc2 Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-to-mark-jan-6-by-putting-threats-to-democracy-at-center-of-2024-message-66fce44c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 framed this election  }}}\uc2  as a watershed moment for American democracy, saying Trump, who spread false claims about election fraud and played down the Jan. 6 attack on the Capitol, could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-say-in-prime-time-address-democracy-is-at-stake-in-midterm-elections-11662048825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threaten the country's future  }}}\uc2  should he go back to the White House. Trump said Biden is "fear mongering."\par \par \uc2 Economy\par \par \uc2 While views of the economy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/gdp-us-economy-fourth-quarter-2023-9fc372f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are improving  }}}\uc2 , voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/voters-are-more-upbeat-on-economy-but-biden-gets-little-benefit-wsj-poll-shows-8e608db8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largely don't credit Biden  }}}\uc2  for his stewardship and say they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/economy-inflation-consumer-spending-unemployment-e6856381"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remain anxious  }}}\uc2  about high prices.\par \par \uc2 Immigration\par \par \uc2 Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-expands-title-42-migrant-expulsions-to-more-countries-11672934432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaned on Trump-era policies  }}}\uc2  to try to deter migrants but has also opened new pathways to allow migrants to enter the country legally with work permits. He has slowed arrests and deportations of longtime immigrants to concentrate on deporting criminals.\par \par \uc2 Trump has vowed to be a dictator just on "Day 1," his first day in office, in part to close the border. He has promised the largest-ever deportation of migrants who are in the country illegally, vowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/why-trumps-drastic-plan-to-slash-the-government-could-succeed-6828ccbe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to deny citizenship  }}}\uc2  to tens of thousands of people born in the U.S. and used incendiary rhetoric, such as saying people in the U.S. illegally are "poisoning the blood of our country."\par \par \uc2 Foreign Policy\par \par \uc2 Israel's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/a-guide-to-the-middle-easts-growing-conflicts-in-six-maps-2ea0c0da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight against Hamas  }}}\uc2  and the war in Ukraine are competing for the president's time with domestic issues U.S. voters care about most. The Biden administration and Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/u-s-sends-israel-2-000-pound-bunker-buster-bombs-for-gaza-war-82898638"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back Israel  }}}\uc2 . Biden, under pressure to address the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/tiny-gaza-is-home-to-most-of-the-worlds-hungriest-people-df62eeda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing humanitarian crisis  }}}\uc2  in Gaza, is also trying to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/biden-to-announce-creation-of-gaza-port-to-receive-aid-5fc131b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 direct more aid to the enclave  }}}\uc2 . On Ukraine, Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/how-trump-turned-conservatives-against-helping-ukraine-d9f75b3b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to commit  }}}\uc2  to continuing Biden's effort to help counter Russia.\par \par \uc2 What are the key states to watch?\par \par \uc2 The candidates are expected to focus on the battleground states of Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, which swung to Biden in 2020 from Trump in 2016. North Carolina and Nevada have been close in recent elections and will also be heavily contested.\par \par \uc2 What role does the Electoral College play?\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/meet-the-electoral-college-americas-most-important-voters-11607868000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Electoral College  }}}\uc2  hands outsize power to voters in smaller states. The system assigns a certain amount of delegates to each state based on population, but because each state gets at least three electors, smaller states get more sway.\par \par \uc2 Wyoming, with a population of about 580,000 people, has three electoral votes, meaning each elector potentially represents roughly 193,300 people. In California, which has approximately 39 million people and 54 electoral votes, each elector represents about 723,000 people.\par \par \uc2 Biden in 2020 won the popular vote by seven million votes and the Electoral College by a count of 306 to Trump's 232.\par \par \uc2 This article may be periodically updated.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Calfas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alyssa Lukpat at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alyssa.lukpat@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alyssa.lukpat@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240408ek48003ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
