\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Florida  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rulings to Keep Issue Front and Center in November; Democrats seek to capitalize on state's six-week ban\u8212\'20\'14and a ballot measure that could undo it\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,115 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par 19:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A pair of decisions by the Florida Supreme Court are poised to help Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/bidens-first-2024-campaign-rally-to-promote-abortion-rights-c89e1fa7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keep \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2  top of mind for voters heading into November, when the party will try to hold on to the White House, its narrow Senate majority and retake the House.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/florida-abortion-ballot-measure-supreme-court-a3340feb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the state's highest court  }}}\uc2  issued a ruling that clears the way for a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy to take effect next month. In a separate decision, the state court approved a ballot measure that, if successful this fall, would undo that ruling and restore the broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access the state had before the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  issued a ruling that clears the way for a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy to take effect next month. In a separate decision, the state court approved a ballot measure that, if successful this fall, would undo that ruling and restore the broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access the state had before the\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Florida is not considered one of the top presidential battleground states this fall, but it does have a Senate race and a handful of congressional races that could become competitive. And it will give Democrats nationally a chance to elevate an issue where they have a political advantage over Republicans, who have hoped to keep the public focused on the economy, immigration and President Biden's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-has-more-than-an-age-problem-voters-dont-see-him-as-presidential-f5212415"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 general fitness for office  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "People see this as a positive reason to go out and vote, and it gives energy to people," said Matt Grodsky, a Democratic strategist based in Arizona, a top political battleground where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-is-the-next-abortion-battleground-afae13a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to be a major issue.  }}}\par \par \uc2 Since Roe fell, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates have won {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-election-ballot-2024-3c50731d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven straight referendum victories  }}}\uc2 . And Democratic candidates for governor, Congress and state legislative contests have successfully campaigned in opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Grodsky said support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access crosses party lines, but Democrats would still need to campaign hard to convince voters that Democratic candidates would be the ones to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Biden has fallen behind former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in most polls, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/voters-are-more-upbeat-on-economy-but-biden-gets-little-benefit-wsj-poll-shows-8e608db8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Wall Street Journal poll  }}}\uc2  from February, in their rematch later this year. But that same poll, in which voters held a dim view of his stewardship of the economy and expressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/bidens-age-back-in-spotlight-after-special-counsel-report-verbal-flubs-159c77f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerns about his age  }}}\uc2 , found 60% of voters said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 After the twin rulings Monday, Julie Chavez Rodriguez, the campaign manager for Biden's campaign, said in a memo that investing in Florida is a potential pathway to Biden's re-election, without detailing how it would spend there. She said the GOP "attacks on reproductive freedom will help mobilize and expand the electorate in the state."\par \par \uc2 The campaign released a television ad airing in battleground states and on national cable tying Trump to the Roe decision. Biden, in the ads, says he is running "to make Roe v. Wade the law of the land again, so women have a federal guarantee to the right to choose."\par \par \uc2 Trump has urged Republicans to take a less restrictive approach after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, which passed in the aftermath of the overturning of Roe, helped field Democratic wins. He recently said he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-nears-decision-on-abortion-stance-aims-to-make-both-sides-happy-433b0904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearing a decision  }}}\uc2  on a stance on federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits that he hopes will be seen as a middle ground. At the same time, he has taken credit for nominating the conservative Supreme Court justices who eliminated the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "President Trump supports preserving life but has also made clear that he supports states' rights," Brian Hughes, a Trump campaign senior adviser, said in a statement after the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Early polling has shown that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unfporl.org/uploads/1/4/4/5/144559024/unf_fall23_statewide.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 60% of Floridians support the amendment  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14enough to clear the threshold for amending the state's constitution. The ballot measure would render the six-week ban unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 Florida joins a group of at least half-a-dozen states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights proponents are trying to get measures on the ballot that would expand or protect access to the procedure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/arizona-is-the-next-abortion-battleground-afae13a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Arizona  }}}\uc2  and Nevada which are both major presidential and Senate battlegrounds and have competitive House races. Montana, which has one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/montana-jon-tester-senate-race-3a41243b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most competitive Senate races  }}}\uc2  in the country, could also see such a measure.\par \par \uc2 Once seen as a political battleground, Florida has moved away from Democrats. Trump won the state by 3 percentage points in 2020, but Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a Republican, won his re-election by 19 percentage points in 2022, the same year many other Democrats had victories around the country. Democrats see Florida's Senate seat as one of their few pickup opportunities on a national map that favors Republicans, though political observers say Republican Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  has a clear edge.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans have acknowledged the issue has benefited Democrats and urged their party to change the way they talk about it.\par \par \uc2 We need to "recognize the political liability of bans and accept the idea of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits because people are going to be much more open to that," Republican strategist Alice Stewart said. She urged Republicans to support some access to the procedure\u8212\'20\'14she said restricting abortions after 15 weeks was reasonable\u8212\'20\'14with exceptions for rape, incest and the life of the mother. She said that would allow Republicans the opportunity to paint Democrats as too extreme on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have in recent weeks also been on the defensive regarding their views on in vitro fertilization, after the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/alabama-supreme-court-embryo-ivf-uncertainty-88cf2146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled in February  }}}\uc2  that frozen embryos can be legally considered children, raising concerns about the future of fertility treatments in that state.\par \par \uc2 After the court ruling in Alabama, the state's GOP-led legislature passed a law to shield providers from prosecution if embryos are destroyed during IVF treatments. Still, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/democrats-embrace-ivf-in-fight-to-regain-house-in-2024-1fdacc87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have begun running on IVF  }}}\uc2  nationwide, working to tie that issue and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  together by highlighting the stance held by many Republicans that life begins at conception.\par \par \uc2 Proponents of the Florida ballot measure say they have raised some $18 million to get the measure on the ballot and support its approval by voters. Antiabortion groups, meanwhile, have been sharpening their tactics after a series of defeats and plan to argue the measure would allow virtually unlimited access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Ken Thomas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240402ek42001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
