\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Florida Supreme Court Allows Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban but Permits Vote on Expanding Access; The decision puts  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  front and center in the state in a presidential election year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 899 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 April 2024\par 21:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Florida Supreme Court ruled Monday that the state's ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy may take effect, but the justices also cleared the way for voters to greatly expand the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 The court's decisions turn up the heat significantly in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/florida-abortion-rulings-to-keep-issue-front-and-center-in-november-1168511c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the battle over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in Florida, teeing up what could be this year's most fiercely contested fight over the procedure.\par \par \uc2 In a 4-3 decision, the court approved the language for a ballot measure that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state through fetal viability, or more than halfway through a typical pregnancy. If passed, the measure would effectively restore to Floridians protections that were afforded to women nationwide under the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision, which the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  struck down in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 In a 6-1 decision, the court also ruled that a privacy provision of the state's constitution doesn't protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a decision that would allow a law that passed last spring banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy to take effect in 30 days, in advance of the November referendum.\par \par \uc2 Currently \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in Florida through 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The court's decision ensures that the stakes of the referendum fight won't be abstract for Floridians. The six-week ban will significantly curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in a state that had been one of the last slivers of accessibility in the South. Florida is one of the top states in the country in terms of the number of abortions it sees. It has also experienced one of the largest increases in abortions over the last two years as women from Texas, Louisiana, Georgia and elsewhere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have come there seeking the procedure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The measure also puts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  front and center in the state in a presidential election year. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has driven turnout and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-supporters-rack-up-victories-putting-gop-in-bind-for-2024-4bec7b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boosted Democrats' electoral prospects in other states.}}}\uc2  Florida Democrats are hopeful that putting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure on the ballot could make the presidential race and some congressional races at least somewhat more competitive in a state that has trended Republican in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The state's attorney general, \uc2 Ashley Moody\uc2 , a Republican, brought the challenge to the measure. \uc2 Moody\uc2  argued that the summary of the ballot measure to be provided to voters vastly understated its "sweeping" scope by failing to clearly define terms such as healthcare provider and viability. Proponents of the measure responded that these are common-sense terms widely understood by voters.\par \par \uc2 The Florida Supreme Court justices ruled that the meaning of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measure, which protects a right to the procedure until fetal viability, was sufficiently clear. The measure allows healthcare providers to determine whether a fetus is considered viable, which falls around 23 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Getting a measure on the ballot in Florida was an expensive gamble fraught with hurdles for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups. But it was seen as worthwhile given the state's practical and political significance. Supporters needed to gather some 900,000 signatures spread out over at least half of Florida's congressional districts.\par \par \uc2 "Now, more than ever, we must double down on our efforts to ensure our message reaches every corner of the state," said Anna Hochkammer, executive director of Florida Women's Freedom Coalition, one of the group's pushing for the ballot measure, in reaction to Monday's decision.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What is your view of the ruling by Florida's Supreme Court? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The state Supreme Court, which is made up entirely of justices appointed by Republican governors, also had the authority to strike the measure from the ballot if the justices decided it was unclear.\par \par \uc2 Proponents of the ballot measure now face what is likely to be a fierce and costly fight. Early polling has shown that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unfporl.org/uploads/1/4/4/5/144559024/unf_fall23_statewide.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 60% of Floridians support the amendment}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14enough to clear the threshold for amending the state's constitution. The ballot measure would render the six-week ban unconstitutional.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-election-ballot-2024-3c50731d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are pursuing ballot measures}}}\uc2  in a host of other politically important states, including Arizona, Nevada, Colorado and Nebraska, and Democrats are hopeful that could give them a boost with groups including independent voters and suburban women.\par \par \uc2 The court's decision that the privacy provision in the state's constitution doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the most important legal victories for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Legally \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents had faced an uphill battle in trying to enact a six-week ban because Florida had among the strongest constitutional protections for the procedure in the country. Voters in 1980 had inserted an explicit privacy protection into the state's constitution that the Florida Supreme Court later ruled encompassed a "woman's decision of whether or not to continue her pregnancy."\par \par \uc2 John Stemberger, president of Liberty Counsel Action, a conservative law firm, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are bracing to defend the decision from the ballot initiative that could essentially cancel it out.\par \par \uc2 "I think we're going to be able to defeat this at the ballot," Stemberger said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240402ek41001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
