\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Is VP Contender Kristi Noem Ready for Prime Time? South Dakota governor on Trump's shortlist faces scrutiny for everything from  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  policy to her new smile\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kristina Peterson \par \uc2 1,218 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par 14:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14As the chances that former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will pick South Dakota GOP Gov. \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  as his running mate are growing, so too is scrutiny over everything from her policy positions to her new teeth.\par \par \uc2 Her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Her opposition to TikTok. And most puzzling to many, her decision earlier this month to post a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C4ZiRjcNOWW/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lengthy video on Instagram  }}}\uc2  praising a cosmetic dentistry practice in Texas for fixing her teeth.\par \par \uc2 Noem, 52, has declined to say whether she paid for her own dental work, raising questions about whether she filmed the testimonial in exchange for services.\par \par \uc2 "Participating in an ethically dubious commercial is just odd," said Brendan Buck, who served as spokesman for former House Speaker \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2  (R., Wis.) when he was the 2012 GOP vice presidential nominee. For that role, "are you picking a person who is going to thoughtfully advance and amplify your message or are you picking somebody who is going to become a distraction? This felt like a distraction," Buck said.\par \par \uc2 Noem spokesman Ian Fury criticized the focus on her controversies rather than her policy accomplishments, adding: "Much like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Governor Noem has never been a Washington, D.C., insider."\par \par \uc2 Trump, who met one-on-one with Noem at Mar-a-Lago in late February, has enthusiastically talked her up as a possible running mate in recent discussions, according to people familiar with the talks. She appeared on stage with him at a rally in Ohio earlier this month, wearing a "Make America Great Again" hat and praising his leadership.\par \par \uc2 "You're not allowed to say she's beautiful, so I'm not going to say that," Trump said after her remarks.\par \par \uc2 But Trump's advisers are hoping to find a running mate who could help win over voters wary of hard-line \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, an issue that helped fuel Democratic wins in the 2022 midterms after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 . That could be a mark against Noem in the Trump campaign's calculations.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prohibited in South Dakota, except to save the mother's life. Earlier this month, Noem signed into law a bill allowing people to rescind signatures from petitions for ballot measures. That bill is seen by opponents as an effort to siphon support for a measure aimed at restoring some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state.\par \par \uc2 Supporters have gathered about 55,000 signatures for the proposed amendment to the state constitution, which would largely restore South Dakotans' ability to get abortions in the first and second trimesters. The measure needs around 35,000 signatures to qualify for the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Noem is also at odds with Trump's recent criticism of legislation passed by the U.S. House that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/tiktok-bill-ban-house-vote-af4d0800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would ban TikTok  }}}\uc2  unless its Beijing-based parent company divests its U.S. operations. Under Noem, South Dakota in late 2022 banned TikTok on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-dakota-bans-tiktok-surveillance-beijing-ccp-government-devices-data-farm-food-security-app-noem-11670277776"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state government-owned or leased devices  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And while Noem is a vigorous cheerleader for Trump's immigration and tax policies, she hasn't endorsed some other tenets of his agenda. At a House Agriculture Committee hearing last week, she sidestepped a question about Trump's plans to levy tariffs on U.S. imports, which could hurt U.S. farmers were they to spark a trade battle.\par \par \uc2 "I think that is a proposal that people are still looking at," Noem said.\par \par \uc2 The 1990 South Dakota "Snow Queen," Noem grew up working on her parents' farm and cattle ranch in the northeastern part of the state. She became the general manager of the farm's business operations after her father died in a grain-bin accident when she was 22 and eight-months pregnant with the first of her three children.\par \par \uc2 "She's a smart, tough farm kid," said state Sen. Lee Schoenbeck, a Republican who at times clashed with Noem as governor. "This isn't somebody that's had a Barbie doll, easy way through life."\par \par \uc2 Noem served in the South Dakota Legislature before being elected to the U.S. House in 2010. In Washington, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/some-congresswomen-are-bunking-at-the-office-1407286500"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slept in her House office  }}}\uc2  and dressed down her own GOP leaders when a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424127887323393804578559910161544792"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 version of the farm bill  }}}\uc2 , which sets agricultural policy, failed in 2013. After four terms in Congress, she was elected governor of South Dakota in 2018 and re-elected in 2022.\par \par \uc2 She drew national attention for her more hands-off approach during the Covid-19 pandemic, refusing to institute a mask mandate and reopening schools earlier than many other states\u8212\'20\'14moves that were popular in conservative South Dakota. But she also later tangled with the GOP-controlled legislature, which didn't embrace her 2022 campaign pledge to eliminate the state's 4.5% sales tax on groceries.\par \par \uc2 In late 2021, the state legislature's GOP-controlled Government Operations and Audit Committee found that one of Noem's daughters was given preferential treatment by the state labor and regulation department after she didn't initially qualify for her state-certified real estate appraiser's license. A spokesman for Noem has said that she didn't seek special treatment for her daughter and that she didn't receive any.\par \par \uc2 Most recently, Noem has drawn skepticism over her decision to post a five-minute video on March 11 detailing her experience getting her teeth fixed at SmileTexas, a cosmetic dentistry practice in Sugar Land, Texas. Noem said her front teeth were kicked out while riding her bike with her children years ago.\par \par \uc2 "The team here was remarkable and finally gave me a smile that I can be proud of," she said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post isn't labeled as an advertisement, and Noem has refused to answer questions about whether she paid for her own dental work. Noem likely didn't violate any legal statutes, but promoting a specific business could be considered conduct unbecoming of a public official, said Michael Card, professor emeritus of political science at the \uc2 University of South Dakota\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What would \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  bring to the ticket if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were to choose her as his running mate? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "That's what I do all the time for a lot of businesses, so it's silliness," she said when asked about the post recently. Travelers United, a consumer travel nonprofit, sued Noem, alleging that she advertised a service without disclosing her financial connection to the business.\par \par \uc2 Some Democratic state legislators have indicated they would press for more information about Noem's compensation or use of state resources connected with the trip. And fellow Republicans have said they considered it odd for Noem to publicly boost a business not in her own state.\par \par \uc2 "It's not something that when I was governor I did, that I can recall, unless it was for a business in South Dakota," said Sen. Mike Rounds (R., S.D.), a former governor of the state.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Noem starred in a series of ads touting the state's job openings, including one in which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=omEOiTZGKdI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she dressed as a dental hygienist  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alex Leary and Suryatapa Bhattacharya contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kristina Peterson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kristina.peterson@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kristina.peterson@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240327ek3r001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
