\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 She Fought the  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill in Court. Her Husband Is a Senator. Lawyer Erin Hawley tries to persuade the Supreme Court to roll back access to mifepristone\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 976 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par 18:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley, the lawyer who argued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-arguments-abortion-pill-mifepristone-c31de31a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the case against the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill  }}}\uc2  at the Supreme Court on Tuesday, is a rising star in conservative legal circles and the lower-profile half of a young Washington power couple.\par \par \uc2 Hawley's arguments didn't appear to sway the Supreme Court justices to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/abortion-pill-case-puts-supreme-court-back-in-the-hot-seat-dec8edad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limit access to mifepristone  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hawley, an \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  lawyer in her 40s, has kept largely out of the political spotlight even as her husband, Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R., Mo.), has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hawley-faces-fierce-backlash-from-colleagues-donors-after-capitol-riot-11610150574"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polarizing national figure.  }}}\uc2  After the 2020 election, he was the first senator to say he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-senator-says-he-will-force-votes-on-bidens-win-11609348249"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would object to certifying Joe Biden's electoral-college victory  }}}\uc2 , and on the day of the vote, Jan. 6, 2021, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/jan-6-hearing-today-trump/card/josh-hawley-s-fist-pump-at-capitol-irked-police-officer-XYYtRa2lfgmCQMobCZWh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pumped his fist  }}}\uc2  at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's supporters gathered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/jan-6-key-moments-leading-up-to-the-attack-on-the-capitol-11654796246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outside the Capitol  }}}\uc2  before the riot.\par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley, by contrast, is seen by those who know her as a reluctant political spouse who has cut a low profile on the campaign trail but applied a brilliant legal mind to issues dear to Christian conservatives. That includes the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 , the 1973 case that for decades protected a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Thom Lambert, a law professor at the \uc2 University of Missouri\uc2 , where both Hawleys worked early in their careers, said Erin Hawley was in some senses the more highly regarded legal mind of the couple.\par \par \uc2 "She's been more involved in serious, hard-core legal work than he has," Lambert said. "She was the one who was getting asked by the very, very top appellate lawyers in the country to help with things."\par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley, who grew up on a ranch in New Mexico, has said her career drive grew out of her father's alcoholism and severe depression, which had her constantly striving to win his approval.\par \par \uc2 "I had, for the longest time, and still have, in many ways, a performance-based mentality. So through law school, through clerking, through working at a large law firm, sort of my go-to was just to work harder," Hawley said in a 2018 broadcast by Focus on the Family, an evangelical Christian nonprofit.\par \par \uc2 Hawley was a member of the livestock judging team at \uc2 Texas A&M University\uc2 , where she received an animal-science degree in 2002. She did a year at the \uc2 University of Texas\uc2  law school, where a professor encouraged her to transfer to Yale Law School.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  was a year behind her at Yale, but the two fell in love while clerking for Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 . "He likes to take credit for our marriage," the senator joked on stage last year at a summit of the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 , a Christian advocacy group. "We like to say to him that we're the most conservative thing he has ever done."\par \par \uc2 After law school, the Hawleys eventually moved to Columbia, Mo., where they both landed jobs at the \uc2 University of Missouri\uc2 's law school. Lambert, who was on the hiring committee, recalls that Erin Hawley was in some ways the bigger priority hire because she was willing to teach tax law, filling a need at the time.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  eventually served as Missouri attorney general and then ran successfully for the Senate. His wife told him early in their relationship that she had little interest in such a life, he recalled at the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2  event. "Well, one thing: I hate politics. I don't ever want to do that," he recounted her saying.\par \par \uc2 The couple relocated to northern Virginia after \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  entered the Senate. They have two young sons and a daughter.\par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley joined the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a conservative legal group, several years ago and has worked on some of its most prominent cases.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How successful do you think arguments in favor of restricting access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill will be? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 She was on a significantly reduced schedule with her baby daughter when she was asked to help with the Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization case. Hawley has publicly recounted that she spent one of the early meetings dealing with her screaming infant. That case would eventually lead the Supreme Court to overrule Roe v. Wade in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's hearing was the first time she had argued in front of the Supreme Court. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  sat in the gallery and watched the arguments.\par \par \uc2 Even some of the court's more conservative justices appeared skeptical about her argument for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-arguments-abortion-pill-mifepristone-c31de31a?mod=hp_lead_pos1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rolling back access to the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug nationwide.  }}}\uc2 She remained poised but also struggled to deflect many of the tough questions.\par \par \uc2 "I think she did as well as she could with a weak case," said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 . The \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  "is swinging for the fences at the moment, and that means testing how much the Court will buy cases like this one with glaring issues."\par \par \uc2 As her legal prominence has risen, Hawley has largely stayed out of the Washington political fray but not always. She was home with her newborn daughter, she said, when a group assembled outside her house to protest her husband's decision to object to the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 But despite her longtime reluctance to live in the D.C. area, she said that the experience only strengthened her resolve to stay.\par \par \uc2 "It actually made me a little angry," she said at the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2  event. "I definitely would like to go back home to Missouri, but not for that reason."\par \par \uc2 Lindsay Wise, Jess Bravin and Liz Essley Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document W