\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Appears Unlikely to Upend  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Pill Access; The case is the first major  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  issue to reach the Supreme Court after it overruled Roe v. Wade two years ago\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin and Jan Wolfe \par \uc2 1,217 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par 20:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court appeared likely to preserve access to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/abortion-pill-case-puts-supreme-court-back-in-the-hot-seat-dec8edad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone  }}}\uc2 , following arguments Tuesday in which justices suggested that protecting doctors who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't enough justification to roll back access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 Several justices, including some who voted to overrule Roe v. Wade two years ago, focused their questioning on whether the doctors and medical associations that brought the case in fact have the right to sue. Those doctors and groups don't prescribe mifepristone, don't perform abortions and have no legal obligation to help women end unwanted pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 "Just to confirm," said Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , "under federal law, no doctors can be forced against their consciences to perform or assist in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , correct?"\par \par \uc2 "Yes," answered U.S. Solicitor General \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , who argued on behalf of the Biden administration. "We think that federal conscience protections provide broad coverage here."\par \par \uc2 The case is the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue to reach the Supreme Court after it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  two years ago, rescinding women's constitutional right to end unwanted pregnancies before fetal viability the justices had recognized in 1973.\par \par \uc2 While the 2022 decision made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation largely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/florida-abortion-rulings-to-keep-issue-front-and-center-in-november-1168511c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a matter of state law  }}}\uc2 , Tuesday's case has the potential to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrict access to medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , the most common form of the procedure, even in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case was brought by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a Christian conservative group that helped overturn Roe, on behalf of doctors and medical associations that oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and long have fought to reduce {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/supreme-court-abortion-pill-ruling-access-9a5597e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the availability of mifepristone  }}}\uc2 . Because pills can be sent through the mail and self-administered, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 antiabortion groups fear mifepristone  }}}\uc2  can help women flout \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in states that have outlawed the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley, a lawyer for the organization, won a lower-court ruling reimposing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/erin-hawley-abortion-pill-supreme-court-03c14274"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictions on mifepristone  }}}\uc2  that had been in place from 2000, when the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  first approved the drug, to 2016, when the agency said research demonstrated the rules could safely be relaxed. The order\u8212\'20\'14on hold while the Supreme Court appeal is pending\u8212\'20\'14would again require women to make three in-person visits to obtain a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, however, she faced a stream of skeptical questioning from the justices.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  questioned why the case should affect anyone other than the doctors involved.\par \par \uc2 "This case seems like a prime example of turning what could be a small lawsuit into a nationwide legislative assembly on an \uc2 FDA\uc2  rule," Gorsuch said.\par \par \uc2 Hawley said it would be impracticable to limit a court order to protecting the individual plaintiffs. The unpredictable nature of emergency room work, she argued, means the doctors still would risk encountering a mifepristone patient.\par \par \uc2 Hawley's husband, Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R., Mo.), observed the argument from the visitors gallery, as did New York Attorney General Letitia James, who filed a brief backing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  on behalf of some two dozen states and the District of Columbia.\par \par \uc2 Even if the court found the doctors had legal standing to sue, Prelogar said, there was no basis to second guess the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's scientific judgment that mifepristone could safely be dispensed the same way other prescription drugs are: By remote doctor's appointment with delivery from a mail-order pharmacy or pickup at a drugstore such as CVS or \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The agency relied on dozens of studies involving tens of thousands of women," she said. Allowing the suit to prevail "would severely disrupt the federal system for developing and approving drugs, harming the agency and the pharmaceutical industry," she said.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , who wrote the 2022 opinion rescinding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, questioned whether the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was entitled to such deference.\par \par \uc2 "You think the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's infallible?" he asked Jessica Ellsworth, an attorney for mifepristone manufacturer Danco Laboratories. "Has the \uc2 FDA\uc2  ever approved a drug and then pulled it" after discovering safety problems? he said.\par \par \uc2 Ellsworth said that both the agency and the manufacturer monitor the drug's use and would take action if risks emerged. Drugmakers, she said, are liable for defective products and frequently are sued by people claiming they have been harmed.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  then turned Alito's question around.\par \par \uc2 "You were asked if the agency is infallible," she said. "I'm wondering about the flip side, which is do you think that courts have specialized scientific knowledge with respect to pharmaceuticals?" she said. "Do you have concerns about judges parsing medical and scientific studies?"\par \par \uc2 Ellsworth said the pharmaceutical industry indeed was concerned, pointing to friend of the court briefs saying it depended "on \uc2 FDA\uc2 's gold standard review process to approve their drugs and then to be able to sell their products."\par \par \uc2 The November 2022 lawsuit was filed in Amarillo, Texas, where it was sure to land before U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee who previously worked for another conservative religious advocacy group. Kacsmaryk determined that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's initial approval of mifepristone in 2000 was flawed and in April 2023 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered the drug withdrawn  }}}\uc2  from the market altogether.\par \par \uc2 Both the Biden administration and Danco appealed to the Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, in New Orleans. That court last year found that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  cut corners in relaxing dispensing rules for mifepristone, in part by failing to consider the cumulative effect of several regulatory changes. The administration and Danco then appealed to the Supreme Court, which agreed to hear the case.\par \par \uc2 Hawley has also argued that allowing mifepristone delivery by mail violates the Comstock Act, a 19th-century federal law that outlawed mailing contraceptives, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements and other materials then considered immoral. Although the statute's current iteration no longer restricts contraceptives, the language against mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements remains on the books.\par \par \uc2 Alito and Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  both asked about the Comstock Act's relevance to the case.\par \par \uc2 Prelogar said it wasn't the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's job to enforce that statute. Under federal law, she said, "it's very clear that the only thing \uc2 FDA\uc2  can take into account for restrictions are safety and efficacy concerns," she said.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, she said, the \uc2 Justice Department's Office of Legal Counsel\uc2 , which advises executive branch agencies, concluded that the Comstock Act prohibits mailing only of unlawful \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements, not an approved medication such as mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 While the 2022 ruling that struck down Roe settled a longstanding legal question at the heart of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, it hasn't freed the Supreme Court from litigation over the procedure. Next month, the justices will consider whether emergency-room doctors at hospitals receiving Medicare funding are permitted to perform abortions to stabilize critical patients\u8212\'20\'14even if state law bans the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Idaho, which outlaws nearly all abortions, is appealing a lower court order the Biden administration won permitting such emergency procedures.\par \par \uc2 A decision in the case argued Tuesday, \uc2 FDA\uc2  v. Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, is expected by early July.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jess.Bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jess.Bravin@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jan Wolfe at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jan.wolfe@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jan.wolfe@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jan Wolfe at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240326ek3q001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
