\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Pill Case Puts Supreme Court Back in the Hot Seat; The justices are considering whether to roll back access to mifepristone, whose demand has swelled since the high court eliminated the constitutional right to an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Jess Bravin and Liz Essley Whyte \par \uc2 1,469 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 March 2024\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-arguments-abortion-pill-mifepristone-c31de31a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will consider}}}\uc2  whether to roll back the availability of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill known as mifepristone}}}\uc2  as women increasingly rely on medication to end unwanted pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The case has quickly forced the court back into the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  thicket after its decision two years ago in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated federal protections}}}\uc2  for the procedure. Since then, roughly one-third of states have banned many or most abortions, but mifepristone is more readily available than ever, especially by mail, and\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/roe-v-wade-is-gone-but-abortions-are-on-the-rise-383ffaf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overall abortions haven't declined}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This has bedeviled Republican politicians and disappointed antiabortion groups who hoped the demise of Roe v. Wade would substantially reduce the number of pregnancy terminations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/abortion-pill-increase-roe-wade-68472ff8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medication abortions now make up}}}\uc2  nearly two-thirds of abortions. There were some 150,000 more of them in 2023 than there were before the decision, in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "That model really poses a threat to the antiabortion movement because once pills are in the mail it's pretty hard to track where they go and where they end up," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, the dean of \uc2 Temple University\uc2 's law school.\par \par \uc2 At issue in Tuesday's case is whether the Food and Drug Administration acted reasonably in adopting rules that have made it easier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/supreme-court-abortion-pill-ruling-access-9a5597e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to obtain mifepristone}}}\uc2  since 2016. As a legal matter, that is fundamentally different from the Dobbs case, which discarded the 1973 court's view in Roe that a woman's control over pregnancy before fetal viability could be inferred from broad constitutional guarantees protecting individual liberty. By withdrawing the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the court left states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to restrict the procedure or not}}}\uc2  as they see fit.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups have spent years fighting the pill's approval, which came in 2000, and later decisions lifting dispensing restrictions. But the current litigation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuit-filed-to-reverse-approval-access-to-abortion-pill-11668796816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which began in November 2022}}}\uc2 , caught fire last year when a conservative federal judge in Amarillo, Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended the pill entirely}}}\uc2 . The judge found the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval process was flawed from the get-go and said the agency didn't sufficiently study the pill's safety.\par \par \uc2 Months later, a U.S. appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/pharma/appeals-panel-rules-fda-improperly-expanded-access-to-abortion-pill-4ffbd3b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scaled back that ruling considerably}}}\uc2 , but concluded the \uc2 FDA\uc2  overstepped with recent moves in 2016 and 2021 to make the pill easier to obtain. The ruling blocked regulations that extended the pill's use for pregnancies up to about 10 weeks and allowed the drug to be administered without an in-person visit with a medical provider.\par \par \uc2 Under an April 2023 Supreme Court order, the decisions rolling back access to mifepristone are on hold while a final ruling is pending. Justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , who wrote the Dobbs opinion, and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , said they would have let the rollback take place.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Sepper, a law professor at the \uc2 University of Texas\uc2 , said Tuesday's case could show how far the court's conservative majority, already critical of regulatory agencies, is willing to let litigation rather than rule making shape policy decisions.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to expertise, "the Food and Drug Administration is really the gold standard," Sepper said, and the agency has been central to the success of the American pharmaceutical industry. Drugmakers are backing the regulators. "They are very, very worried about the idea that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  could be second-guessed in the courts based on the say-so of any E.R. doctor anywhere," she said.\par \par \uc2 The high court's ruling, expected by July, will land in the middle of the election season and has the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/republicans-new-abortion-strategy-talk-about-it-more-not-less-d68d80ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potential to shake up races}}}\uc2  that are up and down the ballot, at a time when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-dobbs-year-after-roe-support-politics-d1ef5a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has proved to be a key political issue}}}\uc2  post-Dobbs.\par \par \uc2 In some ways, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill case has the potential to affect a greater number of women than Dobbs. Even without the constitutional protections Roe provided, more than half the states have legal access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But if pill access is restricted, abortions will be more difficult to obtain across the nation.\par \par \uc2 "States like California and New York are going to be just as affected by any roll back," said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and chief executive of the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which represented an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in the Dobbs case.\par \par \uc2 The current suit, filed by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a Christian conservative advocacy group, on behalf of antiabortion doctors and medical associations, alleges the \uc2 FDA\uc2  flouted legal obligations to ensure patient safety when it relaxed restrictions on access to the drug. Erin Hawley, an \uc2 ADF\uc2  attorney and wife of Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R., Mo.), will argue Tuesday for the challengers.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups have asserted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill can pose dangers, such as severe hemorrhage and infection, which are often undercounted because they say the \uc2 FDA\uc2  isn't tracking serious, nonfatal side effects. And they argue it is more risky as it is currently administered with no in-person visit with a provider required.\par \par \uc2 "What this case is really about is common-sense safeguards," said Donna Harrison, director of research for the American Association of Pro-Life Obstetricians and Gynecologists.\par \par \uc2 Physicians' groups have said that hundreds of studies show the drug's safety and that serious side effects occur in less than 1% of patients. A legal brief from the \uc2 FDA\uc2  said that as of December 2022, 32 deaths had been reported among nearly six million women who have taken mifepristone and some of those had obvious alternative causes, such as drug overdose.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Solicitor General \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , representing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , said in the brief that an exhaustive scientific record supported loosening the pill's restrictions, including experience from the Covid-19 pandemic when the in-person requirement was temporarily suspended. And until this case, she said, no court had ever "restricted access to an \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved drug by second-guessing \uc2 FDA\uc2 's expert judgment about the conditions required to assure that drug's safe use."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What impact will the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have on 2024 races? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 It is possible the court could decide the case without having to weigh in on the \uc2 FDA\uc2  at all. Prelogar argues none of the plaintiffs have a proper basis to sue, because it is only speculation that an emergency-room doctor opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may one day be forced to treat a mifepristone patient facing complications. The challengers disagree, arguing that such a scenario is more probable since the \uc2 FDA\uc2  allowed women to take the pill without visiting a doctor.\par \par \uc2 Danco Laboratories\uc2 , the drug's brand manufacturer, requested the 2016 changes after being pushed by \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, as states had started passing laws that were limiting a common practice of doctors providing the drug off-label later in pregnancy. Danco, which is also involved in the litigation, said it worked for about six years to update the drug's label for expanded use, at a price tag north of $1 million.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pills-to-be-available-more-widely-under-new-fda-rules-11672789765"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FDA said mifepristone could be dispensed}}}\uc2  via specially certified bricks-and-mortar pharmacies, rather than by certified doctors or mail-order pharmacies, opening up yet another avenue for women to obtain the pills. In March, pharmacy chains CVS and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said they would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/cvs-walgreens-to-sell-abortion-pill-mifepristone-within-weeks-8d36f801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carry the drug}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14a change that also could be undone if the Supreme Court rules for the challengers.\par \par \uc2 Since Dobbs, clinics have relied on mifepristone to accommodate a surge in demand after many clinics in conservative states shut down. For blue states, that has helped keep clinic wait times, which can stretch for several weeks, in check.\par \par \uc2 One reason women across the U.S. have been able to obtain the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill is that blue states have passed so-called shield laws designed to protect providers from liability or prosecution if they send pills to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned.\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project is one such provider. Patients communicate with a doctor online who prescribes the pills, in accordance with Massachusetts law. Doctors generally avoid traveling to states with bans to avoid run-ins with laws there.\par \par \uc2 Angel Foster, head of the group, said the mifepristone lawsuit has led to a consequence the plaintiffs surely didn't intend: a surge in demand for the drug. A few years ago "most people hadn't heard of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Foster said. "This has entered into a broader public consciousness."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jess.Bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jess.Bravin@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240324ek3o000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
