\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Trump Nears Decision on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Stance, Aims to 'Make Both Sides Happy'; Presumptive GOP presidential nominee also defends use of harsh language regarding immigrants\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Leary \par \uc2 912 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2024\par 20:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Presumptive Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would make a decision soon on where he stands on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/republicans-new-abortion-strategy-talk-about-it-more-not-less-d68d80ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  limits}}}\uc2 , aiming for a middle ground that would protect access earlier in a pregnancy but bar later procedures for women nationwide.\par \par \uc2 In a Fox News interview that aired Sunday, he also defended his use of harsh, dehumanizing language for migrants who cross the border illegally.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Trump is staking out a position on a contentious issue that has been blamed for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/frustrated-republicans-try-to-explain-lack-of-midterm-red-wave-11668036382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weaker-than-expected performances}}}\uc2  by Republicans in recent elections, as Democrats rallied to the polls to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the wake of a\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 Supreme Court ruling}}}\uc2  that ended the right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Trump was asked in the Fox News interview about a{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/16/us/politics/trump-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times report}}}\uc2  that he was settling on a ban after 16 weeks of pregnancy and whether that would be politically acceptable.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to find out and pretty soon I'm going to be making a decision," Trump said, without confirming that specific number. "I would like to see if we could make both sides happy."\par \par \uc2 Trump said he believes in exceptions for rape and incest and to save the life of the mother. "You have to go with the exceptions. And the number of weeks, I'll be coming up with a recommendation fairly soon. I think the recommendation will be accepted," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling overturning Roe v. Wade kick-started a wide-open debate about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, both at the state and federal level. Some states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have backed near-total bans}}}\uc2  on the procedure, while others have set limits after a certain number of weeks of pregnancy. Other states have passed laws preserving broader access to the procedure, up through around 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The former president has taken credit for the ruling overturning Roe v. Wade\u8212\'20\'14he put three conservative justices on the high court during his administration. But he has also criticized some state laws, including a six-week ban in Florida, as harsh, and said Republicans need to find a way to talk about the issue and must allow for exceptions.\par \par \uc2 "You have to go with your heart. But beyond that, you also have to get elected," Trump said Sunday, reflecting past comments he has made, some privately, about the harm the issue has done to the GOP at the polls.\par \par \uc2 Trump on Sunday said Democrats are "radicals" on the issue for resisting setting a number of weeks in pregnancy at which the procedure should be banned.\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/florida-abortion-rulings-to-keep-issue-front-and-center-in-november-1168511c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have harnessed the issue}}}\uc2  in recent elections and state referendums. President Biden, the presumptive Democratic nominee, has made it a centerpiece of his 2024 campaign, calling for nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including through medicated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as with mifepristone, which can be used to end a pregnancy through 10 weeks of gestation.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court, meanwhile, will hear a high-stakes case later this month that has the potential to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill more difficult to obtain, an issue that cuts to the heart of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in conservative and liberal states alike.\par \par \uc2 Later Sunday the Biden campaign issued a statement from Sen. Elizabeth Warren (D., Mass.). "Trump said we're going to find out if the country will accept his plans for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and he's right," she said. Americans will reject Trump and send President Biden back to the White House, she said.\par \par \uc2 Before he ran for president in 2016, Trump had supported broad \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access before taking a more conservative stance. "I'm pro-life, and I was originally pro-choice," he said during his first campaign. "I have evolved."\par \par \uc2 Trump recently came out in favor of in vitro fertilization following a ruling by an{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/major-alabama-health-system-pauses-ivf-treatments-after-state-court-says-frozen-embryos-qualify-as-children-71ed704e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all-Republican Alabama court}}}\uc2  casting doubt on the legality of the procedure in the post-Roe world.\par \par \uc2 Trump's often harsh rhetoric on other subjects, including immigration, have also gained more attention.\par \par \uc2 Fox News host Howard Kurtz asked Trump on Sunday about saying immigrants are "poisoning the blood" of America. Trump defended his language, saying criminals are entering the country illegally with drugs that harm Americans or end up committing violent crimes.\par \par \uc2 Told critics have said such rhetoric echoes that of Adolf Hitler, Trump said, "I didn't know that, but that's what they say." But he doubled down on what he said was the danger posed by some illegal immigrants. "Our country is being poisoned."\par \par \uc2 Trump has also referred to domestic political opponents as "vermin."\par \par \uc2 During a rally in Dayton, Ohio, on Saturday, Trump leaned heavily into immigration. "I don't know if you call them people\u8212\'20\'14in some cases they're not people, in my opinion," he said. "But I'm not allowed to say that because the radical left says that's a terrible thing to say."\par \par \uc2 Later Trump added, "These are animals, OK?" he said. "And we have to stop it."\par \par \uc2 Trump on Sunday also defended his controversial suggestion that he would encourage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/nato-leader-blasts-trumps-suggestion-he-would-encourage-russian-invasion-of-u-s-allies-3eb96a10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia to attack NATO nations}}}\uc2  that fall short on defense-spending goals. "It sounds like somebody that wants to get people to pay money," he said, referring to his longtime complaint that member nations aren't spending enough on defense.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240317ek3h0028l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
