\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b \uc2 Red-State  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Bans Drive Women to New Mexico; Clinics have expanded and added services for women from Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas | Photographs by Adria Malcolm for The Wall Street Journal \par \uc2 997 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 March 2024\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ALBUQUERQUE, N. M.\u8212\'20\'14Most of the cars parked outside a new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic here are from Texas.\par \par \uc2 Whole Woman's Health of New Mexico is one of the closest places women from Texas can get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas banned the procedure  }}}\uc2  in 2022. The Supreme Court that June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 , removing the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upending reproductive healthcare  }}}\uc2  across the country.\par \par \uc2 The clinic, which opened nearly a year ago, is one outpost in what has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive healthcare perimeter  }}}\uc2  around Southern states that have restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . During a recent week at the clinic, patients drove from Fort Worth and flew from Houston. One planned to start her 10-hour drive home just after her appointment to return in time for her son's basketball game.\par \par \uc2 "Everything we know about the world of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care has changed," said Marva Sadler, Whole Woman's Health's senior director of clinical services.\par \par \uc2 Nearly three-fourths of women who get abortions in New Mexico come from other states compared with about one-third in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/support-for-abortion-access-is-near-record-wsj-norc-poll-finds-6021c712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supports \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2 . Clinics that closed in Texas and Mississippi reopened here, and older clinics added appointments and staff.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2 's ruling in February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/alabama-supreme-court-embryo-ivf-uncertainty-88cf2146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that embryos are people  }}}\uc2  has pushed women's healthcare advocates in New Mexico and elsewhere to protect and expand fertility treatment. New Mexico Gov. \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2 , a Democrat, said she wants more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/elizabeth-carr-first-ivf-baby-reproductive-technology-faecfc6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in vitro fertilization providers  }}}\uc2  and obstetrician-gynecologists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/some-doctors-rethink-careers-after-states-restrict-abortions-11657791001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to practice in the state  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Days after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, \uc2 Lujan Grisham\uc2  signed an executive order protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Her administration hopes this summer to start building an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in southern Do\u241\'00\'F1a Ana County and is widening contraceptive access statewide.\par \par \uc2 "We want to be a state that no matter where a woman or her family is," \uc2 Lujan Grisham\uc2  said, "we figure that out and provide confidential safe, unfettered access."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents in New Mexico resent their leaders' vision of the state as a destination for the procedure. "We don't want to be known for this," said Angie Smith, board president of the Right to Life Committee of New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Cities including Hobbs and Clovis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-states-where-abortion-is-legal-some-cities-look-to-restrict-access-11671749172"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have attempted to effectively ban  }}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within municipal limits. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being glorified in New Mexico," said Sterling Donner, a commissioner for the town of Edgewood, just east of Albuquerque, where he introduced an ordinance last year that would effectively ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 New Mexico lawmakers passed legislation in 2023 prohibiting local governments from restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Attorney General Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Torrez, a Democrat, filed a lawsuit against several communities that had done so. The New Mexico Supreme Court halted enforcement of the local restrictions while litigation continues.\par \par \uc2 Expansion mode\par \par \uc2 New Mexico Religious Coalition for Reproductive Choice, an advocacy group that has added staff, manages a weekly program that flies patients from Dallas to Albuquerque and funds their abortions. The group has expanded from a two-room office in downtown Albuquerque to nearly a full floor.\par \par \uc2 Inside the offices, cots with blankets sit available so that patients can rest before return flights. Patients can take stickers back to Texas that bear QR codes and the question "Need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?" in English or Spanish.\par \par \uc2 "We have never had to turn anyone away," said Joan Lamunyon Sanford, the group's executive director.\par \par \uc2 Across town on a recent morning, three antiabortion protesters jeered from afar at people walking into the University of New Mexico's Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Doctors at the center were among the first to experience {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how their work would change if Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  were overturned after Texas in 2021 passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/behind-texas-abortion-law-an-attorneys-unusual-enforcement-idea-11630762683?mod=wsj_story_thread_st-texas-abortion-3b0992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a law allowing its residents to enforce a ban  }}}\uc2  on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy. Women from Texas started traveling to New Mexico \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, where providers struggled to keep up.\par \par \uc2 More doctors and nurses joined the center's staff. Wait times fell from up to seven weeks to one week or less, said Dr. Lisa Hofler, who performs abortions at the center. The clinic has treated a steady number of women from New Mexico even as more patients have arrived from Texas, thanks to the added capacity and availability at other clinics.\par \par \uc2 "We're not doing this alone," Hofler said.\par \par \uc2 'This ain't Texas'\par \par \uc2 Operating an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Albuquerque is a bit simpler than it once was in Texas. Protesters in New Mexico are a rarer presence outside clinics than they were in Texas. Sadler, who worked for 17 years at Whole Woman's Health clinics in Texas before moving to Albuquerque, said she doesn't feel the same fear that the state might try to shut it down.\par \par \uc2 "I tell my patients who come here from Texas that this ain't Texas," Sadler said.\par \par \uc2 The clinic has lavender interiors and rooms named after Michelle Obama and poet Audre Lorde. After \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures, patients sit on leather chairs in dim lighting. A pot of tea, brewed to ease cramping, sits by the door.\par \par \uc2 A patient who drove from Fort Worth clutched a heating pad on her abdomen. The 22-year-old had arrived in Albuquerque about nine weeks pregnant. Without maternity leave as a personal trainer and without her parents in Texas to help her, she decided to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and searched for the closest facility. The Albuquerque clinic was about 600 miles away.\par \par \uc2 After about 20 minutes of recovery, she was ready to leave. She set down her mug of tea, grabbed her bag and walked out of the room to begin her drive home.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How important do you think the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be in the 2024 election? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240312ek3c002uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
