\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Takeaways From Biden's State of the Union Address; In campaign mode, president challenges Trump and Republicans on Ukraine, immigration and taxes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,549 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2024\par 12:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shifting into campaign mode, President Biden used his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/biden-state-of-the-union-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State of the Union address  }}}\uc2  to promise to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, plead for Ukraine aid and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-to-draw-sharp-contrast-with-republicans-in-state-of-the-union-ab7b4c01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticize Republicans  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14particularly his once and future opponent, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here are some takeaways from the address:\par \par \uc2 Taking on Trump\par \par \uc2 From the start, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-and-trump-in-two-speeches-speak-to-two-visions-of-america-6720a359"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embraced political messaging  }}}\uc2  and targeted his likely Republican rival.\par \par \uc2 While Biden didn't name Trump, he accused him of "bowing down" to Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , saying it is "outrageous, it is dangerous and it is unacceptable." Biden called for funding Ukraine in its war against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Standing in the House of Representatives, Biden also referenced the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/jan-6-key-moments-leading-up-to-the-attack-on-the-capitol-11654796246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jan. 6, 2021, U.S. Capitol riot  }}}\uc2  and said Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-say-in-prime-time-address-democracy-is-at-stake-in-midterm-elections-11662048825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are undermining U.S. democracy  }}}\uc2  with false claims about widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election. "My predecessor and some of you here seek to bury the truth of Jan. 6," he said.\par \par \uc2 "You can't love your country only when you win," he added.\par \par \uc2 Biden also assailed Trump's response to the Covid-19 pandemic, saying, "My predecessor failed the most basic presidential duty that he owes the American people, the duty to care."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot\par \par \uc2 Biden confronted the Supreme Court\u8212\'20\'14with some justices in the audience\u8212\'20\'14over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the decision  }}}\uc2  that eliminated the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "With all due respect, justices, women are not without electoral or political power," Biden said. "You're about to realize just how much." It was an unusually direct rebuke of the court by Biden, an institutionalist who has long said he respects the independence of the court.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been driven to the polls since the 2022 Supreme Court decision that eliminated the right to the procedure. While Biden, a devout Roman Catholic, has been a reluctant messenger on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, he has embraced the issue. In the speech, he never actually used the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite it being in his prepared text. Many Democratic women in the audience wore white in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Without naming Trump, Biden pointed out that the former president has bragged about appointing the Supreme Court justices who overturned the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision. He also argued that Republicans are blocking access, citing restrictive laws that have been passed around the country. And he assailed the state Supreme Court ruling in Alabama that frozen embryos qualify as children under a state law, upending in vitro fertilization services in the state.\par \par \uc2 Biden also referenced two of the guests in the first lady's box to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  message: Kate Cox, a woman who had to leave Texas to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a fetus with a fatal diagnosis, and Latorya Beasley, an Alabama woman whose in vitro fertilization process was disrupted.\par \par \uc2 "My God, what freedoms will you take away next?" he said to Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Immigration clash\par \par \uc2 Republicans wanted Biden to say the name of Laken Riley, a 22-year-old nursing student from Georgia who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/a-college-students-killing-in-georgia-opens-new-front-in-immigration-debate-e47fd344"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was allegedly killed  }}}\uc2  by a Venezuelan migrant. He said it.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans wore buttons\u8212\'20\'14and Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R., Ga.) wore a shirt\u8212\'20\'14with the words "Say Her Name," a reference to Riley. Greene said, "Say her name" to Biden as he entered the room, and then shouted it again when Biden began speaking about immigration.\par \par \uc2 Holding up a button, Biden said her name, but appeared to pronounce it as "Lincoln Riley." He called her "an innocent young woman who was killed by an illegal." Addressing her parents, he added, "My heart goes out to you, having lost children myself, I understand."\par \par \uc2 Biden then launched into a rebuke of Republicans and Trump for opposing a bipartisan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/why-the-border-deal-never-stood-a-chance-eb5a24ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 border agreement in the Senate  }}}\uc2 . Trump has opposed the measure, calling it a "gift" to Democrats in an election year. Biden called on Republicans to work with him. "We can fight about fixing the border, or we can fix it," he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden has been weighing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-executive-actions-on-border-would-face-steep-legal-political-hurdles-d8a5cc4d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive action on immigration  }}}\uc2 , but has yet to make such a move. Those efforts have drawn criticism from some within his party as well as questions over whether they would be challenged in court.\par \par \uc2 The age factor\par \par \uc2 Biden came into the chamber looking for opportunities to joust with Republicans.\par \par \uc2 His team wanted to show a feisty Biden, knowing he would be closely watched for any signs of age or fatigue, and he frequently raised his voice. Polling shows the public is concerned about his age, particularly following a special counsel report that raised questions about his memory.\par \par \uc2 Biden narrowly trailed Trump in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/voters-are-more-upbeat-on-economy-but-biden-gets-little-benefit-wsj-poll-shows-8e608db8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest Wall Street Journal poll  }}}\uc2 , with 47% backing Trump and 45% picking Biden\u8212\'20\'14and 73% of voters saying he is too old to run for another term.\par \par \uc2 His exchange with Republicans on Riley was the kind of moment the White House wanted to see. At another point, Biden knocked Republicans for touting the flood of cash that has been funneled into their districts from bills that they opposed, such as the infrastructure law.\par \par \uc2 "If any of you don't want that money in your district, just let me know," Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Biden also went off script a few times, including a point where he suggested that people could fly on Air Force One with him to Toronto, Berlin or Moscow to find cheaper prescription drugs.\par \par \uc2 And he directly referenced his age at times. "I've been told I'm too old," he said as he concluded his speech. "Whether young or old, I've always known what endures."\par \par \uc2 "The issue facing our nation isn't how old we are," he said. "It's how old are our ideas."\par \par \uc2 Middle East politics\par \par \uc2 Biden tried to walk a careful line on the toughest policy issue on his plate, Israel's war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14as protesters calling for a cease-fire gathered outside the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Biden stressed the need for a temporary cease-fire and called for hostages to be released. He also said the U.S. military {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/biden-to-announce-creation-of-gaza-port-to-receive-aid-5fc131b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will install a temporary pier  }}}\uc2  off the Gaza coast for cargo ships to unload food, water and other emergency supplies, boosting the direct American role in addressing the humanitarian crisis.\par \par \uc2 Biden stressed that Israel has a right to defend itself, but said "Israel also has a fundamental responsibility to protect innocent civilians in Gaza." He also said: "As we look to the future, the only real solution to the situation is a two-state solution over time."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you think was the most important moment in President Biden's speech? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrats have been vocally critical of his response to the war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and pressed him to do more to curtail the bombardment of Gaza and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/u-s-and-allies-reach-for-last-resort-to-get-aid-to-gazans-ce145704"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing humanitarian crisis  }}}\uc2 . When Biden brought up Gaza, Rep. \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  (D., Mich.)\u8212\'20\'14the only Palestinian-American in Congress\u8212\'20\'14jumped up to display a two-sided sign. One side read "Stop Sending Bombs," and the other side said "Lasting Ceasefire Now."\par \par \uc2 There was also a vocal protest unrelated to Israel: Steven Nikoui\u8212\'20\'14the father of Marine Kareem Nikoui, who was killed in the 2021 terrorist attack outside Kabul airport during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/report-blames-top-biden-officials-for-failures-during-afghanistan-exit-b5ac183d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evacuation of U.S. troops from Afghanistan  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14was arrested by \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  after yelling to Biden from the gallery to "remember Abbey Gate." Nikoui was at the speech as a guest of Rep. \uc2 Brian Mast\uc2  (R., Fla.).\par \par \uc2 Divided chamber\par \par \uc2 Biden drew repeated cheers and applause from Democrats but little love from Republicans.\par \par \uc2 He drew little bipartisan support until he spoke about the late congressman \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  and civil rights. Members of both parties stood up, including House Speaker Mike Johnson (R., La.), who was seated alongside Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  behind Biden, in his first State of the Union address as speaker.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans took to social media to complain. Rep. \uc2 Dan Bishop\uc2  (R., N.C.) said that this "is not a State of the Union. This is an angry screed vilifying half the country."\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Don Bacon\uc2  (R., Neb.)\u8212\'20\'14one of the few Republicans to cheer Biden's calls for supporting Ukraine\u8212\'20\'14in another post characterized the address as "thus far one of the most divisive speeches ever for a State of the Union."\par \par \uc2 Trump reacted in real time to Biden's speech, railing against his successor on his social-media platform, Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 "He is so angry and crazy!" Trump wrote, in one of a string of posts during the speech.\par \par \uc2 In the GOP response to the speech, delivered from her kitchen, Sen. Katie Britt (R., Ala.), 42, targeted Biden's age, calling it the "the performance of a permanent politician who has actually been in office for longer than I've been alive." She attacked Biden's policies on the border in graphic detail, citing Riley's death, and criticized him as out of touch while people struggle with inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Let's be honest\u8212\'20\'14it's been a minute since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pumped gas, ran carpool or pushed a grocery cart," she said. "Meanwhile, the rest of us see every day that our dollar doesn't go as far."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240308ek380012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
