\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 What to Watch for in Biden's State of the Union Address; Biden will deliver his election-year speech to Congress Thursday as his expected rematch with Trump intensifies\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Thomas and Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2024\par 15:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14President Biden will push for corporate-tax hikes, restoring Roe v. Wade and boosting the middle class in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/biden-state-of-the-union-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State of the Union address  }}}\uc2  with major stakes for his re-election effort.\par \par \uc2 The speech will give him what will likely be his largest televised audience before this summer's Democratic convention. With former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  now unchallenged to win the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/nikki-haley-drops-out-2024-presidential-election-625277ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican presidential nomination  }}}\uc2 , it will provide Biden with a prime-time platform {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-to-draw-sharp-contrast-with-republicans-in-state-of-the-union-ab7b4c01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to contrast his vision  }}}\uc2  with his rival's and appeal to the diverse coalition of voters who elected him in 2020.\par \par \uc2 But it also comes as the 81-year-old president faces a public that is skeptical {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/bidens-age-back-in-spotlight-after-special-counsel-report-verbal-flubs-159c77f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over his age  }}}\uc2  and ability to handle a second term, and as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-campaign-contends-with-new-challenge-hecklers-from-his-own-side-9b222ca1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces criticism  }}}\uc2  from parts of his political base over his response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/gaza-cease-fire-talks-enter-critical-moment-aa45f994?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel's conflict with Hamas  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here's what to watch in Thursday's State of the Union address at 9 p.m. ET:\par \par \uc2 The 2024 campaign\par \par \uc2 Biden will be addressing the nation two days after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-super-tuesday-wins-will-add-pressure-on-haley-to-drop-out-35b013b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump dominated  }}}\uc2  the Super Tuesday contests and in the aftermath of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/supreme-court-ruling-trump-ballot-colorado-092852fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's ruling  }}}\uc2  that Trump can remain on Colorado's primary ballot in a rejection of an attempt to challenge his eligibility.\par \par \uc2 Biden huddled with top aides to work on the speech over the weekend at Camp David and revisions are expected to continue until showtime. Aides said the address will focus on ways "to make life better for every American," including lowering costs for such essentials as prescription drugs, raising taxes on the wealthy and corporations, and protecting the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In short, Biden will try to draw a direct contrast with Trump under the mantra, "Whose side are you on?"\par \par \uc2 Trump, for his part, has painted his contest with Biden in stark terms, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112049357098381588"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posting  }}}\uc2  on his social-media platform Wednesday that "Biden is the enemy, he is destroying our country!"\par \par \uc2 The key for Biden, Democratic allies said, is to present a forward-leaning message.\par \par \uc2 "There's always an inclination to talk a lot about accomplishments, but it's also important to lay out future goals because you have to give people something to vote for," said Celinda Lake, a Democratic pollster who worked on Biden's 2020 campaign.\par \par \uc2 The age factor\par \par \uc2 Biden is also going to be judged on style and delivery\u8212\'20\'14and closely watched for any flubs or missteps.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/voters-are-more-upbeat-on-economy-but-biden-gets-little-benefit-wsj-poll-shows-8e608db8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polling shows  }}}\uc2  that most voters think Biden is too old to serve another four years. Those fears were amplified following a recent special counsel report that alleged Biden had memory issues.\par \par \uc2 "People will be listening to what Biden says, but also watching how he says it," said Michael Waldman, who served as former President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 's chief speechwriter. "If he can show some zest and joie de vivre and be a happy warrior, it will help him a lot."\par \par \uc2 The president has angrily rejected the suggestion that he is too old and his advisers see the speech as an opportunity to showcase vigor. They often recall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/state-of-the-union-2023-president-biden/card/biden-booed-by-republicans-over-social-security-remarks-1Y4l3TkDLR1yK33msxwx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a moment  }}}\uc2  from the 2023 speech\u8212\'20\'14when Biden went off script and jousted with Republicans on Social Security\u8212\'20\'14as an example of him showing his ability to improvise. Biden was working with speech coach Michael Sheehan, who coached Clinton and former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , ahead of the speech, said a person familiar with the planning.\par \par \uc2 "If he can come close to doing what he did last year that would be great," said Rep. \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  (D., Calif.).\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 Biden will seek to use the address to point to progress on the economy, including declining rates of inflation and improving confidence. He will also include a consumer focus. Ahead of the speech, the White House outlined plans to cut credit-card late fees from an average of $32 down to $8 and target so-called "junk fees" across a range of goods and services.\par \par \uc2 The president plans to propose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-offers-more-corporate-tax-ideas-as-he-draws-contrast-with-trump-9f026f44"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising taxes  }}}\uc2  on large companies, reprising some previous plans such as raising the corporate tax rate to 28% and boosting taxes on U.S. companies' foreign profits. He will also propose raising a corporate minimum tax, which took effect this past year, to 21% from 15%, and will call for imposing stiffer limits on companies' ability to deduct the wages of their highest-paid workers, according to White House officials.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to address immigration after he and Trump made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/biden-trump-border-visit-immigration-698bb50e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dueling visits  }}}\uc2  this past week to the U.S.-Mexico border in Texas. Biden has blamed Republicans for opposing a bipartisan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/why-the-border-deal-never-stood-a-chance-eb5a24ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 border agreement in the Senate  }}}\uc2  that would have allowed the government to expel migrants if crossings surpassed a daily threshold of 4,000. Trump has opposed the measure, calling it a "gift" to Democrats in an election year.\par \par \uc2 Biden is also expected to emphasize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights more than he has in past speeches, as the Supreme Court ruling that eliminated the right to the procedure has proved a powerful motivator for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Chamber drama\par \par \uc2 Biden could face drama from the left and the right on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 Republicans opposed to his agenda will be in attendance. House Speaker Mike Johnson (R., La.), will be seated alongside Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  behind Biden, in his first State of the Union address as speaker. Any instances in which Johnson appears to object, or joins in applause, signaling bipartisan support, will be notable.\par \par \uc2 Biden could also see frustration from within his own party. Progressive Democrats have been vocally critical of his response to the war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and pressed him to do more to curtail the bombardment of Gaza and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/u-s-and-allies-reach-for-last-resort-to-get-aid-to-gazans-ce145704"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing humanitarian crisis  }}}\uc2 . Those frustrations have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/biden-campaign-contends-with-new-challenge-hecklers-from-his-own-side-9b222ca1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led to protests  }}}\uc2  at many of Biden's public events, and over 100,000 voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/in-michigan-primary-uncommitted-is-a-protest-vote-22915829?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chose "uncommitted"  }}}\uc2  in Michigan's Democratic primary to push Biden to change course. The president has been calling on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to accept a potential deal to release Israeli hostages in exchange for a temporary pause. Rep. \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  (D., Mo.) has passed out pins for lawmakers to wear at the State of the Union showing their support for a cease-fire in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The GOP's response will be delivered by Sen. Katie Britt (R., Ala.), who at 42 is the youngest woman serving in the Senate. Britt is expected to make a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/katie-britt-state-of-the-union-response-16447c76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generational appeal to viewers  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rep. Nancy Mace (R., S.C.) said Biden would offer "denial and delusion, in terms of what's currently going on in America."\par \par \uc2 Guest stars\par \par \uc2 The speech will be attended by a number of prominent guests, including Kate Cox, a Texas woman at the center of a high-profile dispute with the state's restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are you watching for in the State of the Union address? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Cox, who will be a guest of first lady Jill Biden, sought legal permission to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas after she learned that her fetus had a fatal diagnosis and later traveled out of state to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. The case appeared to be the first time a pregnant woman sought court intervention to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Other guests in the first lady's box will include \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  Union President Shawn Fain; Maria Shriver, a journalist and activist who is a member of the Kennedy family; and Latorya Beasley, an Alabama woman whose in vitro fertilization process was disrupted by a state Supreme Court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/major-alabama-health-system-pauses-ivf-treatments-after-state-court-says-frozen-embryos-qualify-as-children-71ed704e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frozen embryos  }}}\uc2  qualify as children under a state law.\par \par \uc2 The parents of imprisoned Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/video/born-to-be-a-reporter-wsjs-evan-gershkovich-detained-in-russia/AEA785E9-EFBF-4939-95C2-3A99460500AB?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detained in Russia  }}}\uc2 , will be there as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/parents-of-russian-held-evan-gershkovich-to-attend-bidens-state-of-the-union-e7e5553f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guests of Johnson  }}}\uc2 . The \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  has designated Gershkovich as wrongfully detained.\par \par \uc2 Who will watch?\par \par \uc2 In 2023, 27.3 million people watched the address, according to the Nielsen company. That was down from the 38.2 million who watched it in 2022. The audience is older. Of the 2023 audience, 73% were aged 55 and older, 19% were aged 35-54 and 5% were aged 18-34.\par \par \uc2 Lake, the Democratic pollster, said swing voters weren't likely to tune in for this speech. "The people that are going to be paying the most attention are the base," she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ken Thomas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ken.thomas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ken.thomas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Catherine Lucey at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240307ek37000jj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
