\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Flimflam; The governor sets himself up for the 2028 presidential election by falsely attacking red-state restrictions.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Tomaino \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 March 2024\par 22:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Is \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  running for something? In 2022, while pursuing an easy re-election as California governor, he paid for 18 billboards in seven states promoting California as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sanctuary. One, featuring a woman in handcuffs, read: "Texas doesn't own your body. You do." Another appended a scriptural appeal beneath its pitch: "Love your neighbor as yourself. There is no greater commandment than these."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom is taking his message to the digital commons. On Feb. 25, he tweeted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1761777701407571985"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video advertisement }}}\uc2  from his Campaign for Democracy PAC that shows a young woman chained to a hospital bed and crying for help. A rape kit rests nearby. "Trump Republicans want to criminalize young women who travel to receive the reproductive care they need," the narrator says. "Don't let them hold Tennessee women hostage." The associated website, RightToTravel.org, asserts that the state "basically" wants to "imprison women and young girls."\par \par \uc2 Neither Mr. Newsom, the ad nor the website mentions the legislation they have in mind, and it's obvious why. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TN/text/HB1895/id/2901267"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 H.B. 1895 }}}\uc2  would do nothing of the sort. Tennessee Rep. Jason Zachary, who introduced the measure, describes it in an interview as a "parents' rights bill." It would amend the criminal code to establish a felony offense, "\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking," if an adult "recruits, harbors, or transports a pregnant unemancipated minor" to procure an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without the knowledge and assent of her parent or guardian. A violation would also allow for civil action for the wrongful death of an unborn child.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Zachary says he was inspired to propose the bill by a couple who found themselves in exactly those circumstances\u8212\'20\'14someone they "trusted" had shuttled their 14-year-old daughter out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without their say-so. Abortions are lawful in Tennessee only to protect the mother's life, but no law purports to prohibit leaving the state to obtain one. Mr. Zachary's bill would allow for convictions only of third parties, and not if the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was performed on an adult or with parental consent.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom is doubtless positioning himself to be the Democratic presidential front-runner in 2028 and, contingently, in 2024. Yet ushering minors across state lines without their parents' consent seems an odd hill to die on. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americas-abortion-quandary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 Pew poll }}}\uc2  found that among adults who think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, 56% say parental notification should be required for minors.\par \par \uc2 Which explains why Mr. Newsom is aggressively misrepresenting the law. Portraying pro-life Republicans as extremists appeals to both the Democratic base and voters who are moderate on or ambivalent about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Campaigning on the issue in red states may not influence policy there, and Mr. Newsom is unlikely ever to carry overwhelmingly Republican Tennessee. But there are Democrats there, and they vote in presidential primaries.\par \par \uc2 Still, the brazen dishonesty of this campaign tells voters something about the governor's political character.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tomaino is an assistant editorial features editor at the Journal.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240305ek35005sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
