\par\par \uc2 Europe News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 France Enshrines  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights in Constitution; French lawmakers endorse change in rare moment of national unity\b0\par\par\uc2 By Noemie Bisserbe \par \uc2 587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 March 2024\par 21:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PARIS\u8212\'20\'14France became the first country in the world to explicitly enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in its constitution after French lawmakers overwhelmingly endorsed the change in a historic vote in the Palace of Versailles on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The amendment, which passed 780-72 in a special joint session of Parliament, changes Article 34 of the French constitution to state that "a woman has the guaranteed freedom to have recourse to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The vote followed President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  's pledge to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  an irreversible right in France after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  eliminated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruling the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In changing its constitution, France is reinforcing a 1975 law that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country. The time limit on elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set at 14 weeks of pregnancy. In recent years, several countries in Europe, including Poland and Hungary, have restricted access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I never thought I'd live to see this," said Claudine Monteil, a 74-year-old historian and the youngest signatory of the "manifesto of the 343," a petition written by French writer and philosopher Simone de Beauvoir in 1971. The 343 women included the legendary French actress Catherine Deneuve and writer Marguerite Duras. By signing the manifesto, they went public in saying they had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a crime punishable by up to six years in jail at the time. The manifesto paved the way for the legalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in France a few years later.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, hundreds of people gathered on the Place du Trocad\u233\'00\'E9ro, in the center of the French capital, to watch the parliamentary debate on a big screen. They burst into cheers and applause after the amendment passed. The Eiffel Tower, rising behind the crowd, started scintillating seconds after the vote's results were announced.\par \par \uc2 The vote marked a rare moment of relative unity in France's divided Parliament. Macron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/macrons-parliamentary-majority-at-risk-in-final-round-of-french-elections-11655631002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost his majority  }}}\uc2  in the National Assembly, the lower house of Parliament, in June 2022 as the far left and the far right gained ground. Since then, the government has struggled to push legislation through Parliament, often prompting Macron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/macron-government-bypasses-frances-national-assembly-to-pass-pension-overhaul-26089695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to use special constitutional powers  }}}\uc2  to bypass lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Two-thirds of French people were in favor of the change, according to a recent \uc2 YouGov\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 "There are moments in the life of a country when unity, general interest must prevail over daily quarrels," French Prime Minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/europe/macron-appoints-youngest-prime-minister-in-frances-modern-history-7e185863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gabriel Attal  }}}\uc2  told lawmakers, speaking in the ornate 19th-century Congress Chamber of the Palace of Versailles, where he received a standing ovation.\par \par \uc2 "Yes, the freedom to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains under threat, our rights are inherently threatened, inherently fragile," said Attal. "Talk to American women about it," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's 2022 decision to overturn Roe v. Wade created a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/cvs-walgreens-to-sell-abortion-pill-mifepristone-within-weeks-8d36f801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access  }}}\uc2  across the U.S., with millions of women of reproductive age now living in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is largely illegal.\par \par \uc2 The vote in Versailles on Monday represented the final step of a long legislative process that started several months ago. The National Assembly approved the proposal in January, and the Senate adopted the bill on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Attal said on Monday that the message sent to women was clear. "Your body belongs to you, and nobody has the right to control it in your place," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Noemie Bisserbe at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:noemie.bisserbe@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noemie.bisserbe@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240304ek34003ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
