\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Republicans Confront Political Damage From Alabama IVF Ruling; Florida lawmakers tap brakes on 'fetal personhood' bill\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephanie Armour \par \uc2 1,128 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2024\par 10:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans are working to minimize the political fallout from an Alabama court ruling upholding the legal rights of embryos by reassuring voters they will protect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/alabama-supreme-court-embryo-ivf-uncertainty-88cf2146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 access to in vitro fertilization  }}}\uc2  treatments.\par \par \uc2 There are signs the damage will be difficult to undo. Democrats are stepping up their offensive on the issue, asserting that GOP lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-republican-lawmakers-forced-to-defend-ivf-as-gop-abortion-woes-mount-55729386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defending in vitro fertilization  }}}\uc2  can't be trusted because many have also backed early \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or legislation stating that life begins at fertilization.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, legislation stalled that would let parents recover financial damages for the wrongful death of an unborn child after a Republican state lawmaker on Monday asked that the bill be postponed. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups had said it could lead to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/healthcare/elizabeth-carr-first-ivf-baby-reproductive-technology-faecfc6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictions on fertility services  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rep. Nancy Mace (R, S.C.) drafted a nonbinding legislative proposal expressing support for continued access to fertility care and assisted reproductive technology. She said she wants Republicans to be vocal about protecting infertility treatments.\par \par \uc2 In Alabama, GOP state lawmakers working to preserve access to the treatment following the court's ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/alabama-ivf-gop-rushes-to-pass-protections-be65fa9c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have prepared proposals  }}}\uc2  that would say a fertilized egg is a potential life rather than a human one if outside the uterus. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has urged state lawmakers to find a solution that preserves access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Republicans' enthusiasm for protecting in vitro fertilization underscores the risks to the party in November elections if Democrats are successful in portraying GOP lawmakers as extremists who could endanger contraception, fertility services and other \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Polling shows strong support for in vitro fertilization, with an estimated 2% of births in the U.S. occurring with the aid of fertility services.\par \par \uc2 The question now is whether the damage has already been done.\par \par \uc2 "To some degree it has," said Doug Heye, a former Republican congressional aide. "It has reawakened a lot of activism on the Democratic side."\par \par \uc2 But he said congressional advocacy groups have done a good job advising party members on how to respond with data that helped lawmakers understand where voters stand. "They saw the damage coming," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  on Tuesday launched a billboard campaign in battleground states linking Trump's statements about ending Roe v. Wade with the Alabama court ruling. The DNC is placing 40 billboards across Arizona, Florida, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen a lot of backpedaling from Republicans because it is dawning on them that their agenda is horribly unpopular with most Americans," Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Sen. Tammy Duckworth of Illinois said Tuesday that she would bring up her bill to protect in vitro fertilization services nationwide for a vote on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Even GOP lawmakers who have backed restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in pregnancy signaled that they still support in vitro fertilization after the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  ruling.\par \par \uc2 The court said last week that frozen embryos can be considered children under the state's Wrongful Death of a Minor Act, enacted in 1872, which allows parents to recover punitive damages in the event of a child's death. The case was brought by several couples whose embryos were destroyed when they were dropped.\par \par \uc2 The decision prompted several health clinics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/major-alabama-health-system-pauses-ivf-treatments-after-state-court-says-frozen-embryos-qualify-as-children-71ed704e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pause in vitro fertilization treatments  }}}\uc2  because the process can lead to destroying some embryos. Those embryos that aren't ultimately transferred into a uterus may be discarded or frozen.\par \par \uc2 Democratic voter groups and lawmakers have been calling out the more than 100 House Republicans who endorsed legislation last year that would have established life as beginning at conception, with no exception for in vitro fertilization. The Life at Conception Act sought to implement "equal protection right to life of each born and preborn human person, and pursuant to the duty and authority of the Congress," according to the legislation.\par \par \uc2 The House Majority PAC, which focuses on electing Democrats to the House, sent out online bulletins Monday identifying specific GOP candidates by name who supported the legislation and now say they support access to in vitro fertilization treatments.\par \par \uc2 "It shows how disconnected Republicans are from the American people and how they don't give a damn about some constituencies, particularly women," said Antjuan Seawright, a Democratic strategist. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
