\par \par \uc2 A lab at an IVF fertility center in Waltham, Mass. PHOTO: Kayana Szymczak for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already one of Republicans' biggest liabilities heading into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/on-debate-stage-and-campaign-trail-republicans-still-dont-know-how-to-talk-about-abortion-f70905e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November election  }}}\uc2 . A state court ruling that prompted some health clinics to halt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/alabama-supreme-court-embryo-ivf-uncertainty-88cf2146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in vitro fertilization treatments  }}}\uc2  this week is making it an even bigger problem for the party.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  ruled that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/major-alabama-health-system-pauses-ivf-treatments-after-state-court-says-frozen-embryos-qualify-as-children-71ed704e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frozen embryos  }}}\uc2  qualify as children and are therefore protected by a state law that allows parents to recover punitive damages in the event of a child's death. Because the process of in vitro fertilization can include destroying embryos, some IVF providers in the state said they were suspending the treatments because it may expose them to lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party has struggled to coalesce around an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance that appeals broadly to voters ever since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in 2022 and ended the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . State-level ballot measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access drove turnout in the midterms that year that favored Democrats, even in red states.\par \par \uc2 With polls showing strong support for fertility services such as in vitro fertilization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/republicans-confront-political-damage-from-alabama-ivf-ruling-f552988f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans risk losing voters  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14especially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-needs-white-suburban-women-his-indictment-splits-them-1a0a9e81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suburban women  }}}\uc2 , a key bloc for both parties\u8212\'20\'14as Democrats portray the Alabama ruling as extreme.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the GOP presidential front-runner, on Friday said he was calling on the Alabama legislature to find an immediate solution to preserve IVF access in the state.\par \par \uc2 "Under my leadership, the Republican party will always support the creation of strong, thriving, healthy American families," he said on Truth Social. "We want to make it easier for mothers and fathers to have babies, not harder! That includes supporting the availability of fertility treatments like IVF in every State in America."\par \par \uc2 The National Republican Senatorial Committee, which works to elect Republicans in the Senate, on Friday urged candidates to "clearly and concisely reject efforts by the government to restrict" in vitro fertilization, according to a memo from the committee's executive director Jason Thielman.\par \par \uc2 "When responding to the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  ruling, it is imperative that our candidates align with the public's overwhelming support for IVF and fertility treatments," the memo reads.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Nancy Mace (R., S.C.) said Republicans need to be more outspoken on the issue. Though Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-control-undecided-with-republicans-one-seat-shy-11668620031"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the House majority  }}}\uc2  in 2022, they did so with a narrow margin and Democrats were able to mobilize voters around resolutions to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "I'm going to file a resolution next week supporting protecting IVF access for women everywhere," Mace said in an interview. "In a year when we want to win women, we need to show them that we care."\par \par \uc2 GOP candidates seemed to be caught off guard in responding to the ruling. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley  }}}\uc2 , who is challenging Trump for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/nikki-haley-tries-to-hold-back-trump-onslaught-in-south-carolina-b144f4c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican presidential nomination  }}}\uc2 , told CNN on Wednesday that an embryo is an unborn baby. The former South Carolina governor later tempered her stance, saying Thursday on CNN that "we don't want fertility treatment to shut down."\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tim Scott of South Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/how-tim-scott-went-from-faith-in-america-to-leading-role-in-trumpworld-917c8dd0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a potential running mate  }}}\uc2  for Trump, said in a press conference and on CNN that "I haven't studied the issue."\par \par \uc2 In Alabama, House and Senate members are working on a legislative solution to preserve access to in-vitro fertilization services, and Republican Gov. \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  has signaled her support.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are seizing on the Alabama decision to turn up the heat on Republicans, portraying it as a genuine threat to in vitro fertilization. IVF accounts for some 2% of U.S. births.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , a Democrat, said he believes voters of both parties are "deeply offended" by the Alabama decision.\par \par \uc2 "I can't tell you how many of my friends\u8212\'20\'14but everyone's friends\u8212\'20\'14have needed IVF to start their families and how deeply personal it is to people to their hopes and their dreams," Beshear said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In his recent gubernatorial race, Beshear said that restrictions on abortions that barred victims of rape and incest from the procedure were deeply unpopular. He predicted voters would feel similarly about impeding IVF treatments.\par \par \uc2 "It's just a message of extremism," Beshear said. "Where some people have gone so far they're going to prevent you from having a family."\par \par \uc2 President Biden on Thursday derided the Alabama court decision as "outrageous and unacceptable" in a statement. His campaign on Friday pinned the blame on Trump, given he appointed justices that voted to overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are pointing to the ruling as fruition of their warning that the reversal of constitutional access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would limit fertility treatments.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tammy Duckworth (D., Ill.), who used IVF to have her two daughters, introduced legislation with Rep. Susan Wild (D., Pa.) last month that would establish a right to treatments including IVF.\par \par \uc2 The effort by GOP lawmakers to distance themselves from the ruling is a tricky balancing act because the decision has been widely praised by a number of prominent antiabortion groups whose support is also critical to Republican candidates.\par \par \uc2 Katie Daniel, state policy director for SBA Pro-Life America, said in a statement that "the Alabama Court recognized what is obvious and a scientific fact\u8212\'20\'14life begins at conception."\par \par \uc2 She said it doesn't mean a prohibition on fertility treatment, but it does mean treatments shouldn't "carelessly or intentionally destroy the new life created."\par \par \uc2 But some antiabortion groups disagree, saying it's unethical and immoral to carry out in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone is very thankful about the decision," said Judie Brown, president and co-founder of American Life League, a Catholic antiabortion group. "There should be no IVF. There never should have been. It's imposing science where the procreative gift should be from God."\par \par \uc2 Lila Rose, president and founder of Live Action, a national antiabortion organization, also supported the decision.\par \par \uc2 "IVF is morally fraught, the whole industry is fraught," she said, adding that lawsuits such as the one in Alabama are likely in other states. "This is not the way. It is opening up new frontiers to what has been allowed in our country. It's time for a reckoning."\par \par \uc2 Alabama is among 15 states that allow a cause of action for the wrongful death of an unborn child at any stage of development, according to an analysis of a similar Florida legislative proposal. Antiabortion groups could try to bring similar litigation that prevailed in Alabama in other states.\par \par \uc2 "It's the first time a court has said the logical extension of that applies even beyond pregnancy to embryos," said Greer Donley, an associate professor at the \uc2 University of Pittsburgh\uc2  law school. "This is an opportunity for some folks to use the same strategy state by state."\par \par \uc2 Some voters are concerned about the implications. Sara Abell, 59, of Owensboro, Ky., conceived her 30-year-old son using in vitro fertilization. The Democrat said she believes people will vote for candidates based on their stances on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fertility access.\par \par \uc2 "We're going backward to the pre-1950s," she said. "I did consider my embryos a life at that time. I got my son out of that. But I feel it's a personal choice for the woman."\par \par \uc2 Alex Leary, Siobhan Hughes and Katy Stech Ferek contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Stephanie Armour at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Stephanie.Armour@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie.Armour@wsj.com  }}}\uc2 , Annie Linskey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:annie.linskey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 annie.linskey@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Natalie Andrews at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240223ek2n005h9\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
