\par \par \uc2 Cyrena Martin says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is ready to serve as president if needed, but her concern is whether others would see that. PHOTO: Sara Stathas for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Maleah Wright, 28, of Spring Green, Wis., said she strongly favors a woman's right to choose, but she is planning to vote for a third-party candidate because she is worried about Biden. "Mentally, I'm not sure he's a fit president," she said. "If [Harris] has to step in, I think that she would do a fine job of holding office, but for four years as a president, I would have to say that I don't feel like she is ready," she added.\par \par \uc2 Harris, who is known to be extremely private, has been sharing more of her personal story in recent months. On her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights tour, Harris said she became a prosecutor after her best friend in high school told her she was being molested by her stepfather. As soon as she learned, Harris arranged for her friend to live with her family for several months.\par \par \uc2 "She was fighting for people's rights way back then," said that friend, Wanda Kagan, who lives in Montreal.\par \par \uc2 As a former district attorney of San Francisco and attorney general of California, Harris was involved in several legal battles on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including leading a multistate brief on the 2014 Supreme Court Hobby Lobby case on access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 Harris said in the interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-kamala-harriss-family-of-fighters-influenced-her-campaign-message-11572429601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her upbringing prepared her  }}}\uc2  to not shy away from talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly. She was raised by a mother who worked as a breast-cancer researcher and made women's \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  a frequent topic of conversation. "She was talking about hormones at the dinner table all the time," she said with a laugh.\par \par \uc2 Turning more serious, Harris added: "This stuff should not exist in the shadows. We don't talk about it and then people suffer, because women aren't supposed to talk about these things." \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich427\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6405
