\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Who's Radical on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Now? Wisconsin Democrats oppose restrictions even after 14 weeks.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 381 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 January 2024\par 22:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats have been winning elections running against a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Republicans have until recently been at a loss about how to respond. But a proposal by the GOP-controlled Legislature in Wisconsin bids to see if Democrats will accept a middle-ground consensus.\par \par \uc2 The GOP-run state Assembly on Thursday passed a bill (53-46) that would ban abortions after 14 weeks except in cases of rape, incest or to protect the health or life of the mother. If the bill becomes law, it would then go before the voters in an April referendum. Yet it took Democratic Gov. \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  milliseconds to announce he'd veto the proposal before Wisconsinites have a chance to decide for themselves.\par \par \uc2 In December Mr. Evers said his constituents should get to make reproductive decisions "without interference from politicians" and that he would "veto any bill" that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  less accessible. A Dane County judge ruled that an 1849 state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law doesn't apply and returned Wisconsin to the law that prevailed under Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Democrats want to keep exploiting the issue rather than reach a political and social consensus. They are ignoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reality and public opinion. According to the \uc2 Wisconsin Department of Health Services\uc2 , 54% of abortions obtained by Wisconsin residents in 2022 were in the first eight weeks of pregnancy. Another 22% were in weeks 9 or 10 and 10% in weeks 11 and 12. Only 14% of abortions were done between 13 and 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin GOP's bill is a compromise that a majority of voters nationwide say they want. A Gallup survey in July 2023 found that 51% of Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal but with restrictions. Two thirds said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in the first trimester (first 12 weeks) while only 37% said it should be legal in the second trimester.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats want to portray any restriction on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a total ban, and they want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal throughout pregnancy for any reason. Wisconsin Republicans were caught flat-footed by the repeal of Roe, but they're finally looking for compromise. Who's the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  radical now?\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240126ek1q006sh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
