\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Uses First 2024 Campaign Rally to Promote  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; Democrats see the issue as their most potent ahead of an expected tough race against Trump in November\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 894 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2024\par 23:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden campaigned on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at his first political rally of 2024, blasting former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the Supreme Court decision that eliminated the right to the procedure and calling on women to deliver him another term to protect access.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is betting you won't vote on this issue," Biden said at a rally in northern Virginia, looking to harness an issue that has energized Democrats since the 2022 ruling. "He's betting that you're going to stop caring, by the way, that you'll get distracted, discouraged, stay home."\par \par \uc2 Biden raised his voice as he added: "Well guess what? I'm betting he's wrong."\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke from a state where Democrats took control of the legislature in November, following a campaign that focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. He was joined by first lady Jill Biden, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her husband, Doug Emhoff. His speech was repeatedly interrupted by shouts from roughly a dozen protesters against Biden's support for Israel in the Gaza war.\par \par \uc2 The event came as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most polls show Biden }}}\uc2  tied or narrowly trailing in an expected rematch with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/new-hampshire-gop-primary-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces Republican primary voters }}}\uc2  in New Hampshire Tuesday and is the heavy favorite to win the party nomination. (The Democratic primary in New Hampshire is unsanctioned by the national party and Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/new-hampshire-gop-primary-election-2024/card/why-isn-t-biden-on-the-new-hampshire-ballot--rjbGIEr6zKpvHtJYTQIy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn't appear }}}\uc2  on the ballot, though there is a write-in effort supporting him.)\par \par \uc2 While Biden has at times been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-abortion-restrictions-supreme-court-mississippi-texas-11638024836"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reluctant messenger on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , he has embraced the argument that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is a freedom that has been stripped away by Republicans. And he has assailed Trump, who as president appointed three justices to the court that overturned the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 Trump has bragged about his role in overturning Roe, declaring at a recent Fox News town hall in Iowa: "I did it. I'm proud to have done it." Many Republicans have advocated for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Trump has avoided saying whether he would support a federal ban at a particular point in a pregnancy, and has criticized Republicans who he says take too hard a stance. "You have to win elections," he said at the Fox event.\par \par \uc2 Biden was introduced by Amanda Zurawski, a Texas woman who says she nearly died when she couldn't receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She spoke of her excitement at getting pregnant in 2022 after fertility treatment only to learn of "catastrophic" complications at 18 weeks.\par \par \uc2 "What I needed at that point was an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  so I could safely and with dignity deliver my daughter," she said. She said that only after a "near death crash into septic shock" that she got the procedure, adding: "What I went through was nothing short of barbaric and it didn't need to happen."\par \par \uc2 Biden hugged Zurawski when he came on stage before a crowd of women holding signs that read "Restore Roe" and "Defend Choice."\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the rally, the Republican Party of Virginia issued a statement, saying: "Democrats cynically believe that celebrating unrestricted late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -on-demand is the best way to appeal to voters. Republicans will continue to be advocates for mothers and children, including the unborn."\par \par \uc2 Biden's rally capped a flurry of events to mark this week's anniversary of the Roe decision, including a speech in Wisconsin by Harris. On Tuesday Harris attacked Republican lawmakers who have enacted restrictive laws in many states around the country, calling them extremists. She also cited women she had met who had miscarried in toilets and been turned away from emergency rooms.\par \par \uc2 "Across our nation, women are suffering. And let's be very clear about who is responsible," she said. "President Trump handpicked three Supreme Court justices because he intended for them to overturn Roe. He intended for them to take your freedom."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How significant do you think the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be in the 2024 campaign? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court ruling in June 2022 created a patchwork of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the U.S. and millions of women now live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is largely illegal. Over the weekend, Biden's campaign released an ad featuring Dr. Austin Dennard, a doctor based in Texas who says she had to leave the state to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a life-threatening pregnancy. The ad will play in battleground states and on national broadcast television during the season premiere of "The Bachelor."\par \par \uc2 For Democrats, who have struggled with Biden's low approval ratings and frustration over inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a clear rallying cry, bringing out voters in off-year elections around the country. The issue is particularly powerful in the types of suburban counties that were key in determining the results of the 2016 and 2020 races and will be crucial again in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Polling indicates most Americans favor some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May Gallup poll }}}\uc2 showed that 34% say it should be legal under any circumstances, 51% say it should be legal under "certain circumstances" and 13% say it should be illegal in all circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020240123ek1n002xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
