\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court to Decide on Access to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Mifepristone; Case is expected to be heard in 2024, keeping  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  in the spotlight during election year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin \par \uc2 748 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2023\par 19:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court said Wednesday it would decide a challenge to the federal regulations issued since 2016 that relaxed restrictions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-fresh-deadline-in-abortion-pill-case-6d7b9049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone  }}}\uc2 , ensuring the court's power over \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain in the forefront during a presidential election year.\par \par \uc2 A lower court invalidated those regulations, issued by the Food and Drug Administration , but they have remained in force while the justices weighed whether to hear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/biden-administration-asks-supreme-court-to-maintain-abortion-pill-access-69882ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Biden administration's appeal  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2022, a divided court rescinded the\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/roe-v-wade-is-gone-but-abortions-are-on-the-rise-383ffaf4?mod=series_scotusroe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  it first had recognized in the 1973 case, Roe v. Wade. Since then, the battle over women's rights to end unwanted pregnancies largely has played out in the states, with a minority of states, concentrated in the South, outlawing or sharply limiting the procedure, while voters elsewhere have surprised Republican lawmakers by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 buttressing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2  through ballot initiatives, most recently last month in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 The mifepristone case, however, has nationwide implications, because a loss for the Biden administration could curtail access to a widely used medication even in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \uc2 The suit against mifepristone was filed in an Amarillo, Texas, federal court last year by medical groups and doctors who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , challenging both the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's original approval of the drug in 2000 as well as more recent regulations easing the strict procedures initially required to obtain it.\par \par \uc2 They argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  improperly approved mifepristone under a pathway used to treat serious or life-threatening illnesses and failed to adequately consider potential safety concerns.\par \par \uc2 Original dispensing regulations limited mifepristone's use to the earliest weeks of pregnancy, required three doctors' visits to obtain, precluded mailing pills to patients and required a higher dosage than research later deemed effective.\par \par \uc2 In April, U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, who worked for a religious conservative advocacy group before former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed him to the bench in 2019, found that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's initial approval of mifepristone, as well as the more recent regulations, was invalid.\par \par \uc2 Upon the Biden administration's appeal, the Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, in New Orleans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/health/pharma/appeals-panel-rules-fda-improperly-expanded-access-to-abortion-pill-4ffbd3b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reinstated the 2000 approval  }}}\uc2 , but threw out the more recent \uc2 FDA\uc2  rules.\par \par \uc2 The White House welcomed the court's action Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit decision "threatens to undermine the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's scientific, independent judgment and would reimpose outdated restrictions on access to safe and effective medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  . "This administration will continue to stand by \uc2 FDA\uc2  's independent approval and regulation of mifepristone as safe and effective."\par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley, an attorney representing the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, which brought the suit, said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had eased access to mifepristone for political reasons.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has harmed the health of women and undermined the rule of law by illegally removing every meaningful safeguard from the chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug regimen," said Hawley, senior counsel of \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  , a Christian conservative advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 "Its removal of common-sense safeguards\u8212\'20\'14like a doctor's visit before women are prescribed chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs\u8212\'20\'14does not reflect scientific judgment but rather a politically driven decision to push a dangerous drug regimen," added Hawley, who is married to Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R., Mo.).\par \par \uc2 While agreeing to hear the government's appeal to reinstate the post-2016 regulations, the court turned down Hawley's petition asking the court to throw out the drug's initial 2000 approval.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone, sold under the brand name Mifeprex, is part of a two-step regimen. Up to two days after taking the drug, women usually take misoprostol, which causes uterine contractions. The lower-court orders don't affect misoprostol, which isn't \uc2 FDA\uc2  -approved for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own but could be prescribed off-label. Researchers say women seeking a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take misoprostol alone, but it is less effective and can cause more significant side effects.\par \par \uc2 The case, \uc2 FDA\uc2  v. Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, along with a companion appeal filed by Mifeprex maker Danco Laboratories, is expected to be argued in 2024 with a decision before July.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 FDA\uc2  actions at issue were well supported by extensive safety and effectiveness data from clinical trials and decades worth of real-world experience in millions of patients," Danco said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jess.Bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jess.Bravin@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231213ejcd003pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
