\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b \uc2 What the Supreme Court's Decision Means for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills; Medication  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  accounts for more than half of procedures nationwide\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dominique Mosbergen \par \uc2 1,668 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2023\par 23:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court said on Dec. 13 that it would weigh whether to limit access to mifepristone, a pill used in most abortions in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 In April, the Biden administration and Danco Laboratories LLC, which sells the drug under the brand name Mifeprex, had appealed a ruling by the Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals that would have significantly affected the way mifepristone is used and dispensed for abortions. The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-swift-new-abortion-test-with-mifepristone-case-b79b2a7e?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the lower court's order  }}}\uc2  while it decided whether or not to hear the case.\par \par \uc2 Oral arguments are expected to be scheduled in the coming months. It will be the court's most significant case involving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since its vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to overturn Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in the summer of 2022.\par \par \uc2 Some two dozen states have passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-and-texas-laws-roe-v-wade-leak-put-focus-on-abortion-access-11653587006?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans  }}}\uc2  or have severely restricted abortions in the aftermath of the Supreme Court decision. Several states remain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in legal battles  }}}\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 More patients have sought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/more-women-requesting-abortion-pills-outside-formal-channels-study-finds-11667316848?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -inducing drugs  }}}\uc2  from channels outside the formal medical system, including websites {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/websites-selling-unapproved-abortion-pills-are-booming-11661079601?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 selling unapproved medication  }}}\uc2 , since the overturning of Roe v. Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts said.\par \par \uc2 What happens to access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills now?\par \par \uc2 Access to mifepristone is unchanged for now in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed. U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk in Amarillo, Texas, ruled on April 7 to temporarily suspend the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 's approval of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit later blocked part of Judge Kacsmaryk's order and voted to retain \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone for abortions up to about seven weeks of pregnancy. The drug had previously been approved for use up to about 10 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The appellate court also rolled back other earlier efforts by the government to loosen access to mifepristone. Under the court's ruling, mifepristone couldn't be sent to patients through the mail and required three in-person doctor's visits.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts said the restrictions would significantly affect access to abortions. The Supreme Court suspended the Fifth Circuit's order in April, preserving the status quo of how mifepristone can be used and dispensed. That suspension will hold until the high court makes a decision on the case.\par \par \uc2 What is medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also known as medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or plan C, involves the administration of so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to terminate a pregnancy. Patients obtain the pills from a prescribing clinician or from online pharmacies and can take the medications in a clinical setting or at home.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-sue-fda-over-access-to-abortion-pill-f9f6b691"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved by the FDA  }}}\uc2  for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy. Though their efficacy decreases as gestational age increases, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills can be safe and effective beyond the 10-week mark, according to the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 . In some countries, including the U.K., \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are used to terminate pregnancies of up to 24 weeks. For later-term abortions, the pills are administered in clinical settings.\par \par \uc2 A two-drug regimen of mifepristone and misoprostol is the gold standard for safe and effective medication abortions, according to \uc2 ACOG\uc2 . Misoprostol alone can be used to terminate pregnancies and is an acceptable option if mifepristone is unavailable, \uc2 ACOG\uc2  said. The misoprostol-only regimen is less effective than the two-drug option, research shows.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, about 98% of medication abortions in the U.S. used the two-medication regimen of mifepristone and misoprostol, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 In the combination regimen, a single dose of mifepristone is followed by a course or several courses\u8212\'20\'14depending on the number of weeks of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14of misoprostol pills. The regimen is safe and highly effective, \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts say, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/evidence-you-can-use/medication-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efficacy rates of 95%  }}}\uc2  if administered at 10 weeks of pregnancy or earlier.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., mifepristone is sold under the brand name Mifeprex, manufactured by Danco Laboratories, a pharmaceutical distributor based in New York, and Korlym, made by Silicon Valley-based \uc2 Corcept Therapeutics\uc2 . Korlym isn't prescribed or marketed for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. and is approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  only for the treatment of Cushing's syndrome, a hormonal disorder. A generic version of the drug, also known as RU-486, was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2019 and is distributed by GenBioPro, a Nevada-based pharmaceutical company.\par \par \uc2 Costs for a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vary by state and aren't always covered by insurance. The combination regimen can cost up to $750, according to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . U.S. telehealth providers including Hey Jane and Just the Pill charge $350 or less for a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including pills and a medical consultation. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich427\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6405
