\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy. PHOTO: Taylor Glascock for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 What is a one-pill \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 A misoprostol-only regimen has been used internationally for decades and is considered safe and effective, though it has a lower rate of efficacy compared with the combination regimen, \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts said.\par \par \uc2 The misoprostol-only regimen has an efficacy rate of upward of 80% when administered during the first trimester of pregnancy, studies have shown.\par \par \uc2 About 0.7% of people using misoprostol alone to induce abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6309472/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were hospitalized  }}}\uc2  or received blood transfusions related to the procedures, according to a 2019 meta-analysis.\par \par \uc2 Patients take several doses of misoprostol to terminate a pregnancy. Side effects such as nausea, diarrhea and cramping can be more severe with the misoprostol-only regimen, compared with the two-medication regimen, physicians said.\par \par \uc2 Misoprostol is available as a generic drug and under the brand name Cytotec, which is manufactured by \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How common is the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, or medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for 54% of abortions in the U.S. in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . Since 2000, when the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone, a steadily increasing proportion of patients have chosen medication abortions. Some 37% of U.S. abortions were medication abortions in 2017, up from 14% in 2005.\par \par \uc2 How do \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills work? How long do they take to work?\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone blocks the hormone progesterone, which is needed to sustain a pregnancy. Misoprostol causes uterine contractions and bleeding. Physicians say the experience is similar to a miscarriage, and typically involves several hours of heavy bleeding and cramping.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
