\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas Judge Grants Pregnant Woman's Request for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; Kate Cox filed a lawsuit after learning that her fetus has a fatal chromosomal disorder\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,046 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 December 2023\par 22:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Texas judge granted an emergency request Thursday permitting a pregnant woman whose fetus has a fatal diagnosis to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers representing Kate Cox, a 31-year-old pregnant mother of two, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/Cox-v.-Texas-original-petition-FINAL-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit }}}\uc2  Tuesday asking the court to forbid Texas officials from prosecuting medical professionals who provide her with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case appears to be the first time a pregnant woman has sought court intervention to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in June 2022, leading {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen states }}}\uc2  to ban nearly all abortions.\par \par \uc2 It also comes as the Texas Supreme Court weighs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-women-denied-abortions-testify-about-impact-of-state-bans-999b8cff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a broader challenge }}}\uc2  that, if successful, would carve out a more robust medical exception for women across the state.\par \par \uc2 Cox, who is 20 weeks pregnant, learned last week her fetus has full trisomy 18, a chromosomal disorder with high miscarriage rates and little chance of survival after birth, according to the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Doctors informed \uc2 Cox\uc2  continuing the pregnancy would affect her health and fertility, the lawsuit said. The Texas mother has visited the emergency room several times during the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "The idea that Ms. Cox wants desperately to be a parent and this law might actually cause her to lose that ability is shocking and would be a genuine miscarriage of justice," Travis County District Judge Maya Guerra Gamble, a Democrat, said. Cox appeared to tear up as the judge spoke at the end of the virtual hearing Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Guerra Gamble said in the order that Cox qualified for a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under Texas' laws due to serious risk to her life, health and fertility. "The longer Ms. Cox stays pregnant," the judge wrote, "the greater risks to her life."\par \par \uc2 The temporary restraining order, or TRO, applies to Cox, her husband and her doctor, Damla Karsan, who would perform the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The lawsuit named all three as plaintiffs, seeking to protect them from liability under Texas laws.\par \par \uc2 Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , in a letter to hospitals where Karsan has admitting privileges, referred to Guerra Gamble as "an activist Travis County Judge" and threatened potential long-term implications if the hospitals allowed the procedure to be performed there.\par \par \uc2 "The temporary ruling fails to show that Dr. Karsan meets all of the elements necessary to fall within an exception to Texas' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws," Paxton wrote. "Judge Guerra Gamble is not medically qualified to make this determination and it should not be relied upon. A TRO is no substitute for medical judgment."\par \par \uc2 A representative for Paxton didn't respond to a request for comment. Johnathan Stone, a lawyer with the Texas attorney general's office, said during the hearing the plaintiffs haven't shown they would suffer "immediate and irreparable harm" without the emergency order.\par \par \uc2 Marc Hearron, senior counsel at the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Paxton is misrepresenting the court's order.\par \par \uc2 "He is trying to bulldoze the legal system to make sure Kate and pregnant women like her continue to suffer," Hearron said.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers representing Cox and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say Texas' overlapping civil and criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans leave limited options for pregnant patients managing medical complications.\par \par \uc2 While there are medical exceptions to bans, confusion remains over the details and scope that need clarification from the state, said \uc2 Molly Duane\uc2 , a lawyer from the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  representing Cox, during the hearing Thursday. This creates uncertainty for physicians about when abortions are allowed in medical emergencies, lawyers say.\par \par \uc2 "While we are grateful that Kate will be able to get this urgent medical care, it is unforgivable that she was forced to go to court to ask for it in the middle of a medical emergency," Duane said.\par \par \uc2 Duane declined after the decision Thursday to detail \uc2 Cox\uc2 's next steps for obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to safety concerns. The temporary restraining order expires in two weeks. "We are working with her to figure out the fastest way to get her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care," she said.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said stories such as Cox's "are becoming all too common" in Republican-led states following the Supreme Court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision last year }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "No woman should have to go to a court to get the healthcare that she needs," Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 Thirty-four abortions have been performed in Texas between January and July this year, according to data released in September by Texas Health and Human Services. More than 17,200 occurred in 2022, according to state data, with the vast majority occurring before more Texas restrictions took effect over that summer. More than 50,000 occurred in 2021, with the monthly number of abortions dropping by thousands beginning in September of that year after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a state law effectively banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy took effect.\par \par \uc2 Texas' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions don't hold pregnant women criminally or civilly liable. Doctors who perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in violation of the laws could face life in prison, a $100,000 fine for each violation and could lose their licenses. Enforced since 2021, a separate Texas law permits anyone to file lawsuits against clinics or anyone helping a patient get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In the broader court case challenging the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, plaintiffs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-women-denied-abortions-testify-about-impact-of-state-bans-999b8cff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said they suffered harrowing pregnancy complications }}}\uc2 , but their physicians told them their options were limited due to the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Women said they were forced to wait until their conditions deteriorated, travel out of state or carry nonviable fetuses to term.\par \par \uc2 A lower court blocked enforcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans against women facing serious pregnancy complications. The state attorney general's office appealed that ruling in August, and the Texas Supreme Court heard arguments in the case last week.\par \par \uc2 The Travis County judge's decision Thursday shows the unworkable standards created under these laws, said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, the dean of Temple University Beasley School of Law.\par \par \uc2 "It's further evidence that the law is not clear," Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 said.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231207ejc7005k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
