\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Tuberville's Hard Beltway Education; The Senator gives up his military promotion blockade in an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  fight he was always going to lose.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 323 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 December 2023\par 23:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Senate on Tuesday approved 425 U.S. military promotions, which usually wouldn't attract much attention. But Republican Tommy Tuberville had for months held these officers as hostages in a fight with the Biden Pentagon over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Give the Alabama Senator credit for relenting.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tuberville announced he'd release most of his holds, with the exception of a handful of four-star officers. Senate Democrats had been floating a procedural resolution to duck Sen. Tuberville's blockade, a risky precedent that could cramp every Senator's prerogatives to review nominees. That was an institutional outcome worth avoiding.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon was the aggressor and wrong on the merits of public financing for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In saner times the Biden Administration would have dropped its travel policy underwriting trips for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the Biden crowd is bloody-minded enough to subjugate military promotions to their culture-war priorities.\par \par \uc2 Yet that was also predictable. The Biden Administration will now declare victory on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because Mr. Tuberville blinked. Democrats will take military officers hostage en masse next time they don't like the priorities of a Republican President, and they will cite the Tuberville blockade as precedent.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tuberville was egged on by right-wing groups, which valorized him as a fighter for the sincerely held anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beliefs of much of the country. But Sen. Tuberville took a hill he couldn't hold, and the political damage compounded as more military officers became ensnared in the fight, unable to move their families or start new billets.\par \par \uc2 Don't be surprised if many Republican voters end up more cynical, having been promised a pro-life victory that was never attainable. The practical problem with scorched-earth political strategy is that it's usually more cathartic than successful.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231205ejc5006pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
