\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Tuberville's One-Man Stand Strains Senate Patience; Alabamian says blocking Pentagon nominees in protest of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  policy is just; foes say he's '100% wrong'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Molly Ball \par \uc2 1,878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2023\par 10:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 If anyone in Washington expects Sen. Tommy Tuberville to back down, he is here to dispel that idea.\par \par \uc2 "I hate to hold people hostage like this," the Alabama Republican says, sitting in a barren anteroom of his Capitol Hill office suite. "They have nothing to do with this. But what do you do? Do you fight for the Constitution?"\par \par \uc2 For nearly nine months now, Tuberville, a freshman senator and former football coach, has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/tommy-tuberville-goes-on-defense-over-hold-on-military-promotions-racial-comments-235c8ed2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single-handedly blocking }}}\uc2  Senate consideration of military promotions in protest of the Pentagon's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, a crusade that has earned him the enmity of many of his colleagues and left him increasingly isolated. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/News/Transcripts/Transcript/Article/3583055/deputy-pentagon-press-secretary-sabrina-singh-holds-an-on-camera-press-briefing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blockade has ballooned }}}\uc2  to include 452 officers, the department said last week\u8212\'20\'14more than half of the total number of generals and admirals in the Defense Department. The Army, Navy and Marines were for a time all without a confirmed top officer for the first time in history, even as the U.S. is supporting allies in two wars abroad.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville contends the Biden administration is to blame for the impasse. "It takes two people to get it done," he said. "I guess they think I would have broken by now."\par \par \uc2 Democrats and many Republicans accuse Tuberville of playing a dangerous game. Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  blamed him for damaging military readiness, hindering officer retention and "upending the lives of far too many American military families." Even his wife, Tuberville says, has confronted him about it. In an extraordinary scene on the Senate floor Nov. 1, his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/republican-senators-confront-tommy-tuberville-over-blocked-military-promotions-4c40c1ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP colleagues excoriated him }}}\uc2  in sharply personal terms. A Republican aide said they intend to do it again Monday if the situation isn't resolved.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville, whose father fought in World War II, seems pleased that recent events have drawn attention to his cause. "Nobody noticed early on," he said in his courtly Southern drawl. "Now that, you know, we're on the edge of another war in a different part of the world\u8230\'20\'26when you're tinkering around with the Pentagon, it made a little bit more sense of urgency."\par \par \uc2 The Nov. 1 floor session was a dramatic scene for the normally staid Senate. Over five hours of impassioned speeches, fewer than five of Tuberville's 48 Republican colleagues urged him to drop the holds. Several publicly berated him, saying their efforts to placate him in private had gotten nowhere and they were at their wits' end. They insulted his intelligence, questioned his integrity, accused him of imperiling national security and even implied he bore responsibility for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/tuberville-pushes-to-confirm-marines-no-2-after-commandant-hospitalized-feaade86"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent hospitalization }}}\uc2  of the Marine Corps commandant, Gen. Eric Smith. Before his apparent cardiac arrest on Oct. 29, Smith had complained about having to do two jobs as a result of the confirmation logjam.\par \par \uc2 "No matter whether you believe it or not, Senator Tuberville, this is doing great damage to our military," said Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.), an Air Force veteran.\par \par \uc2 "I am a pro-life woman. I am also a veteran and a combat veteran," said Sen. \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2  (R., Iowa), an Army veteran who serves in GOP leadership. "I continue to fight for life\u8212\'20\'14in ways that make sense."\par \par \uc2 Sen. Dan Sullivan (R., Alaska), a Marine Corps Reserve colonel, red-faced and yelling as the night wore on, declared himself "really frustrated" and called Tuberville "100% wrong."\par \par \uc2 As his colleagues got increasingly worked up, Tuberville remained at his desk in his bright-blue suit, his silver hair combed neatly back, taking the lashings in stride and evenly proclaiming after each name was put up for unanimous consent: "I object."\par \par \uc2 To hear Tuberville tell it, he didn't start this fight. Federal law has long prohibited military hospitals and health insurance from providing or covering abortions except in cases of rape, incest or the mother's life being at risk, meaning service members and their families must pay out of pocket and are subject to local laws for abortions that don't meet these criteria. (Then-Sen. Joe Biden voted for the 1984 codification of that restriction; before changing his position during his 2020 presidential campaign, Biden also supported the Hyde Amendment, which has prohibited the use of federal funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1976.)\par \par \uc2 After the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last year and several states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to restrict \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , Austin issued a memo directing the Defense Department to change its policies to facilitate travel for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by giving service members paid time off and travel reimbursement. Similar policies, where the government pays for travel but not the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself, have been allowed under Hyde for such cases as federal prisoners and Peace Corps volunteers. But Tuberville believed this improperly put taxpayers on the hook, violating the spirit if not the letter of Hyde. If such a change was to be made on such a controversial issue, he believed it should come from Congress, not the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How can Congress break Tuberville's stranglehold on military nominations and promotions? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 In December 2022, Tuberville fired off a letter to Austin threatening to hold up all of the department's civilian and general and flag officer nominees if it proceeded with the policy. This wasn't an unprecedented tactic: individual senators frequently use their ability to block nominations to get the attention of cabinet agencies they believe have overstepped. In January, for example, Sen. Michael Bennet (D., Colo.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defensenews.com/congress/2023/01/24/colorado-dem-threatens-to-hold-pentagon-nominees-over-space-command-hq/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to hold up nominations }}}\uc2  because Austin refused to meet with him to discuss the U.S. Space Command. In 2020, Sen. Tammy Duckworth (D., Ill.) also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.duckworth.senate.gov/news/press-releases/duckworth-announces-blanket-hold-on-senior-military-confirmations-following-reports-of-trumps-unprecedented-political-interference-into-military-promotion-process"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened a blanket hold }}}\uc2  unless then-Sec. \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2  confirmed he wouldn't interfere with the promotion of Lt. Col. Alexander Vindman, who had testified in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's first impeachment trial. In those and similar cases, the senators' questions were swiftly answered and the holds weren't imposed.\par \par \uc2 But in Tuberville's case, the Pentagon rebuffed him. And so, in February, Tuberville went through with his threat. Tuberville's holds could have been overcome through a series of procedural votes on each nomination, but Democratic Senate leadership argued that would eat up too much floor time and only validate Tuberville's tactic. The Pentagon, too, dug in. Austin and Tuberville have had three brief phone conversations on the issue, the last one in mid-July, but Tuberville says they have all consisted of one-sided harangues from the retired four-star general.\par \par \uc2 The Defense Department said that its engagement with Tuberville had been respectful but that the policy in question was legal and nonnegotiable. "Secretary Austin and the Department engaged Senator Tuberville and his office on multiple occasions in good faith and directly relayed how his holds on our general and flag officers have created risks to our military readiness and severely limit the Department's ability to ensure strategic and operational success," a Pentagon spokeswoman, Sabrina Singh, said.\par \par \uc2 The administration's refusal to come to the table, Tuberville argues, undercuts its claim that the holds have devastated the military. "This thing should have been done after a month, maybe even less than that," he said.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville, 69 years old, came to fame long before he entered politics as a superstar college football coach in the South, where football is like a religion and coaches have godlike status. He led \uc2 Auburn University\uc2 's Tigers to eight consecutive bowl appearances with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/senator-tommy-tuberville-military-blockade-angering-gop-1234868970/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 risk-taking style }}}\uc2 . He was also accused of disloyalty, repeatedly breaking his public word to take a new job or score a coveted recruit. In 1998, he famously declared he would only ever leave Ole Miss "in a pine box"\u8212\'20\'14only to be announced two days later as the Auburn coach without notifying his Ole Miss players or colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville said his time in the coaching spotlight was good preparation for his current position. "Listen, I've coached in front of 100,000 people before, and when we didn't play very well, half the stadium that was supposed to be on my side, they even didn't like me," he said. "I got called all kind of names, so that doesn't bother me." There have been times, he says, when his colleagues' criticisms and the stories of the military veterans have tugged on his heartstrings and made him search his soul, but he has always come back to his conviction that he's doing what's right.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville ran for Senate in 2020, taking on Trump's ex-attorney general, Jeff Sessions, who'd gotten crosswise with his former boss for his handling of the Russia investigation. In Tuberville's first campaign ad, he said, "God sent us \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because God knew we were in trouble." He refused to debate his opponents. With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-endorses-tommy-tuberville-over-jeff-sessions-in-alabama-gop-senate-race-11583895215"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump's backing }}}\uc2 , he easily defeated Sessions and the incumbent Democratic senator, \uc2 Doug Jones\uc2 . On Jan. 6, 2021, Tuberville's first full day in the Senate, he hid in a closet during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/jan-6-key-moments-leading-up-to-the-attack-on-the-capitol-11654796246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Capitol riot }}}\uc2 , then objected to certifying Biden's Electoral College victory. Tuberville has since become known for some head-scratching comments, such as misstating the three branches of government and seeming to defend white nationalists.\par \par \uc2 It is easy to see why his colleagues find Tuberville frustrating. Contrary to what you might expect, he's not a fire-and-brimstone type; rather, he is relentlessly amiable, conceding many of his opponents' arguments and sometimes contradicting himself, yet all the while standing firm. Some Republicans grouse he has undercut the GOP's traditional strength on national security while highlighting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/on-debate-stage-and-campaign-trail-republicans-still-dont-know-how-to-talk-about-abortion-f70905e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the party's unpopular position on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . His stand, they argue, is self-defeating, less likely to achieve his goal than to result in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/11/07/sinema-moves-to-defuse-tubervilles-holds-and-avoid-the-nuclear-option-00125573?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=0000015a-0e6e-dc8c-ab7a-7e7fb2270000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 change to Senate procedure }}}\uc2  that would weaken the minority's power.\par \par \uc2 But most Republicans are still with him, and Tuberville's allies believe he would have more leverage if they all united behind him. Sen. \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  (R., Utah) and Rep. Chip Roy (R., Tex.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chiproytx/status/1722115434579689877?s=42&t=4Hcg_xsPHNRk5AR8FJWBRA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blasted Sullivan on social media }}}\uc2  last week for being, in Roy's words, "focused on tearing down @SenTuberville\u8230\'20\'26while DOD refuses to follow the law." Conservative groups such as \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  have aired ads and erected billboards praising him back home, and both Trump and former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  have lauded him.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville has said there are compromises that would satisfy him, such as the creation of a private fund for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  travel. He plans to try to change the policy in the defense-funding bill that he will play a role in negotiating beginning this week. (The House's top Democratic negotiator, Rep. \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2 , responded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/11/09/dems-tuberville-abortion-defense-00126384"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to that possibility by saying }}}\uc2 , "No, screw him.") But all of the solutions Tuberville finds acceptable would require others to bend, not a concession on his part. Any compromise will only be on his terms.\par \par \uc2 "You can't change people's mind. There's no reason to try to do that," Tuberville said. "You've just got to take it."\par \par \uc2 Lindsay Wise and Nancy A. Youssef contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Molly Ball at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:molly.ball@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 molly.ball@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231113ejbd0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
