\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Supporters Rack Up Victories, Putting GOP in Bind for 2024; From red Ohio and Kentucky to purple Virginia and Pennsylvania, Tuesday's results show issue's continued potency\b0\par\par\uc2 By Aaron Zitner and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,547 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 03:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 They were disparate elections in different states\u8212\'20\'14for governor, state Senate, a supreme court seat and on a constitutional amendment. But the results of off-year races on Tuesday pointed in one direction: Voters will come to the polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to defend \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republican-debate-miami-what-to-expect-ab891722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican strongholds }}}\uc2  of Ohio and Kentucky, as well as politically purple Virginia and Pennsylvania, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters spent millions of dollars to tell voters that GOP lawmakers couldn't be trusted to set state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy after the Supreme Court last year\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated a right to the procedure }}}\uc2  under the U.S. Constitution.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-2023-gubernatorial-races-247b7d34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Those efforts worked }}}\uc2 , giving Democrats hopes that they can harness the issue once again in 2024 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/black-voters-show-signs-of-slipping-away-from-biden-in-2024-69ae78b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offset voter disenchantment }}}\uc2  with the economy and President Biden, who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/bidens-age-economic-worries-endanger-re-election-in-2024-wsj-poll-finds-67a7bba8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running for re-election }}}\uc2  with weak job-approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/support-for-abortion-access-is-near-record-wsj-norc-poll-finds-6021c712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an issue that motivates }}}\uc2  and turns out Democrats, and that advantage for them is not going to fade," said Tucker Martin, a longtime Republican political strategist in Virginia, where Democrats retained control of the state Senate and, in a substantial victory, gained control of the House.\par \par \uc2 The poor results were invoked during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/gop-republican-debate-miami"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican presidential debate }}}\uc2  Wednesday night in Miami. "I'm sick of Republicans losing," said Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Former United Nations Ambassador Nikki Haley said the GOP needed to do a better job trying to find consensus in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, including with supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights side did particularly well in the types of suburban counties that were key in determining the results of the 2016 and 2020 races and will be crucial again in 2024. And some Democrats were quick to point to Tuesday's results as evidence that the party was in solid shape and shouldn't fret so much about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/democrats-grow-more-confident-in-campaign-message-but-more-nervous-about-biden-dcd5cca6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden's personal unpopularity }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "What if\u8212\'20\'14and just hear me out for a second\u8212\'20\'14the Democratic brand and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have policies people actually like? And the way people voted last night is a reflection of both those things?" asked Jim Messina, who managed \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 's 2012 campaign, in a post on X.\par \par \uc2 The results also suggested that Republicans and antiabortion groups haven't yet found their footing on the issue, as Democrats have zeroed in on strict bans in some states to portray the other side as extreme. Tuesday's elections underscore that whether conservatives seek to paint themselves as compromising, push for tougher restrictions or try to avoid talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether, they continue to struggle when the issue is an electoral focal point.\par \par \uc2 In campaigning for Republican legislative candidates, Virginia GOP Gov. Glenn Youngkin had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/why-a-2023-virginia-election-is-a-proving-ground-for-2024-ae3bbbeb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for a ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after 15 weeks }}}\uc2  of pregnancy, rather than the state's current limit after 26 weeks\u8212\'20\'14an idea that is off the table now that Democrats will control both legislative chambers. He and national antiabortion leaders had hoped Tuesday's contests would show that Youngkin's proposal, which they are promoting as a compromise position, would appeal to moderate voters.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, voters approved an amendment to the state constitution protecting access to the procedure until the fetus can live outside the womb, generally at about 23 weeks of pregnancy. The decision was a rebuke to Republicans in the state legislature and GOP Gov. \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 . The governor in 2019 signed a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy, which has been blocked in court for most of the past year.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Democrat Daniel McCaffery won a state Supreme Court seat, after running ads promising to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and voting rights. His win over Republican Carolyn Carluccio fortifies the existing Democratic majority on a court that decided important cases about voting access before the 2020 election in the nation's biggest presidential swing state.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, a state that former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won twice by more than 25 percentage points, voters re-elected Democratic Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  and rejected Republican Attorney General \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , who supports the state's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kentucky-legislature-overrides-governors-veto-passes-abortion-restrictions-11649896715"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 . }}}\uc2  Beshear had run {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/kentucky-governors-race-offers-test-can-a-popular-democratic-incumbent-win-in-trump-country-15c93d29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the sharpest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related ads }}}\uc2  of the year, featuring a young woman who says she was raped by her stepfather at age 12.\par \par \uc2 "This is to you, \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 ,'' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hRYVgGKdtxE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she says }}}\uc2  to the camera. "To tell a 12-year-old girl she must have the baby of her stepfather who raped her is unthinkable."\par \par \uc2 Cameron had at times indicated support for adding exceptions for rape and incest to the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Trey Grayson, a Republican and former Kentucky secretary of state, said Cameron's policy shift showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had become a factor in the election, as did the fact that Beshear highlighted the issue. "In the past, Democrats didn't talk much about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  last June, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have scored {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/the-abortion-rights-movement-is-on-a-winning-streak-will-ohio-stop-it-4c13d41f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a string of victories }}}\uc2  in states as wide-ranging as Kansas, Kentucky, Michigan and Wisconsin. The issue also helped bolster Democratic fortunes in last year's midterm elections in gubernatorial races in Arizona and Michigan, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a central point of division between the candidates, as well as in congressional races.\par \par \uc2 The victory in Ohio is likely to create new momentum behind efforts to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot in 2024 in states including Arizona, Florida, Nevada and Nebraska. That could help boost turnout by Democratic voters in places that could be key battlegrounds in the presidential election and other races.\par \par \uc2 The two parties will look for clues in Tuesday's results for how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  might affect the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 The results from some states suggested that voters in upper-income suburbs outside big cities, who often lean Republican, are eager to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, for example, close to 60% of voters in Delaware County, just outside Columbus, backed the constitutional amendment protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\u8212\'20\'14substantially more than the 53% who backed Trump in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Mike Madrid, a Republican political consultant based in California, said that many of these voters, particularly women, were leaving the GOP.\par \par \uc2 "The tendency of college-educated, suburban Republican women to vote Democratic is now more likely than less likely," he said. "Not all of them, but significant numbers. There is a very critical part of the Republican coalition that appears to be leaving permanently on cultural issues."\par \par \uc2 Outside Richmond, Va., a Republican senator lost her seat to a Democrat after campaigning in favor of a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Democrats also won a competitive Senate race in the Virginia suburbs outside Washington, D.C., in which their candidate promised to prevent a rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Polling also showed that support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights crossed party lines. In Ohio, a survey of election voters, conducted for news organizations, found that about 20% of Trump voters backed the constitutional amendment. By contrast, 8% of voters who had backed Biden in 2020 opposed the amendment.\par \par \uc2 While those voters may stick with their party's nominees in the next presidential election, the survey surfaced a warning sign for the GOP: Nearly half of voters said they trusted the Democratic Party more to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , compared with 42% who trusted the GOP more. At the same time, voters trusted the Republican Party more on the economy.\par \par \uc2 The challenging terrain of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has prompted Trump to leave his intentions unclear. He often highlights the fact that his Supreme Court nominees helped overturn Roe v. Wade, but he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-takes-heat-from-religious-conservatives-for-softness-on-abortion-bans-c856397b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hasn't endorsed a national law }}}\uc2  banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point in pregnancy, as some antiabortion groups have pushed him to do.\par \par \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2  of the Democratic voter data firm TargetSmart said Tuesday's results showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could boost Biden's re-election effort, which has drawn muted enthusiasm from voters. Polls show overwhelmingly that voters are worried about the president's age and effectiveness.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are your biggest takeaways from Tuesday's elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "What you're seeing in these limited results is that the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has actually grown in saliency. People have had more than a year to live with the Dobbs decision," Bonier said, referring to the Supreme Court case that overturned Roe v. Wade, "and the lived reality is more stark and more impactful than anyone had anticipated."\par \par \uc2 He said election results since the decision showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could motivate those Democratic voters who so far have been unengaged, while also winning over "some number of Trump voters."\par \par \uc2 Martin, the Virginia Republican, said that while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a powerful issue, it might not be the most powerful by Election Day next year. "Every election is different in the hierarchy of issues that matter to voters," he said. "When we get to the presidential election, with the world in its current state, it might be foreign policy. It might be the economy. No one can tell you what the top issue in 2024 will be."\par \par \uc2 Write to Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231108ejb8001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
