\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 On Debate Stage and Campaign Trail, Republicans Still Don't Know How to Talk About  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; Tuesday's resounding  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -rights victories left GOP candidates grasping for a position they could sell to voters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Molly Ball \par \uc2 1,045 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2023\par 10:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 For a change, the central problem facing the candidates in Wednesday night's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/gop-debate-takeaways-haley-takes-fire-as-she-jockeys-for-second-place-27ee6cb0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican debate }}}\uc2  wasn't necessarily \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14yet the men and woman who would be president had little better idea how to solve it.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's off-year election offered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-supporters-rack-up-victories-putting-gop-in-bind-for-2024-4bec7b38?mod=hp_trending_now_article_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating new evidence }}}\uc2  of the unpopularity of the Republican Party's positioning on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yet even as the party collectively reeled from this setback, with lawmakers and operatives squabbling over how to move forward, the party's presidential candidates struggled to offer an alternative approach. Taken together, their responses on the issue were a revealing glimpse into the dilemma vexing the GOP after a series of bruising election losses.\par \par \uc2 Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said he was "sick of Republicans losing" and pointed to campaign strategy as an explanation for Tuesday's result. The antiabortion movement, he argued, had been "caught flat-footed on these referendums" such as the one voters approved Tuesday that inserted a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the Ohio constitution. Earlier this year, DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2  that caused some influential Republicans to question his viability in a national campaign. After initially avoiding a position on a federal ban, he has said he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-republicans-desantis-trump-bdccde60987da99018bf3abcbafedea0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support a 15-week national limit }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Businessman \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who lives in Ohio, said he was "upset" by Tuesday's outcome and lamented Republicans becoming a "party of losers." He said that Republicans should be promoting "sexual responsibility for men" through paternity tests, apparently arguing that voters who rejected government control over women's bodies would like it better if applied to both genders.\par \par \uc2 Former United Nations Ambassador Nikki Haley, the only woman in the field, argued that Republicans should "stop the judgment" and "focus on how to save as many babies as we can." Repeating a point she had made in previous debates, she said it was disingenuous to promise voters further restrictions that won't get through Congress. "Don't make the American people think we're going to push something on them when we don't even have the votes in the Senate," she said. Haley proclaimed herself "unapologetically pro-life" and said she would sign whatever restrictions Congress could pass, but she didn't say what she would personally favor as a hypothetical federal limit.\par \par \uc2 Former New Jersey Gov. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  made a similar argument on different grounds, saying states should make their own policies and the federal government should stay out of it.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Sen. Tim Scott had the most concrete stance in terms of federal policy, arguing for a "15-week national limit" and contending that 75% of Americans would agree. But it was just such a stance that Virginia voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-2023-gubernatorial-races-247b7d34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to reject }}}\uc2  on Tuesday\u8212\'20\'14and Haley fired back by pointing out that Scott didn't initially support a 15-week federal ban proposed last year by his fellow South Carolina senator, \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The collective evasion only intensified the feeling of unreality that has pervaded this year's debates for the Republican nomination, in which also-rans have bickered while the front-runner, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , steadily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/gop-republican-debate-miami/card/trump-defends-choice-to-skip-debate-NKUkmfWPhKDkfXk6mQ5F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 builds a double-digit lead in absentia }}}\uc2 . Trump, for his part, didn't mention \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the rally he held not far from the debate site, though his son's fianc\u233\'00\'E9e, Kimberly Guilfoyle, praised him in her introduction for having "stood for the unborn."\par \par \uc2 Trump has alternated between taking credit for the Supreme Court decision overturning Roe v. Wade and expressing discomfort with states' moves to restrict the procedure. He has called DeSantis's six-week ban "too harsh" and "a terrible mistake" without articulating a clear position of his own, yet has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/gop-republican-debate-miami/card/trump-defends-choice-to-skip-debate-NKUkmfWPhKDkfXk6mQ5F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawn only scattered criticism }}}\uc2  from the antiabortion activist groups that have traditionally been major Republican power brokers.\par \par \uc2 The fallout from the elections reverberated across Washington Wednesday. In addition to the Ohio referendum, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-supporters-rack-up-victories-putting-gop-in-bind-for-2024-4bec7b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans fell short of their hopes }}}\uc2  in state races in Kentucky and Virginia in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a central theme of the campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Sen. J.D. Vance (R., Ohio) said on social media that the result in Ohio was "a gut punch." Sen. \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  (R., N.C.) said states such as Ohio "need to get on board with where their constituents are." Rep. Marcus Molinaro (R., N.Y.) said that in the wake of the Supreme Court decision, "the American people want every level of government to more appropriately respect the difficult choices women have to make."\par \par \uc2 The party's Senate campaign arm planned to push candidates on next year's ballot to campaign vocally against a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, articulating the position in speeches and campaign ads, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/republicans-urge-congress-candidates-oppose-national-abortion-ban-rcna124253"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported }}}\uc2 . GOP Senators were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/senate-republicans-seek-winning-path-on-abortion-restrictions-175d3eab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefed on the issue in September }}}\uc2  but no consensus policy position emerged.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Can any of the Republican candidates devise a winning message on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue in 2024? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 On some level, the lack of willingness to confront the issue in the debate was understandable. Primary campaigns tend to be more about feeding red meat to the base\u8212\'20\'14which in Republicans' case is strongly against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14than reaching general election voters. The moderators, who only brought up the topic in a brief segment just before the debate's end, were at least as responsible as the candidates for the lack of emphasis on it. Haley has previously broached the topic as part of her broader electability argument, yet Iowa caucus-goers have generally rewarded hard-core social conservatives who take strong positions against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Where the party will land is anybody's guess. Given Trump's lead in the primary polls, the internal debate may be irrelevant. His tendency is to seem to endorse several sides of an issue simultaneously, allowing voters to hear what they want to hear. It appears likely that different wings of the party will continue to quarrel over the issue\u8212\'20\'14while Democrats sit back and relish the fight.\par \par \uc2 Lindsay Wise and Jennifer Calfas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Molly Ball at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:molly.ball@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 molly.ball@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231109ejb9002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
