\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democratic Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  Re-Elected in Kentucky, and Democrats Have Big Night in Virginia; Elections around the U.S. gave the nation an early read on the electorate ahead of 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 By Scott Calvert, Arian Campo-Flores and Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 1,415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2023\par 06:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  won re-election in Kentucky, beating back a strong challenge from his Republican opponent in a deeply conservative state\u8212\'20\'14despite efforts by the GOP to yoke him to President Biden's sagging approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Virginia, the Democratic Party's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights message {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-supporters-rack-up-victories-putting-gop-in-bind-for-2024-4bec7b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fueled victories }}}\uc2  that gave it full control of the legislature in Richmond. Together with Beshear's victory, which showed Democrats can find strength in Trump country, the results gave an early read on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/why-a-2023-virginia-election-is-a-proving-ground-for-2024-ae3bbbeb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electorate's mood }}}\uc2  heading into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/presidential-election-2024-candidates-dates-guide-a264d4fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 presidential campaign. }}}\par \par \uc2 "We have thwarted MAGA Republicans' attempt to take total control of our government and our bodies," said Virginia Sen. Mamie Locke, who chairs the Democratic Caucus.\par \par \uc2 Virginia Democrats captured the 21 seats needed to retain its state Senate majority, according to a Wall Street Journal tally of races called by the AP, and they won the 51 seats needed to wrest the majority from Republicans in the House of Delegates.\par \par \uc2 The results signaled the party's message on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still a winner. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also on the ballot in Ohio, where voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved a measure to enshrine \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  in the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, in New Jersey, another state where the parties battled for control of the state legislature, a Democratic incumbent held a key district and the party was on track to keeping its statehouse majority. And in a widely expected outcome, Mississippi's Republican Gov. \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  defeated Democrat Brandon Presley, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-governors-race-expected-to-pit-incumbent-republican-against-elvis-relative-bd485171"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distant cousin of Elvis }}}\uc2  Presley, the AP projected.\par \par \uc2 The Virginia races were closely watched because a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/republican-debate-miami-what-to-expect-ab891722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican-led }}}\uc2  legislature would have enabled Gov. Glenn Youngkin, who some GOP donors hope will make a late, long-shot entry into the party's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/the-2024-election-rematch-americans-are-dreading-looks-likely-c89a6630"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 presidential nominating }}}\uc2  contest, to pass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/glenn-youngkins-effort-to-reshape-virginias-schools-is-off-to-modest-start-1efbadb3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative policies }}}\uc2  in areas such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , taxes and education.\par \par \uc2 Democrats made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access their top issue, campaigning in support of existing state law that allows the procedure until around 26 weeks. Republicans embraced Youngkin's call for a ban on the procedure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/can-glenn-youngkin-pull-off-another-magic-trick-in-virginia-d94f6a44"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after 15 weeks, }}}\uc2  with exceptions for rape, incest or to protect the mother's life, while painting Democrats as soft on crime and out of touch with parents on education policy.\par \par \uc2 "This was an election about choice," said Democratic political consultant Ben Tribbett. He said Democrats had focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access ever since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in June 2022. Youngkin's effort to change the conversation by highlighting his proposed 15-week ban backfired, Tribbett said, adding: "He was talking about an issue that really favored us."\par \par \uc2 Republican pollster Robert Cahaly said he thought the Democrats' message was effective because the party's candidates consistently characterized it as a ban.\par \par \uc2 "You hear the word 'ban,' 'ban,' 'ban,'" said Cahaly, who polled for Youngkin in 2021. "Republicans have got to learn to articulate this better. And the problem is the Democrats are very good at spinning it and putting their money where their mouth is."\par \par \uc2 Still, Cahaly said he didn't think failing to win a trifecta in Richmond would tarnish Youngkin's political future, even though the governor campaigned hard for Republicans across the state. "It's a minor setback," he said.\par \par \uc2 While Republicans ran on other issues like the economy, Youngkin had hoped to show the party how to win on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  message. "We wanted to be really clear that I support a bill to protect life at 15 weeks," Youngkin told CNN on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In the run-up to Tuesday's elections, several suburban districts emerged as battlegrounds, including a Senate district in southeastern Virginia that includes Williamsburg and Yorktown.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about GOP efforts to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access motivated Les McCorkle of Williamsburg, a self-described independent voter, to cast a ballot for Democratic Sen. T. Montgomery "Monty" Mason, who was seeking re-election in the closely watched race.\par \par \uc2 "It should be a woman's right. It's her body," said McCorkle, a retired Army command sergeant major. The 61-year-old said the 15-week limit backed by Republicans would be overly restrictive.\par \par \uc2 Registered Republican Teresa Woodward, who voted for Mason's Republican challenger, former Sheriff J.D. "Danny" Diggs, said GOP calls for a 15-week ban represented a reasonable compromise. And at any rate, for Woodward, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranks below other concerns like crime and the economy.\par \par \uc2 "We're all struggling right now," said Woodward, 42, who lives in Yorktown and owns a contracting business with her husband. "Any tax that can be lowered is obviously appreciated."\par \par \uc2 As of about 1 a.m. Eastern, the race between Diggs and Mason was too close to call.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-governor-race-is-still-too-close-to-call-11635940355"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey, Republicans }}}\uc2  were hoping for a repeat of a 2021 red wave that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/articles/the-big-new-jersey-election-upset-a-truck-driver-beats-steve-sweeney-11636063518"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swept former }}}\uc2  Democratic State Senate President \uc2 Steve Sweeney\uc2  out of office. Going into Tuesday, Democrats held a 25-15 majority in the Senate and a 46-34 majority in the General Assembly.\par \par \uc2 GOP candidates campaigned against recently adopted sexual-education learning standards and Democratic Gov. \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 's support of offshore wind development. Energy company \u216\'00\'D8rsted last month canceled plans for the state's first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/energy-oil/americas-offshore-wind-ambitions-are-coming-with-bigger-price-tags-95693495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offshore wind farm, }}}\uc2  citing higher costs.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What hints about the 2024 elections are you watching for during Election Day 2023? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Democratic incumbent Sen. Vin Gopal won re-election despite relentless GOP attacks about wind energy and sex education. Gopal and other Democrats have emphasized their support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and several property-tax relief programs.\par \par \uc2 Ashley Koning, director of the Eagleton Center for Public Interest Polling at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2 , said a survey taken over the weekend showed 40% of voters named economic concerns as their top issue.\par \par \uc2 "It tells us that even if we're hearing these loud voices or anecdotal voices\u8212\'20\'14and even if they're coming across as the strongest thread of an election cycle\u8212\'20\'14it doesn't mean they're representative of the electorate as a whole," she said.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, Beshear, 45, faced \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2 , the state's first Black attorney general and a rising GOP star. The AP projected Beshear had won; Cameron conceded in a Tuesday night speech.\par \par \uc2 Beshear went after Cameron on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, criticizing him for supporting current law in the state that bans virtually all abortions. The Democrat ran an ad that went viral featuring a woman who was raped as a 12-year-old and asserted that Cameron would force someone in that situation to have the baby. Cameron seemed to modify his position during the campaign, saying he would sign a bill with rape and incest exceptions if it passed the legislature.\par \par \uc2 "It was a victory that sends a loud, clear message, a message that candidates should run for something and not against someone," Beshear said at his election party in Louisville.\par \par \uc2 Recent polling showed the race tightening to a dead heat, after a string of surveys this year gave Beshear an edge. Beshear\u8212\'20\'14whose father, Steve Beshear, was a popular two-term Democratic governor from 2007 to 2015\u8212\'20\'14benefited from a bigger campaign war chest and a spending advantage on the airwaves. He pitched himself to voters as a moderate who is focused on all Kentuckians' needs, regardless of party, and who presided over a period of strong economic performance.\par \par \uc2 Cameron challenged that image, casting Beshear as a liberal extremist allied with President Biden and out of touch with Kentucky values. Boosting Cameron's chances were Republicans' voter-registration advantage, which they gained for the first time last year, and his endorsement by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is more popular in Kentucky than Biden.\par \par \uc2 In a contentious campaign in Mississippi, Reeves and Presley presented sharply different views of the state's economy. Reeves said that the state of about three million people was on the upswing with record-low unemployment. Presley said the state government had ignored the needs of the poor and middle class while Republican leaders have been embroiled in scandals. The GOP has held the Mississippi governor's office continuously since 2004.\par \par \uc2 Jack Gillum and Cameron McWhirter contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Scott Calvert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.calvert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.calvert@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Arian Campo-Flores at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:arian.campo-flores@dowjones.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arian.campo-flores@dowjones.com }}}\uc2  and Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jimmy.vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jimmy.vielkind@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231107ejb70025x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
