\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 The 2024 Election Rematch Americans Are Dreading Looks Likely; One year before voting, a weakened Biden and a criminally indicted Trump appear to be on a collision course\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Thomas, Catherine Lucey and John McCormick \par \uc2 1,969 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2023\par 16:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A year before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/presidential-election-2024-candidates-dates-guide-a264d4fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2024 election}}}\uc2 , a divided nation is stuck in a political loop: President Trump's weaknesses helped deliver President Biden to the White House, and now the incumbent's vulnerabilities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/bidens-2024-challenge-taking-down-trumps-poll-numbers-9cb9076e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could lead his predecessor to a comeback}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden, the nation's oldest president at age 80, is poised to reclaim the party's nomination, yet he has been dogged with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/is-biden-too-old-to-run-again-we-asked-people-born-on-his-exact-birthday-476bdff3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questions about his age}}}\uc2 , frustration over his handling of the economy and anxiety about two wars. Trump, 77, has a comfortable lead as he seeks the Republican nomination for a third time, even as many moderate and independent voters are repelled by his repeated efforts to overturn the 2020 elections results and the many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/a-guide-to-donald-trumps-legal-perils-b9b64891"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal indictments he faces}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two are likely headed for a general election rematch that will unfold against a backdrop of discontent, pitting two unpopular candidates against each other on inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and America's role in an unstable world. Given the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-2023-gubernatorial-races-247b7d34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowly divided electorate}}}\uc2 , the outcome will hinge on a small slice of voters spread across a half dozen or so states, with the possibility of multiple independent or third-party candidates scrambling the results.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Don Bacon\uc2 , a Nebraska Republican who represents a closely divided Omaha-based district, said he believed that in 2020, "a lot of people didn't vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , they voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 This time around, he said, "I think the same issues that challenged Trump in our district are still there. People don't like the name-calling, they want order." But he added: "The difference this time is people are unhappy with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's performance."\par \par \uc2 A poll released this past week from \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2  showed the two men {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3881"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essentially tied in a hypothetical matchup}}}\uc2 , with 47% of registered voters supporting Biden and 46% backing Trump. The perennial question is where independent voters, who are evenly split in the poll, land.\par \par \uc2 A series of polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/11/05/us/elections/times-siena-battlegrounds-registered-voters.html?unlocked_article_code=1.8Ew.PEVT.yLDez68a2s5k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released Sunday}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College showed Biden trailing Trump among registered voters in five of the six swing states they surveyed. The polls found voters said, by a wide margin, that Trump's policies as president helped them more than Biden's did, and that majorities in every demographic group thought Biden was "too old" to be president.\par \par \uc2 The race would be one for the history books\u8212\'20\'14the first rematch of major party nominees since the 1950s. If Biden and Trump again lead their party's tickets, the contest would feature the nation's oldest president against the nation's second-oldest president. If Trump prevails, he would become the first former president to reclaim the White House since Grover Cleveland in 1892.\par \par \uc2 Many say this is a sequel they could do without.\par \par \uc2 "I feel very sad that that's the best we can do," said Cindy Roth, 64, a retired Republican from Morton, Pa., a state won by Trump in 2016 and Biden in 2020. "I would love to see younger people."\par \par \uc2 Trump's 2020 fixation\par \par \uc2 Even as he dominates the Republican field, Trump faces a number of hurdles as he looks to the general election. He continues to claim falsely that the 2020 election was stolen from him\u8212\'20\'14assertions he made to his supporters leading up to the attack on the U.S. Capitol on Jan. 6, 2021.\par \par \uc2 Polls show a majority of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/03/politics/cnn-poll-republicans-think-2020-election-illegitimate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans don't view Biden's election}}}\uc2  as legitimate, raising the prospect that the 2024 results could again be disputed. Yet polls and the results of the 2022 midterm elections\u8212\'20\'14in which several high-profile Trump-backed candidates lost\u8212\'20\'14indicate that many swing voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-election-grand-jury-georgia-voters-4cd64c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are tired of his claims about 2020}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We've never had an election like this. We had the 2020 election and it never ended," said Democratic pollster Jeff Horwitt. "Usually the loser of the election goes away. That has never happened. Usually their supporters take some time and move on. That has never happened."\par \par \uc2 While Trump has a massive polling lead over the GOP field, he is trying to make his nomination inevitable. The former president has been taking constant shots at his two closest competitors, Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and former South Carolina Gov. Nikki Haley. His team is looking to score decisive wins in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/in-first-state-for-gop-presidential-voting-the-race-is-on-for-second-place-e5b87464"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early Republican contests}}}\uc2  in Iowa and New Hampshire, hoping to lock up the nomination by "Super Tuesday" in early March, when more than a dozen states will hold contests.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, who has heavily focused his campaign on the Jan. 15 Iowa caucuses, is expected to formally receive the endorsement of Iowa Gov. \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  at an event in Des Moines on Monday, according to a person familiar with the matter. The endorsement was first reported by NBC News and the Des Moines Register.\par \par \uc2 Trump's campaign responded with a statement suggesting Reynolds has "begun her retirement tour early as she clearly does not have any ambition for higher office" after the endorsement. "Her endorsement will not make any difference in this race," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Trump's allies have called for all other candidates to quit and unite behind him, as a show of party support against his onslaught of legal problems, which include a civil fraud trial and four criminal indictments. Charges against the former president include attempting to overturn his 2020 election loss in Georgia, civil fraud in New York, his handling of classified documents in Florida and a federal trial in Washington, D.C., for election interference.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are you watching for as the 2024 campaigns intensify? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Trump will have to spend time in various courtrooms next year, away from the campaign trail, complicating his pitch to voters. For example, Trump faces a March 4 trial date\u8212\'20\'14the day before Super Tuesday\u8212\'20\'14in the federal case in Washington, D.C., over charges that he tried to overturn the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 Trump's advisers want to remind people about the economy during his term, which reached historic milestones for jobs, income and stock prices until the Covid-19 pandemic hit in March 2020 and sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/UNRATE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unemployment to historic highs}}}\uc2 . While they acknowledge Trump's court cases are a drag on his time, they think Trump has a unique ability to turn out infrequent voters.\par \par \uc2 Nevada-based GOP strategist Zachary Moyle said many voters would see a rematch between Biden and Trump as one forcing them to pick "the lesser of two evils" and thus creating a turnout challenge for both parties.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also sought to target Biden's age and fitness for office, mocking his walk and speaking style.\par \par \uc2 Charles Franklin, director of a state and national poll conducted by Marquette Law School in Milwaukee, said there has been a very deliberate\u8212\'20\'14and effective\u8212\'20\'14messaging strategy from Republicans almost from the moment Biden was elected that he's too old for the job. "Every poll I've done that asks about age finds twice as many people saying Biden is too old than saying Trump is too old," he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden's age problem\par \par \uc2 Biden will enter the general election with the backing of party leaders, but as surveys show a majority of voters, including large numbers of Democrats, urging him not to seek re-election. His age and calls for a new generation of leadership are at the heart of a long-shot primary challenge by Rep. \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  (D., Minn.), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/in-running-against-biden-dean-phillips-seeks-to-tap-democrats-unease-with-an-elderly-president-d11968db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who filed for the New Hampshire ballot}}}\uc2  late last month.\par \par \uc2 Biden will need to reassemble the diverse coalition of voters that elected him in 2020 and make a proactive case that his first-term agenda has led the nation out of the Covid-19 pandemic into a strong economy.\par \par \uc2 Biden officials contend that the eventual Republican nominee will be forced to take unpopular positions on taxes, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Social Security and Medicare in order to placate the party's MAGA base. In particular, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, which helped power Democratic victories in 2022 following the Supreme Court decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating a constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , could again prove energizing for Democrats and some women.\par \par \uc2 "No matter who emerges from the field, the toxicity of these positions will be difficult to overcome with the voters who will decide this election," wrote Julie Chavez Rodriguez, Biden's campaign manager, in a memo released Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump are expected to fight for the same battleground states that decided the 2020 election: Arizona, Michigan, Georgia, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, all of which were won by Trump in 2016 and Biden in 2020. North Carolina and Nevada also are seen as competitive by both parties.\par \par \uc2 Biden and his allies started advertising far earlier than President Obama did when he was running for re-election in 2012, according to ad tracker AdImpact. Democrats started in April of this year, roughly nine months earlier than in the 2012 cycle, and their ads have so far played most frequently in Pennsylvania, Arizona and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Biden's team believes he will ultimately get credit for a string of legislative accomplishments, including a $1 trillion infrastructure measure and new laws promoting the development of semiconductors and climate projects, as well as the backing of voters who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. They argue concerns about Biden's age will fade when voters are faced with a direct choice, and have highlighted Trump's campaign gaffes, such as when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/in-first-state-for-gop-presidential-voting-the-race-is-on-for-second-place-e5b87464"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he recently confused}}}\uc2  Sioux City, Iowa, with Sioux Falls, S.D.\par \par \uc2 Both sides acknowledge that voters' mood on the economy will play a major role. While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/us-gdp-economy-third-quarter-f247fa45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 economic growth surged}}}\uc2  over the summer and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/jobs/jobs-report-september-economy-unemployment-d9409b8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hiring shot up in September}}}\uc2 , surveys show the public remains{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/the-economy-is-great-why-are-americans-in-such-a-rotten-mood-6e1044d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pessimistic about the current economic direction}}}\uc2 , which is likely due to ongoing pains of inflation or other factors.\par \par \uc2 "We recognize that people right now are anxious about the economy despite the good [economic] numbers from a macro perspective," said Rep. \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  (D., Calif.). "To me, it has to be a choice election, not a ratification election."\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats are concerned that the White House effort to promote "Bidenomics" as a shorthand for his economic accomplishments has been unpersuasive, but Biden has stuck with it.\par \par \uc2 A third-party opening?\par \par \uc2 The possibilities of independent or third-party challenges, which were minimal in 2020, could make the outcomes in battleground states difficult to predict and provide an outlet for disaffected voters. \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/robert-f-kennedy-jr-shifts-to-independent-presidential-bid-e3570e7f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nephew of}}}\uc2  former President \uc2 John F. Kennedy\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/cornel-west-slams-biden-trump-and-runs-as-2024-independent-d44a2af5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 academic}}}\uc2  Cornel West, are both running as independents, though they will have to expend considerable time and money to make ballots across the country. No Labels, a centrist group, also may launch a unity presidential ticket. And the Green and Libertarian parties, which captured hundreds of thousands of votes in 2016 battleground states, are expected to field nominees.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump accounted for more than 98% of the popular vote in 2020, depriving third-party challenges of much support. But in 2016, when Trump defeated \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the two major-party candidates accounted for just less than 95%.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/images/polling/us/us11012023_regvoter_uomg47.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hypothetical four-way matchup}}}\uc2 , the Quinnipiac poll showed Biden received support from 36% of registered voters, Trump got 35%, Kennedy had 19% and West 6%. Support for third-party candidates often declines as elections draw closer and major party nominees are set.\par \par \uc2 "I think the move by Cornel West and Kennedy to run as independents is going to throw some wild cards in there," said Republican pollster Greg Strimple.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ken Thomas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ken.thomas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ken.thomas@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and John McCormick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mccormick.john@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mccormick.john@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231105ejb5000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
