\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Why a 2023 Virginia Election Is a Proving Ground for 2024; In state legislative races next week, both parties are testing their messaging ahead of presidential race\b0\par\par\uc2 By Scott Calvert \par \uc2 1,350 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2023\par 09:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 THE PLAINS, Va.\u8212\'20\'14For clues about the strength of both parties' messages heading into 2024, look no further than this suburban Northern Virginia enclave, where Democrats and Republicans are betting big on a hotly contested state Senate race.\par \par \uc2 Typically, such local elections don't have a major impact outside their direct communities. But this one could decide control of the Virginia legislature and Republican Gov. Glenn Youngkin's ability to enact conservative policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , taxes and education\u8212\'20\'14making it closely watched in the run up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next year's presidential race}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/election-day-2023-gubernatorial-races-247b7d34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nov. 7 contest}}}\uc2  pits Republican Juan Pablo Segura, a 35-year-old entrepreneur, against Democrat Russet Perry, 39, a former \uc2 Central Intelligence Agency\uc2  officer and prosecutor. The seat is key to Democrats' bid to keep their slim edge in the 40-seat Senate, where they have squared off against Youngkin and Republicans who narrowly lead the House.\par \par \uc2 Virginia's odd-year elections traditionally offer signals about the electorate's mood heading into national contests. Both parties have had recent statewide success in the state: Youngkin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/virginia-governor-election-youngkin-results-11635884218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the governor's mansion in 2021}}}\uc2 , and President Biden won its 13 Electoral College votes a year earlier. In a campaign that mirrors the political playbook across Virginia this year, Perry is pledging to prevent a rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while Segura emphasizes education, crime and cost-of-living concerns.\par \par \uc2 "Whoever wins this seat probably is in the majority," said J. Miles Coleman, associate editor of Sabato's Crystal Ball at the University of Virginia Center for Politics. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
