\par \par \uc2 Juan Pablo Segura, with beard, and GOP Virginia Gov. Glenn Youngkin both attended the Heritage India Festival last weekend in Chantilly, Va. PHOTO: Valerie Plesch for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The battle for the newly drawn seat covering parts of affluent Loudoun and Fauquier counties is shaping up as the state's most expensive Senate race this year, with more than $11 million raised through Oct. 26. If Republicans flip the Senate and hold the House, the GOP will have a trifecta with Youngkin in the governor's office.\par \par \uc2 "This race is critical. I think the path to our majority goes through Juan Pablo Segura," Youngkin said Saturday, after rallying with him and other Republicans before a boisterous crowd at a farm in The Plains. At the event, Republican voter Dave Sullivan, 66, said he came away impressed with Segura, adding, "I think he'll get my vote."\par \par \uc2 Backed by a GOP-led legislature, Youngkin could pass his proposed 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit with exceptions for rape, incest and to protect the mother's life\u8212\'20\'14an idea Segura supports. Existing state law allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until about 26 weeks and thereafter if the mother's life or health is at serious risk. Perry said her priority would be to protect that law and enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state Constitution.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin and GOP candidates are gambling by running on his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposal, given that Republicans nationally haven't had much success on the issue since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022}}}\uc2 , said Dave Wasserman, senior editor at the nonpartisan Cook Political Report. This year's most competitive races in Virginia are in suburbs where the GOP has lost support over time, he said.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin's PAC in October ran an ad that described Republicans' 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposal as reasonable.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, where Democrats have a 22-18 majority, four races including the Segura-Perry contest are rated competitive by the nonpartisan Virginia Public Access Project. The group ranks seven House races as competitive. Republicans have a 48-46 majority in that chamber, with six seats currently vacant.\par \par \uc2 "I would estimate Democrats are narrow favorites in both chambers of Virginia, but there are still enough competitive races for Republicans to have a chance," said Wasserman, who described Perry as the "slight favorite." Youngkin, who some GOP donors hope will make a late, long shot entry into the 2024 presidential contest, barely carried the district in his 2021 gubernatorial run, whereas Biden did so handily in 2020, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The high stakes for Virginia were on the minds of many voters who cast early ballots Saturday in Leesburg, the Loudoun County seat. Analysts say not many independent voters are up for grabs in Virginia\u8212\'20\'14mirroring the national political environment\u8212\'20\'14and the state's races will come down to turnout among core voters from both parties.\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic voters backing Perry said preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was a priority. Michele Carpenter, a 69-year-old retired corporate executive, said she opposed unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but feared Republicans would impose drastic restrictions. Helik Shemer, 66, said he didn't think Republicans would stop at 15 weeks. "They really want to banish it completely," the retired software engineer said.\par \par \uc2 Democrat Brian Parris, a 34-year-old optician, said he hoped his vote for Perry would help avert a Republican trifecta in the state capital, Richmond. "That scares me very badly," he said. "That is exactly what I'm trying to prevent."\par \par \uc2 Some Republican voters endorsed the 15-week proposal as reasonable and feasible. "I would prefer to see no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it's moving in the right direction," said John Harris, a 62-year-old Air Force program analyst who called Segura a good fit for his conservative values. His wife Karen, also 62, said a 15-week limit would be "pretty generous."\par \par \uc2 Republican Samantha Ellis, 29, said a vote for Segura is a vote for enabling Youngkin to more easily pass his agenda, including the 15-week law. A policy analyst, Ellis said she doesn't trust Democrats because of the negative impact of shutdown policies early in the Covid-19 pandemic, when the party had its own trifecta.\par \par \uc2 "I really like Governor Youngkin and [Segura] is someone who would work with Governor Youngkin, and that's big," she said.\par \par \uc2 Dave Rexrode\uc2 , chairman of Youngkin's Spirit of Virginia PAC, said Democrats were too focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The only issue that the Democrats are running on, that they're talking about, that they're spending money on is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Rexrode said, adding that Republicans like Segura are keying in on a host of issues that matter to voters.\par \par \uc2 Don Scott, Democratic leader in the Virginia House, said while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are on the line in the election, Democrats are also campaigning on gun-violence prevention and job creation. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich427\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6405
