\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Juan Pablo Segura listened at a rally in The Plains, Va. PHOTO: Valerie Plesch for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 If elected, Perry said, she would work to fully fund public schools and lower the cost of prescription drugs and child care. But her priority is protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. "I knock thousands of doors across my district, and voters want a senator who will protect their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said in a written response to The Wall Street Journal's request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Segura frames the 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit as a "compassionate consensus," and Democrats as extreme. He called education the No. 1 issue, as Youngkin did during his successful 2021 run against Democrat \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2 . Segura, who co-founded a doughnut business and helped start a maternity-care company, said he wants to bolster parental rights and raise education standards.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are you watching for from Virginia's swing voters? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Segura has criticized Perry's tenure as a Loudoun County prosecutor under Commonwealth's Attorney Buta Biberaj, who has drawn flack from Republicans for what they see as her overly lenient approach to defendants. Segura also noted that Perry is endorsed by some groups that have expressed support for defunding police.\par \par \uc2 Perry, asked about Segura's criticism, said: "I am the only person in this race who has gotten violent criminals like murderers, rapists, and domestic abusers off our streets and put them in jail."\par \par \uc2 Write to Scott Calvert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.calvert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.calvert@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231101ejb1001gt\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgo