\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 House Speaker Built Career Fighting in Conservative Legal Trenches; Mike Johnson came to Congress with a long legal record battling gay rights,  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and limits on religious expression in the public sphere\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Mariah Timms and Scott Patterson \par \uc2 1,065 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2023\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson was in a Louisiana courtroom in June 2015 defending tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions adopted by the state when phones flashed with alerts that the Supreme Court had just recognized a constitutional right to same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Johnson dashed out of the ongoing proceedings to publicly criticize the decision, said opposing counsel Ilene Jaroslaw, who was representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the case. It was a moment, she said, that underscored the depth of Johnson's zeal for conservative legal causes.\par \par \uc2 "Damn, you're in federal court. You don't just get up and leave," she said.\par \par \uc2 While Johnson, a 51-year-old lawyer selected by Republicans last week as the new House speaker, is relatively new to Congress, he spent more than 15 years in the conservative legal trenches, battling over some of the nation's most-contentious social issues\u8212\'20\'14with mixed success. Representing conservative and religious clients, he argued against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and gay rights and advocated for a less-rigid separation of church and state, including in a case that sought tax credits for a biblical theme park. He would later play a key role in former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's long-shot legal efforts to overturn the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 Former legal colleagues and opponents alike said they weren't surprised to see the mild-mannered Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/new-speaker-mike-johnson-made-his-name-as-cultural-conservative-f1e51e78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rise to the top of the heap }}}\uc2  in a prolonged and bruising GOP battle to become House leader. As an attorney, he was courteous and personable. But those who faced off against Johnson said his affability belied his aggressiveness in seeking to advance the objectives of Christian conservatives.\par \par \uc2 His beliefs, they said, ran so deep that he often seemed willing to take on cases, including advocating for school prayer and religious portraits in courtrooms, where legal precedent was against him.\par \par \uc2 "He was arguing positions that, as far as I'm concerned, could not possibly have won," said Marjorie Esman, former executive director of the American Civil Liberties Union of Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 Johnson, a \uc2 Louisiana State University\uc2  law graduate, spent about eight years at the Alliance Defense Fund, which later became the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a formidable conservative legal nonprofit that won recent Supreme Court victories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 and granting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-web-designer-can-refuse-work-on-same-sex-wedding-announcements-f1e55d02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 First Amendment protections to a Colorado web designer }}}\uc2  who refused commissions for same-sex wedding announcements.\par \par \uc2 Johnson worked at the organization during its pioneer years, defending anti-sodomy laws and bans on same-sex marriage. As an \uc2 ADF\uc2  spokesman, he penned a 2004 guest column in The Times, the local paper in his hometown of Shreveport. In it, he supported a proposed Bush administration constitutional amendment banning same-sex marriage, saying such unions would cause "chaos and sexual anarchy" and "place our entire democratic system in jeopardy."\par \par \uc2 His office didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Nate Kellum, chief counsel at the Center for Religious Expression who worked with Johnson on a number of cases, said his former colleague's affable manner could make him easy for opponents to underestimate. "He's a smart guy without coming across as smart," Kellum said, recalling Johnson's ability to take complex legal issues and break them down "in this folksy way."\par \par \uc2 Johnson won the theme park case, which centered on the availability of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ark-builder-in-kentucky-is-buoyed-by-court-ruling-1454276163"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tax credits for a Noah's ark-themed tourist attraction }}}\uc2  in Kentucky, after the state withdrew tax incentives over concerns the project had become overtly religious. Johnson, then at his own law firm named Freedom Guard, represented the project sponsor, creationist group Answers in Genesis. He argued the exclusion of AiG from the state's tourism-development program on the basis of its religious beliefs was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge agreed, rejecting the state's argument that allowing the tax credits amounted to state sponsorship of religion. "Regardless of its religious theme, the Ark project is still a business, and as such involves a customer service aspect that will limit the possibility of forced indoctrination," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.kyed.77195/gov.uscourts.kyed.77195.60.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the judge wrote }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the Louisiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, Johnson, representing the state, defended a law that required doctors at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to have admitting privileges at a nearby hospital, which providers said was designed to close clinics and undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The case eventually landed at the Supreme Court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-strikes-down-louisiana-abortion-law-11593440418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which ruled against the state in 2020 }}}\uc2 . Two years later, a more-conservative high court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 In Congress, Johnson has continued to put his legal background to work, representing Trump as a House attorney in the first impeachment trial about the former president's attempt to pressure Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  to investigate rival \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the days following the Nov. 3, 2020, election, Johnson, like many other Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1325176210666770434"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly supported Trump's efforts }}}\uc2  to contest the election. As dozens of legal challenges against election results by Trump and his legal team failed, their hopes turned to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-bets-on-longshot-texas-election-lawsuit-11607622925"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit filed by the Republican Texas attorney general }}}\uc2  that sought to challenge electoral college votes from Georgia, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, all of which Biden had won. Election-law specialists said the suit had little chance of success.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think Johnson will perform as speaker of the House? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  accused the states of "rampant lawlessness" and alleged they violated their own election laws when officials adjusted voting procedures amid the Covid-19 pandemic. Johnson sent an email to House Republicans calling for signatures for an amicus brief supporting the Texas lawsuit. Trump is "anxiously" waiting for the final list of lawmakers who supported the suit, he told them.\par \par \uc2 "Mike really led the effort on the amicus brief," said Denver Riggleman, a House Republican at the time. "I thought it was ludicrous." After losing his bid for re-election in 2020, Riggleman worked as an adviser for the House select committee investigating the Jan. 6, 2021, attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-campaign-loses-wisconsin-election-lawsuit-11607713668"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected Texas' long-shot bid }}}\uc2 , saying the state lacked legal standing to bring the case.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Mariah Timms at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mariah.timms@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mariah.timms@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Scott Patterson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.patterson@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.patterson@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231029ejat000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
