\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 New Speaker Mike Johnson Made His Name as Cultural Conservative; Louisiana Republican played key role in legal effort to overturn 2020 election\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins, Siobhan Hughes and Katy Stech Ferek \par \uc2 1,866 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2023\par 18:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14In choosing Mike Johnson as the new House speaker, Republicans have cast their lot with a little-known congressman from Louisiana who has made his name {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/house-set-to-vote-on-gop-speaker-nominee-mike-johnson-f1f92e33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing conservative positions }}}\uc2  on cultural issues and who played a key role in unsuccessful legal efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 After 22 days without a speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/house-speaker-vote-mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Republicans came together to elect }}}\uc2  Johnson for the post Wednesday after three other better-known nominees failed to unite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/house-speaker-gop-factions-explained-d4fcdbaf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the fractured conference }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Johnson, 51 years old, represents Louisiana's deep-red fourth district, in the state's northwest that includes Shreveport, where he grew up. Johnson is the son of a firefighter who was critically burned and disabled in the line of duty. He is the father of four children of his own.\par \par \uc2 Johnson was elected to Congress in 2016 after serving in the Louisiana state legislature. He has been an attorney with a focus on social conservative issues, including defending the state's same-sex marriage ban before the Louisiana Supreme Court. His opposition to same-sex marriage and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with support for religious freedoms has continued to guide him as a legislator.\par \par \uc2 As vice chairman of the House Republican Conference, Johnson was one of seven elected leaders for the party. However, he was seen as far enough removed from the top positions that members looking for new leadership\u8212\'20\'14even more moderate lawmakers who might differ with him on some issues\u8212\'20\'14were supportive of him taking over.\par \par \uc2 "Mike Johnson is a person who I think everybody respects, he's a very principled human being," said Rep. \uc2 Mario Diaz Balart\uc2  (R., Fla.).\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (R., Fla.) has been seatmates with Johnson since the two were both elected in 2016 and has served with him on the oversight and armed services committees. "He is not swampy," said Gaetz, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/house-democrats-could-decide-kevin-mccarthys-fate-74de00ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched the vote that first ousted }}}\uc2  former House Speaker Kevin McCarthy (R., Calif.). "He is not beholden to the lobbyists and special interests. Even when we disagree, it comes from a place of sincerity, not whoever's donated to his campaign."\par \par \uc2 Democrats called Johnson an extremist. They said his opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and efforts to overturn the 2020 election results had been losing issues for Republicans in the 2022 election. When at least one Republican who will have a tough election next year voted for Johnson, a Democratic voice could be heard shouting "Bye! Bye!"\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Pete Aguilar\uc2  (D., Calif.), the chair of the House Democratic Caucus, said on the House floor Wednesday that Republicans were choosing a person who "can pass their extreme litmus test to oppose marriage equality, enact a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban without exceptions, gut Social Security and Medicare, support overturning a free and fair election."\par \par \uc2 Aguilar said Johnson had been called "the most important architect of the electoral college objections," and a Republican member shouted "damn right."\par \par \uc2 On paper, Johnson will mark a break from the prior House Republican leadership team. McCarthy, along with House Majority Leader Steve Scalise (R., La.) and House Majority Whip \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  (R., Minn.) all voted for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/federal-government-shutdown-deadline-d714a1ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the stopgap measure }}}\uc2  that is keeping the government funded through Nov. 17. All three also voted for $40 billion in aid to Ukraine in 2022, and again this year for about $300 million toward the Ukraine Security Assistance Initiative. Johnson voted against those measures.\par \par \uc2 Now that Johnson is speaker, the question is how firmly rooted Johnson's beliefs are about those funds, or whether he is part of a perennial "vote no, hope yes" caucus.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to his colleagues, Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/new-speaker-mike-johnsons-to-do-list-a-looming-funding-deadline-and-israel-ukraine-aid-8f4a3200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed advancing a temporary spending measure }}}\uc2  until either Jan. 15 or April 15\u8212\'20\'14depending on what the conference would support, while working to advance the eight individual appropriations bills that haven't yet cleared the House. Without a stopgap measure, the government is set to run out of money next month.\par \par \uc2 For next year, he proposed passing a fiscal 2025 budget resolution by April and keeping the House in session during August if the House hadn't passed all of its fiscal 2025 appropriations bills by that time.\par \par \uc2 When he served as head of the Republican Study Committee, which represents a spectrum of House conservatives, Johnson presided over a budget blueprint designed to balance the federal budget in 10 years. Among other things, it pushed an idea long associated with former House Speaker \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2  (R., Wis.) to turn Medicare into a "premium support" system in which beneficiaries would receive financial assistance to buy health insurance through a regulated Medicare exchange. The plan also proposed raising the retirement age to 69. For people born in 1960 and later, the current retirement age is 67.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has been a strong supporter of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who on Wednesday morning urged Republicans to support Johnson.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has played a key role pushing Trump's false claims of election fraud. In 2020, Johnson organized an amicus brief signed by 126 House Republicans supporting a lawsuit filed by Texas' attorney general arguing that Texas could challenge the election results in four swing states won by President Biden. The conservative Supreme Court rejected the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 At the time, Johnson heavily lobbied fellow Republicans to sign onto the letter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-bets-on-longshot-texas-election-lawsuit-11607622925"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggesting that Trump would be watching to see who signed }}}\uc2 , which some members took as a threat. At the time, Democrats were so upset that one member, Rep. \uc2 Bill Pascrell\uc2  (D., N.J.) argued that then-House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) should bar the GOP signatories from taking their seats, saying that they were attempting to "obliterate public confidence in our democratic system" by installing an "unelected dictator."\par \par \uc2 Johnson also joined with 146 other Republicans in voting against certification of the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 The push to overturn Biden's victory has led to legal peril for the former president. Johnson's selection as the party nominee took place the same day that one of Trump's lawyers, \uc2 Jenna Ellis\uc2 , became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/trump-lawyer-jenna-ellis-pleads-guilty-in-georgia-racketeering-case-2134c82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third legal adviser to plead guilty }}}\uc2  in the Georgia racketeering case involving Trump's 2020 efforts.\par \par \uc2 When a reporter asked Johnson at a press conference Tuesday night about his effort to overturn the election, she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IcVYDU_oYT0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shouted down }}}\uc2  by some of Johnson's colleagues, with Rep. \uc2 Virginia Foxx\uc2  (R., N.C.) telling the reporter: "Shut up! Shut up!"\par \par \uc2 In the lead-up to Johnson's election, Republicans had rallied around three other speaker nominees who all ultimately dropped out of the running after it became clear there wasn't enough support to be elected on the House floor.\par \par \uc2 For Rep. Jim Jordan (R., Ohio), a conservative with many similar stances to Johnson's, some moderate Republicans said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/pressure-campaign-by-jim-jordan-supporters-backfires-in-house-speaker-race-92779873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they couldn't back him }}}\uc2  because of past positions he had taken which they viewed as out of the mainstream. However, they were united in backing Johnson, who is seen as more personable and less combative than Jordan.\par \par \uc2 Though Gaetz considers Jordan a mentor, to him, a Speaker Johnson is an even better outcome: "I get the best of Jordan's brilliance and dogged commitment to oversight with a government funding strategy more closely tailored to my vision," Gaetz said.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  (R., Colo.) who said he wouldn't be able to support Jordan because of the 2020 election issue, backed Johnson for the post. Buck justified his support for Johnson: "I think it is a mistake, but I think people make mistakes and still can be really good speakers," he said about Johnson and 2020.\par \par \uc2 Johnson isn't known for bipartisanship. He was ranked 429th out of 435 lawmakers in the 2021 bipartisan index kept by the Lugar Center and the McCourt School of Public Policy at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2 , situated among members of the staunchly conservative House Freedom Caucus. The measure scores how well members of opposite parties work together using bill sponsorship data.\par \par \uc2 The lobbying arm of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , a conservative Washington think tank, gives Johnson a lifetime score of 90% for his voting record.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has proposed legislation on issues central to Republicans' policy agenda, including a bill that would make it a federal crime to transport a minor across state lines for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He is strongly opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Another proposal would cut off federal funding to any school district, museum or other organization that exposes a child younger than 10 to the topic of gender identity or sexual orientation, enabling parents to sue over violations.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has called for restrictions on medical interventions, such as surgery, for transgender youth. Conservatives say children are too young to access care with lasting consequences based on a self-diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 Democrats say medical interventions provide necessary relief to youth struggling to manage deep distress. Clinicians who defend providing gender-affirming care to minors say there is more harm in denying the care to youth and that the matter has been subject to extensive study and research.\par \par \uc2 Johnson opposed a congressional push to ratify an amendment mandating equal rights for both men and women, saying he opposed it because he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/equal-rights-amendment-could-soon-be-back-in-congress-11562155202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerned it could restrict \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  regulations }}}\uc2 . Some critics of the Equal Rights Amendment have said they worry restricting federal funds for abortions could be struck down under the ERA because only women can get pregnant. Its proponents disputed that its passage would automatically undermine all such limits.\par \par \uc2 Johnson will have a long way to go on the fundraising front to match McCarthy, who by the time he was ousted had already pulled in tens of millions of dollars for the 2024 election on behalf of House Republicans, including for the National Republican Congressional Committee.\par \par \uc2 For his own accounts, McCarthy brought in more than $14 million between January and September, \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  data show, leaving the former speaker's campaign with about $10.6 million cash on hand.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Johnson has brought in roughly $550,000 this cycle for his re-election effort, federal campaign finance data show. Contributors to one of his fundraising arms mostly included executives at logistics firms in his congressional district, as well as retirees. Johnson raised a little more than $1.2 million on average each election cycle since running for Congress in 2016, and his campaign has about $1.1 million in the bank as of late September.\par \par \uc2 Johnson also has few financial assets, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://disclosures-clerk.house.gov/public_disc/financial-pdfs/2022/10055641.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent disclosures show }}}\uc2 . He earned about $29,800 in income from online courses he taught at \uc2 Liberty University\uc2 , the evangelical Christian institution founded by the late \uc2 Jerry Falwell Sr\uc2 . He also has few debts, including only a home mortgage valued between $250,000 and $500,000, a small personal loan and a home equity line of credit. His salary as speaker will increase to $223,500, up from the $174,000 he has earned as a rank-and-file member.\par \par \uc2 Jack Gillum, Kristina Peterson, and Molly Ball contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Katy Stech Ferek at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:katy.stech@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 katy.stech@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231025ejap0053e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
