\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Georgia's Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Upheld; State supreme court says law is valid even though the Georgia legislature enacted it when Roe v. Wade protected  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 570 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2023\par 23:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Georgia's highest court on Tuesday upheld a law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy, a decision that will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access significantly constrained throughout most of the South.\par \par \uc2 A 6-to-1 majority of the Georgia Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gasupreme.us/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/s23a0421.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a claim by \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers  }}}\uc2  that the law, enacted in 2019, was clearly unlawful when it was passed because Roe v. Wade, which protected the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was the law of the land at the time.\par \par \uc2 In June of last year, the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overruled Roe and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated that right  }}}\uc2  in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. Georgia's law took effect a short time later.\par \par \uc2 The state court said Tuesday that it must follow current legal precedent, meaning the six-week ban was constitutional under Dobbs. The decision reversed a state trial judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgias-abortion-ban-after-six-weeks-is-blocked-11668540794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who found that state law invalid  }}}\uc2  on the grounds that it was unconstitutional four years ago.\par \par \uc2 Justice Verda Colvin, writing for the court, noted that the Dobbs decision found Roe "egregiously wrong from the start." The court had already issued an interim order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgias-six-week-abortion-ban-reinstated-by-state-supreme-court-11669224954"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that allowed the ban to be enforced  }}}\uc2  during the litigation.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia ruling was the latest in a flurry of legal battles that have shifted to state courts in the year since Roe was overturned. Without federal constitutional protections for the procedure, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have mounted new legal arguments based on state constitutions, especially in states where the legislature and governor's office are controlled by Republicans. The results so far have been mixed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters won an initial victory in South Carolina earlier this year, but the court quickly reversed itself and allowed a six-week ban to go into effect. They also have scored some narrow victories in states such as Oklahoma, where the state supreme court found a right for women to obtain abortions in medical emergencies. A number of cases, including in Florida, remain unsettled.\par \par \uc2 Georgia has seen a roughly 40% decline in abortions under the six-week ban, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's ruling didn't resolve all the issues in the litigation. The state high court sent the case back to the trial level for consideration of other legal arguments, including whether the six-week ban violates a privacy provision in the state's constitution by constraining women's ability to make medical decisions.\par \par \uc2 Republican Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  , who won re-election last November, has said little publicly about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since signing the law four years ago. His office didn't respond to a request for comment. The state's Republican attorney general, \uc2 Chris Carr\uc2  , said he was "pleased with the court's decision" and that his office would continue to defend the law.\par \par \uc2 The six-week ban is likely to remain a contentious topic in the politically mixed state, where Democrats have sought to paint Republicans as extreme on the issue. President Biden's re-election campaign in a statement Tuesday said, "This election could determine whether every woman in America faces the same terrifying reality Georgians will now face."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020231024ejao003ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
