\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Roe v. Wade Is Gone, but Abortions Are on the Rise; New  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans have done little to reduce frequency of the procedure, new data show\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,266 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2023\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood of Orange & San Bernardino Counties saw a 20% increase in total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patient volume since June 2022 and a fifth of that increase came from out-of-state patients. An earlier version of this article misrepresented the uptick in patient volume. (Corrected on Oct. 26)\par \par \uc2 More than a year after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , one thing seems clear: New state bans have done little so far to deter women from obtaining abortions.\par \par \uc2 Data released Tuesday shows the number of abortions ticked up slightly in the year following the high court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-dobbs-year-after-roe-support-politics-d1ef5a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization decision }}}\uc2 . That ruling, from June 2022, ended federal protections for the procedure, and paved the way for some 16 states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to ban many or most abortions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The data indicate that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, funders and others have adapted quickly to a legal landscape that has changed profoundly. Access has been cut off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-restrictions-pass-across-u-s-as-republicans-overcome-divisions-331d7d31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 throughout much of the South }}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/women-face-abortion-delays-as-clinics-report-surge-in-demand-f95eea65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demand has surged }}}\uc2  in states in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal. Many providers there have had to significantly increase capacity.\par \par \uc2 The findings also underscore the challenges facing antiabortion groups, as the ease of traveling to another state or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/biden-administration-asks-supreme-court-to-maintain-abortion-pill-access-69882ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtaining \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2  online seem to be largely undercutting laws intended to reduce abortions.\par \par \uc2 In the new study, WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, found that nationwide there were 183 more monthly abortions on average in the 12-month period following the Dobbs decision compared with the monthly average prior to the decision. That trend mirrors similar findings by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that also supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which showed the number of abortions rising in most states in the first half of this year compared with 2020, the most recent year for which data are available.\par \par \uc2 "I have been surprised to see the evidence that is mounting that abortions have had a slight increase," said Caitlin Myers, an economics professor at \uc2 Middlebury College\uc2  who has studied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 While it has become much harder since the end of Roe to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states with newly enacted bans, it actually appears to have become easier in many other states, thanks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-legalized-abortion-grows-since-dobbs-ruling-wsj-poll-shows-11662210020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased attention }}}\uc2  and resources. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, nonprofits that help finance abortions and logistics associated with them, have raised millions to help lower-income women pay for procedures and travel, while new clinics have opened in states such as Illinois and New Mexico that have become major destinations for women traveling from other states.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 115,000 fewer abortions were performed in the year after the Dobbs decision in states that banned abortions throughout pregnancy or after six weeks, according to the WeCount data. At the same time, states including Illinois, Florida and North Carolina\u8212\'20\'14where the procedure remained largely legal\u8212\'20\'14saw an increase of 117,000 abortions.\par \par \uc2 The data don't include women who order pills online from overseas outside of the formal medical system, a practice that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/more-women-requesting-abortion-pills-outside-formal-channels-study-finds-11667316848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to have become more common }}}\uc2 . \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
FF
