\par \par \uc2 Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills is being tested in court. PHOTO: Angela Owens/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 In the first month since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolina-passes-12-week-abortion-ban-39b06537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina passed a 12-week limit }}}\uc2 , the number of abortions in the state declined by nearly one-third from the prior month, according to Guttmacher. The law increased requirements for in-person medical visits, which providers say has virtually eliminated visits from out-of-state patients.\par \par \uc2 A challenge to approval for a widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill appears headed to the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  and could potentially upend access across the country in the next year if it succeeds.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups also acknowledge that they face internal risks, including staff burnout at clinics that remain open and a decrease in fundraising firepower if public attention fades.\par \par \uc2 The Chicago \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund has quadrupled its staff and tripled its budget since 2021. The fund has provided about $4.5 million to thousands of patients to assist with plane, train and bus tickets; hotel stays; child care; and other costs since Roe was struck down.\par \par \uc2 "This is not a long-term solution," said Megan Jefyio, executive director of the Chicago \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund. "We are dealing with competing crises in this country and I don't know how long we're going to have this sustained support."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \p