\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Senate Republicans Seek Winning Path on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions; Issue has divided GOP since Supreme Court decision last year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise \par \uc2 969 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2023\par 23:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Senate Republicans stung by disappointing losses in the 2022 midterm elections are working to craft a more effective message on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their party confronts the fallout from last year's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court decision }}}\uc2  to end the constitutional right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 How the GOP handles the issue could be critical to the party's efforts to retake the Senate and the White House in 2024, when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is once again expected to play a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/biden-administration-asks-supreme-court-to-maintain-abortion-pill-access-69882ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central role }}}\uc2  in elections nationwide.\par \par \uc2 At a closed-door lunch this past week, Senate Republicans received a briefing on shifting public attitudes toward \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , based on research by One Nation, a political nonprofit aligned with Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.). The takeaways: Research shows voter support for some restrictions after 12 to 15 weeks; few back absolute bans; and many want exceptions for rape, incest and life or health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Since the 2022 court ruling, more than a dozen GOP-controlled states have enacted a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many of those with few exceptions for rape or incest. Others have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The briefing advised senators it is no longer enough to identify as pro-life without giving voters a detailed description of what they are for and against and suggested that they "own the center" by casting Democrats as extreme in backing looser or no restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.onenationamerica.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Senate-Presentation-IV.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presentation made no policy recommendations }}}\uc2 , but underscored that public attitudes toward \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain a core concern for the party even as polls show advantages on other key issues such as the economy.\par \par \uc2 One Nation surveyed 2,529 voters nationwide and worked with six focus groups in Iowa, Ohio and Montana. Among the findings was strong opposition to the court's decision among female voters in the suburbs, where Republicans have lost ground to Democrats. Republicans failed to retake the Senate in the midterms, and only narrowly won back the House, as an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/frustrated-republicans-try-to-explain-lack-of-midterm-red-wave-11668036382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected "red wave" }}}\uc2  largely didn't materialize.\par \par \uc2 "The suburbs have been the killing field for Republican candidates the last few election cycles, and it is a strongly held view among suburban women that this \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling is a problematic issue," said One Nation President Steven Law, a former McConnell chief of staff.\par \par \uc2 In the group's poll, 71% of suburban women said they were somewhat or strongly opposed to the Supreme Court's decision.\par \par \uc2 Law said McConnell personally endorsed the group's project in May, saying his members needed guidance on the issue as soon as possible. McConnell's office declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party has been split since the ruling over which types of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are appropriate, and whether those rules should be made at the state or federal level.\par \par \uc2 Various state legislatures have moved to roll out new limits or protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In a warning sign for Republicans, voters in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red-leaning Kansas }}}\uc2  rejected before the midterms last year a proposed state constitutional amendment that would have ended protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . More recently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohio-election-abortion-issue-one-vote-d7df6402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio voters defeated a measure }}}\uc2  that would have made it harder to change the state constitution, in a win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already a hot topic in the 2024 election cycle. At the first Republican presidential primary debate last month, several presidential candidates called for a federal law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks, including former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 . But former United Nations Ambassador Nikki Haley said fellow Republicans should acknowledge that such a move isn't politically realistic.\par \par \uc2 Haley called herself "unapologetically pro-life," but said Republicans need to stop pretending that a federal ban would pass Congress.\par \par \uc2 "Let's find consensus," she said. "Can't we all agree that we should ban late-term abortions?"\par \par \uc2 Former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2 , the front-runner in the 2024 GOP race, has avoided committing to a national ban, and has warned that extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions could hinder Republicans.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists scoffed at Republicans' latest messaging efforts.\par \par \uc2 "No matter how much they try to rebrand, it will not change the fact that banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unpopular and unsupported by the majority of the public," said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and chief executive of \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year, in the wake of the court's ruling, Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lindsey-grahams-abortion-bill-gets-cold-shoulder-from-some-republicans-11663098886"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced his proposal }}}\uc2  to ban doctors from performing abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. Some Republicans gave the bill a chilly reception, saying that it had no chance of passage and would simply serve to motivate Democratic voters.\par \par \uc2 One Nation found that it is no longer sufficient for Republicans to label themselves "pro-life" without explaining where they stand, since the term is now perceived by many voters to mean a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without exceptions. In contrast, many voters who support some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limitations consider themselves pro-choice, including some Republicans. NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/republicans-try-find-new-term-life-stave-electoral-losses-rcna103924"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported Thursday }}}\uc2  that GOP senators had discussed the shifting meanings of "pro-life" and "pro-choice" at their meeting.\par \par \uc2 Law said One Nation's data on GOP women in particular caught the attention of senators.\par \par \uc2 Among Republican women overall, 41% disagreed with the Supreme Court decision to overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Asked if they saw themselves as more pro-choice, pro-life or somewhere in between, 24% of Republican women said pro-choice, 32% said in between and 44% said pro-life.\par \par \uc2 "It was with Republican women where we found the largest movement on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Law said. "I think if one were to take this poll 10 years ago, there wouldn't be any gray area, and most Republican women would be pro-life."\par \par \uc2 Write to Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230908ej98007ep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
