\par\par \uc2 Latin America News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 Mexico's High Court Decriminalizes  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  at Federal Level; Ruling expands previous order banning criminal prosecutions over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Juan Montes \par \uc2 457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2023\par 00:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mexico's Supreme Court ruled Wednesday to decriminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the federal level on grounds that the current penal code violates the constitution, a decision that expanded a previous order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mexicos-supreme-court-decriminalizes-abortion-in-historic-shift-11631049288"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning criminal proceedings }}}\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Several Latin American countries have fully legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years. In late 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-once-unthinkable-in-argentina-becomes-legal-11609314445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Argentina became the region's first large country }}}\uc2  to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal, joining Uruguay, Cuba and Guyana. Last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/colombias-highest-court-decriminalizes-abortion-in-historic-shift-11645490007"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colombia's Constitutional Court decriminalized \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  up to the 24th week of pregnancy, further than some European countries. Momentum is also building in other Latin American countries toward expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "The legal system that penalizes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the federal criminal code is unconstitutional, since it violates the human rights of women," Mexico's high court said on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling orders Mexico's Congress to overhaul the code and requires federal government hospitals to provide abortions. About 70% of Mexicans rely on free healthcare provided by the government in a conservative country where around three-quarters of the population are Catholic.\par \par \uc2 "It's a huge change because the court requires the government to provide the service, the number of people able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is much greater," said Isabel Fulda, the deputy director of GIRE, the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nonprofit that challenged the country's criminal code at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 She said Wednesday's ruling doesn't directly affect legal provisions in the 21 Mexican states that still criminalize abortions. The organization has filed similar challenges against the states, and Fulda said she hopes the court rules against them in coming months.\par \par \uc2 "It's a cascading effect," she added.\par \par \uc2 Two years ago, the country's high court ruled that making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime was unconstitutional, striking down several provisions of law in northern Coahuila state, which shares a border with Texas. The provisions called for prison time for anyone who terminates a pregnancy or participates in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That meant that judges across Mexico had to dismiss prosecutions related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even if federal and state laws weren't modified.\par \par \uc2 Despite the high court's ruling two years ago, federal and state provisions against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were still in effect.\par \par \uc2 Six Mexican states have so far legalized abortions up to the first 12 weeks of pregnancy in public state hospitals and clinics, according to the National Alliance for the Right to Choose, an advocacy group. The rest allow abortions only when pregnancy is the result of rape, when the fetus has a severe malformation or if it endangers the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Write to Juan Montes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:juan.montes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 juan.montes@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230906ej960080x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
