\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 The Most Important Elections of 2023 Will Test Purple-State Voters\u8212\'20\'14and Glenn Youngkin's Clout; Virginia races this November to give clues about national contests next year and the GOP governor's future\b0\par\par\uc2 By Scott Calvert \par \uc2 1,406 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2023\par 09:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Virginia voters' choices this November will give crucial clues about the direction of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/whos-running-for-president-in-2024-adb754e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national elections next November }}}\uc2 , and about the political future of a rising Republican star: Gov. Glenn Youngkin.\par \par \uc2 Control of the state legislature is at stake, with all 140 seats in both chambers up for grabs. Democrats hold a slim majority in the Senate, Republicans have an edge in the House.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin, while not on the ballot, is pushing hard for a GOP trifecta so he can pass a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit and other conservative priorities\u8212\'20\'14and so he can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-glenn-youngkin-kept-trump-at-arms-length-but-on-his-side-11636057542"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 burnish his reputation }}}\uc2  as a Republican who can win in swing territory after\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/virginia-governor-election-youngkin-results-11635884218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his 2021 victory }}}\uc2  put him on the national map.\par \par \uc2 If the Nov. 7 elections go well for his party, Youngkin could make a late entry into the 2024 presidential race\u8212\'20\'14a prospect he hasn't ruled out and some national Republicans have pined for privately. GOP primary polling and some early ballot deadlines suggest such a bid would have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-is-top-choice-for-nearly-60-of-gop-voters-wsj-poll-shows-877252b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 little chance of success }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Or Youngkin, 56 years old, could try to continue building legislative and political victories with an eye to running for president in 2028. Virginia governors can't serve consecutive four-year terms.\par \par \uc2 Dominance in the state's General Assembly likely will hinge on a handful of races. The nonpartisan Virginia Public Access Project rates four of 40 Senate races and seven of 100 House contests as competitive.\par \par \uc2 "Truly, this is anybody's game. I think it's going to be really tight," said Rebecca Bromley-Trujillo, an associate professor of political science at \uc2 Christopher Newport University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With no marquee office on the ballot, the key for Republicans and Democrats will be motivating their bases, political analysts say, although both sides are vying for the sliver of potentially persuadable voters in the middle.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are betting on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  to energize voters, along with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/gun-show-sellers-must-do-background-checks-on-buyers-biden-administration-proposes-389a5fe0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gun-control measures }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-web-designer-can-refuse-work-on-same-sex-wedding-announcements-f1e55d02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBT protections }}}\uc2 . Republicans are focusing largely on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/college-board-says-florida-has-effectively-banned-its-ap-psychology-course-over-gender-identity-content-48db14a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 parental involvement in education }}}\uc2  as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/car-thefts-soared-as-violent-crime-dropped-in-first-six-months-of-year-81c10361"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crime }}}\uc2 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/jobs/jobs-report-august-today-unemployment-economy-de847415"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the economy }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Because it's a turnout election, you can glean whose base is more mobilized to come out and vote," said Democratic strategist Ben Tribbett. Democrats need a strong showing from the party's younger voters, he said, adding, "If this is an election decided by senior citizens, Glenn Youngkin will take total control."\par \par \uc2 Virginia's odd-year elections traditionally offer clues about the electorate's mood heading into national contests. The state used to lean Republican, but suburban growth, especially around Washington, has benefited the Democratic Party, which in 2019 won majorities in both houses for the first time since the 1990s. Republicans in 2021 captured the governorship and took back the House; Virginia is now one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsl.org/about-state-legislatures/state-partisan-composition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just two states }}}\uc2  where each party controls one legislative chamber.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think either of the political parties will take control of both chambers of Virginia's legislature? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin, elected amid a wave of frustration over Covid-era school policies, has staked much on these elections. The former private-equity executive waded into 10 GOP primary fights, and all of his picks prevailed. Now his political operation is raising large sums as Youngkin rallies with candidates around the state. Taking a page from Democrats, he is encouraging Republicans to vote early and by mail.\par \par \uc2 "We're kind of engaged at every level of operations with these different campaigns," said \uc2 Dave Rexrode\uc2 , chairman of Youngkin's Spirit of Virginia PAC. The PAC said it raised $3.3 million in August alone, and $12 million so far this year. Rexrode predicted Democrats would still outspend Republicans by up to $30 million, with the entire legislative campaign possibly costing $150 million.\par \par \uc2 Some of that cash is coming from Washington: The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  said Saturday it was putting an additional $1.2 million into Virginia's elections, bringing its total investment in the state so far this cycle to $1.5 million.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee, charged with electing Democrats to statehouses, plans substantial financial and other support for Virginia candidates, a spokeswoman said. Its counterpart, the Republican State Leadership Committee, is coordinating efforts with Youngkin's PAC and other GOP arms, a spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 "When Youngkin won, he was seen as almost the Republicans' shiny new object who was able to capture lightning in a bottle. So it's like, OK, are the Republicans going to get lucky again like that?" said J. Miles Coleman, associate editor of Sabato's Crystal Ball of the University of Virginia Center for Politics.\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.roanoke.edu/documents/rcpoll/RC%20Poll%20Topline%20Aug2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roanoke College poll }}}\uc2  found 51% of Virginians approve of Youngkin's job performance as governor, versus 40% job approval for President Biden, who won the state by 10 points in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Yet the survey also pointed to why a late bid for the 2024 GOP nomination would be tough for Youngkin: Just 9% of Republican respondents in the state that knows him best listed him as their top pick in a hypothetical primary contest, behind former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at 47% and Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  at 13%.\par \par \uc2 Jumping in after Virginia's election would mean missing deadlines to get on the ballot in several key states, including Nevada and South Carolina, which come early in the nominating process.\par \par \uc2 Asked about a White House bid in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://video.foxbusiness.com/v/6336126820112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Fox Business interview }}}\uc2  last week, Youngkin said he wasn't "paying attention to the filing deadlines, etc. I'm paying attention to making sure we hold our House and flip our Senate."\par \par \uc2 Alice Stewart, an aide to Texas Sen. Ted Cruz's 2016 presidential campaign, said a strong showing in Virginia would set Youngkin up for success in future runs, including a 2028 bid for president. His joining the 2024 race, she said, would just end up "fracturing the field even further; it doesn't help us get Trump out of the picture. As a matter of fact, it helps him."\par \par \uc2 Republican voter Gary Libby wants Youngkin to remain governor through 2025. He said tax cuts implemented under Youngkin are netting him $1,800 to $2,200 a year. He said he supports the governor's proposed 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit with exceptions for rape, incest and to protect the mother's life.\par \par \uc2 "He's delivered on every campaign promise he's been able to that the Democrats haven't blocked," said Libby, 62, who lives in a Richmond suburb and sells professional services and software.\par \par \uc2 But independent voter Robin Menefee, 69, who voted for Biden in 2020 and Youngkin in 2021, said she would cast ballots for Democrats this fall because she opposes curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Current Virginia law allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until about 26 weeks and thereafter only if the mother's life or health is at serious risk.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the government has the right to step in and tell a woman what she should do with her body," said Menefee, a retiree from the town of Rocky Mount.\par \par \uc2 A Christopher Newport poll last fall found that a majority of Virginians opposed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's 2022 decision overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  and two-thirds felt \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases. Yet the same poll found about half of voters supported banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks with the exceptions Youngkin endorses.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, meanwhile, have proposed a state constitutional amendment that would guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, "unless justified by a compelling state interest and achieved by the least restrictive means that do not infringe an individual's autonomous decision-making." The measure said a state interest would be compelling only "to ensure the protection of the health of an individual seeking care." Republicans have criticized that proposal as extreme and out of step with what Virginians want.\par \par \uc2 Don Scott, Democratic leader in the Virginia House, said he thinks fears of losing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access will drive many voters to the polls. He said while Youngkin backs a 15-week limit, the governor previously said he would sign any bill restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "Every day they're talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out there is a good day for us," Scott said.\par \par \uc2 Eliza Collins contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Scott Calvert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.calvert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.calvert@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230903ej930005m\par }\par \b \uc2 Search 